/* CSP full-length mock exams — generated by csp-tools/build-mocks.mjs.
   Set A and B are disjoint; each is 200 questions weighted by the CSP11 blueprint.
   Options are pre-balanced so correct answers are spread evenly. */
window.CSP_MOCKS = {
  a: { title: '全真模拟 A', questions: [{"domain":"4","text":"What is the correct extinguishing agent for a Class K fire involving commercial cooking oils?","options":["Carbon dioxide (CO2)","Wet chemical","Dry powder","Water"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Class K fires (cooking oils and fats) require wet chemical extinguishers. The agent works through saponification — reacting with hot fat to form a soap-like foam layer that smothers and cools. Water is extremely dangerous on cooking oil fires.\n\nK类火灾（烹饪油和油脂）需要湿化学灭火器。灭火剂通过皂化反应起作用——与热油脂反应形成肥皂状泡沫层来窒息和冷却。水对烹饪油火灾极其危险。","related":[{"n":"13.4","t":"火灾分类"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"What is the correct order of the Kirkpatrick evaluation levels from lowest to highest?","options":["Learning, Reaction, Behavior, Results","Reaction, Behavior, Learning, Results","Behavior, Learning, Reaction, Results","Reaction, Learning, Behavior, Results"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The correct order is: Level 1 (Reaction — did they like it?), Level 2 (Learning — did they learn it?), Level 3 (Behavior — do they use it on the job?), Level 4 (Results — did it impact the organization?). Each level builds on the previous one.\n\n正确的顺序是：第1级（反应——他们喜欢吗？）、第2级（学习——他们学会了吗？）、第3级（行为——他们在工作中应用了吗？）、第4级（结果——对组织有影响吗？）。每一级都建立在前一级的基础上。","related":[{"n":"20.5","t":"Kirkpatrick四级评估"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A construction contract requires the subcontractor to indemnify and hold the owner harmless for injuries to the subcontractor's own employees. This arrangement is best classified as:","options":["Risk transfer by contract","Risk retention","Risk avoidance","Loss reduction"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Indemnification and hold-harmless clauses shift financial responsibility to another party, which is contractual risk transfer. They do not remove the hazard or reduce injuries, and the owner may still face regulatory and reputational exposure. Retention would mean the owner keeps the loss, and avoidance would mean not doing the work.\n\n赔偿与免责条款把财务责任转移给另一方，属于合同风险转移。它既不消除危害也不减少伤害，业主仍可能面临监管与声誉风险。保留是业主自担损失，规避则是不做这项作业。","related":[{"n":"11.6","t":"风险财务五大策略"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which team composition satisfies the PSM requirement for a process hazard analysis?","options":["A single outside consultant who is certified in the HAZOP method and has ten years of experience","The plant manager plus the maintenance supervisor and the unit process engineer","Any three employees drawn from the plant safety department, one of whom has audited the unit","A team with engineering and operations expertise, one employee who knows the process, and one who knows the method"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The PHA team must combine engineering and process-operations expertise, include at least one employee with specific knowledge and experience of the process being evaluated, and include someone knowledgeable in the selected methodology. A single consultant, or a team without process-specific knowledge, does not meet the requirement. The employee member also supports the employee-participation element.\n\nPHA 团队必须具备工程与工艺操作专长，包含至少一名对被评估工艺有特定知识与经验的员工，以及一名熟悉所选方法的成员。单一顾问或不具备工艺特定知识的团队不符合要求。员工成员同时落实员工参与要素。","related":[{"n":"2.4","t":"PHA与HAZOP"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A Pareto analysis of workplace injuries reveals that 75% of injuries come from three hazard categories out of fifteen total categories. What is the primary purpose of this analysis?","options":["To benchmark the organization against industry averages","To calculate the statistical mean of injury types","To demonstrate compliance with OSHA recordkeeping requirements","To prioritize resources toward the few causes that produce the most effects"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Pareto analysis (based on the 80/20 rule) helps prioritize improvement efforts by identifying the \"vital few\" causes that account for the majority of effects. By focusing resources on those three hazard categories, the organization achieves maximum impact from its intervention efforts.\n\n帕累托分析（基于80/20法则）通过识别占大多数结果的\"关键少数\"原因，有助于确定改进工作的优先顺序。通过将资源集中在三个危害类别上，组织可使其干预措施达到最大效果。","related":[{"n":"6.8","t":"帕累托分析与数据展示"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following scenarios represents ELIMINATION of a hazard?","options":["Automating a manual palletizing task so no worker performs the lifting","Providing respirators to workers painting in a spray booth","Replacing a gasoline engine with an electric motor","Switching from a solvent-based to a water-based paint"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Automating the task removes the manual lifting hazard entirely — the hazard no longer exists, so this is Elimination. Replacing the engine or paint are Substitution; respirators are PPE.\n\n自动化任务完全消除了人工搬运危害——危害不复存在，所以是消除。更换发动机或油漆是替代；呼吸器是PPE。","related":[{"n":"1.2","t":"消除与替代"},{"n":"1.1","t":"控制层级"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A manufacturing process uses a solvent-based adhesive that emits toxic vapors. The BEST control according to the hierarchy of controls is:","options":["Substitute a water-based non-toxic adhesive","Rotate workers every 2 hours","Provide workers with respirators","Install local exhaust ventilation"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Substitution (replacing the solvent-based adhesive with a water-based non-toxic one) ranks above engineering controls (LEV), administrative controls (rotation), and PPE (respirators). Substitution removes or reduces the hazardous agent itself.\n\n替代（用水性无毒胶替代溶剂型胶）排名高于工程控制（局部排风）、行政控制（轮换）和PPE（呼吸器）。替代消除或减少了危险物质本身。","related":[{"n":"9.5","t":"控制层级"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A safety professional finds that an incident was caused by a combination of a faulty sensor AND a maintenance worker bypassing the alarm. Which RCA method is BEST suited to analyze the combination of failures?","options":["5 Whys","Fault Tree Analysis (FTA)","Pareto Analysis","Mean calculation"],"correct":1,"explanation":"FTA uses Boolean AND/OR gates to model combinations of failures leading to a top event. Here, the top event occurred when the sensor failed (AND) the alarm was bypassed — a combination that FTA captures explicitly. 5 Whys follows a single chain and may miss this interaction.\n\nFTA使用布尔与/或门对导致顶事件的故障组合建模。此处，顶事件在传感器失效（与）报警被旁路时发生——FTA能明确捕捉这一组合。5Why法跟踪单一条链，可能遗漏这种交互。","related":[{"n":"7.5","t":"根源分析方法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A safety project requires design (4 weeks), then procurement (5 weeks), then installation (3 weeks). Permitting (6 weeks) can start after design and runs in parallel with procurement and installation. What is the minimum project duration?","options":["18 weeks","10 weeks","12 weeks","14 weeks"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The sequential path is 4 plus 5 plus 3, or 12 weeks, and it is the critical path. The permitting path is 4 plus 6, or 10 weeks, so permitting has 2 weeks of float and does not extend the project. Adding all durations, 18 weeks, would wrongly assume every task is sequential.\n\n串行路径为 4 + 5 + 3 = 12 周，即关键路径。许可路径为 4 + 6 = 10 周，因此有 2 周浮动时间，不会延长项目工期。把各项工期相加得 18 周，是错误假设所有任务都必须串行。","related":[{"n":"8.5","t":"RACI 与项目时间线"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A safety professional is offered a fee by an equipment vendor to recommend that vendor's products over a safer competitor. According to the BCSP Code of Ethics, the CSP should:","options":["Decline, because this is a conflict of interest and the paramount duty is the safety of people","Accept the fee since it does not affect the final recommendation","Accept the fee only if the vendor's products are adequate","Accept the fee but keep it confidential"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The BCSP Code of Ethics requires avoiding conflicts of interest and holding paramount the safety of people. Accepting an incentive to recommend a product over a safer alternative is both a conflict of interest and a compromise of the duty to protect people.\n\nBCSP道德准则要求避免利益冲突并将人员安全置于最高地位。收受激励而推荐某个产品而弃更安全替代品于不顾，既是利益冲突，也损害了保护人员的职责。","related":[{"n":"8.8","t":"道德与法律"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Under TSCA, a manufacturer must submit a Premanufacture Notice (PMN) at least how many days before producing a new chemical?","options":["60 days","90 days","180 days","30 days"],"correct":1,"explanation":"TSCA Section 5 requires a PMN to be submitted at least 90 days before the manufacture of a new chemical not listed on the TSCA inventory. EPA then conducts a review and can impose restrictions.\n\nTSCA第5条要求在制造未列入TSCA清单的新化学品前至少90天提交PMN。EPA随后进行审查并可施加限制。","related":[{"n":"15.3","t":"CERCLA超级基金法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A machine shop with 18 employees keeps six portable fire extinguishers on the floor and trains selected employees to use them on incipient fires. The shop has no written emergency action plan. Which statement is correct under 29 CFR 1910.38?","options":["No plan is needed because the shop has fewer than 20 employees","No plan is needed unless the shop employs more than 25 people","A written emergency action plan is required because employees may use the portable extinguishers provided","A plan is required only if the local fire department inspects the building"],"correct":2,"explanation":"An emergency action plan is triggered when another OSHA standard requires one, or when the employer provides portable fire extinguishers that employees may use to fight incipient fires (1910.38 with 1910.157). The classic exemption applies only where the employer has a total evacuation policy and no employee is permitted to use an extinguisher. Employee-count thresholds such as 25 do not appear in 1910.38; the 10-employee provision concerns oral rather than written communication.\n\n当另一项OSHA标准要求时，或雇主提供便携式灭火器且员工可以用其扑救初期火灾时，就必须制定应急行动计划（1910.38配合1910.157）。唯一典型的豁免情形是：雇主要求全部疏散且不允许员工使用灭火器。1910.38中并没有25人这样的门槛；10名员工的规定只涉及可以口头而非书面传达。","related":[{"n":"12.2","t":"应急行动计划"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A utility crew plans a 6-foot-deep trench in Type B soil. The competent person says no protective system is needed because the soil looks solid. What is the correct determination?","options":["The competent person is correct if no water is present","A protective system is required only above 8 feet","A protective system is required at 5 feet or deeper, unless in stable rock","Shoring is required, but sloping is never permitted in Type B soil"],"correct":2,"explanation":"1926.652 requires a protective system for excavations 5 feet or deeper unless the excavation is made entirely in stable rock. Type B soil permits sloping at 1:1, benching, shoring, or a trench box, so several options exist but one is mandatory. Below 5 feet, a protective system is still required if the competent person finds a potential cave-in hazard.\n\n1926.652 要求深度 5 英尺及以上的挖掘必须设防护系统，除非整个开挖位于稳定岩层中。B 型土可采用 1:1 放坡、台阶式开挖、支撑或沟槽箱，选择多样但必须选一种。深度不足 5 英尺时，若合格人员判定存在坍塌可能，仍须设防护系统。","related":[{"n":"4.6","t":"挖掘与沟槽"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"After a near miss, an investigation shows that operators routinely defeat a keyed interlock with a bent paper clip because the interlock stops the machine every time a part jams. What is the BEST recommendation?","options":["Discipline the operators who defeated the interlock with the paper clip","Redesign the interlock and the jam-clearing method so bypass is unnecessary","Post a sign stating that defeating interlocks is prohibited in the plant","Add the interlock check to the monthly safety inspection checklist"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The bypass is a symptom: the control conflicts with getting the work done, so workers route around it. The durable fix is an engineering redesign — for example an interlock that permits slow jog during clearing, or a jam-clearing tool that keeps hands out — plus tamper-resistant hardware. Discipline, signage, and inspection leave the underlying conflict in place and are lower-level controls.\n\n旁路只是症状：控制措施与完成作业相冲突，工人自然会绕过。持久解法是工程改造——例如允许清堵时慢速点动的联锁，或使手不进入危险区的清堵工具——并采用防拆硬件。纪律、标识与检查没有消除根本冲突，属于较低层级措施。","related":[{"n":"1.3","t":"工程控制"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A compliance audit under PSM must be performed by:","options":["A team that includes at least one person knowledgeable in the process being audited","External third-party consultants exclusively","The facility safety manager alone","Only OSHA inspectors"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The audit team must include at least one person knowledgeable in the process being audited (1910.119(o)(2)). The audit may be internal or external, but the process-knowledge requirement is mandatory.\n\n审核团队必须包括至少一名了解被审核工艺的人员（1910.119(o)(2)）。审核可以是内部或外部的，但了解工艺的要求是强制性的。","related":[{"n":"2.2","t":"PSM的14个要素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A facility stores a chemical at 60 psig. An engineer proposes lowering the storage pressure to 15 psig to reduce release consequences. This ISD strategy is:","options":["Minimize","Moderate","Simplify","Elimination"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Lowering pressure, temperature, or concentration to reduce hazard severity is Moderate (Attenuation). The chemical remains the same and the quantity is unchanged — only the process conditions are made less severe.\n\n通过降低压力、温度或浓度来减轻危害严重性属于缓和（弱化）。化学品种类和数量不变——只是工艺条件变得不那么剧烈。","related":[{"n":"1.7","t":"本质安全设计(ISD)"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"The \"M\" in SMART objectives stands for:","options":["Measurable","Mandatory","Multi-level","Motivating"],"correct":0,"explanation":"SMART = Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound. Measurable means the objective has quantifiable criteria for success (e.g., \"with 100% accuracy,\" \"within 2 minutes\").\n\nSMART = 具体、可衡量、可实现、相关、有时限。可衡量意味着目标有可量化的成功标准（如\"100%准确率\"、\"2分钟内\"）。","related":[{"n":"19.3","t":"ADDIE模型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Site A has a TRIR of 6.0 based on 40,000 hours and one recordable case. Site B has a TRIR of 3.0 based on 2,000,000 hours and 30 cases. Which conclusion is BEST supported?","options":["Site A's rate rests on one case and is statistically unstable","Neither rate is valid because both denominators are too small","Site A is definitely about twice as hazardous as Site B","Site B is definitely about twice as hazardous as Site A"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The 200,000-hour base produces very unstable rates when the numerator is one case, so a single event can move the site rate by 6.0 points. Site B's 30 cases give a far more reliable estimate. The standard practice is to aggregate multiple years, use confidence intervals, or compare case counts rather than point rates when exposure is small.\n\n当分子只有 1 例时，200,000 小时基数会产生极不稳定的率，单一事件就能让场地率变动 6.0。B 场地 30 例的估计可靠得多。规范做法是合并多年数据、使用置信区间，或在暴露量很小时直接比较案例数而非点估计率。","related":[{"n":"6.4","t":"基准比较"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"What is the primary purpose of the Annex SL high-level structure shared by ISO management system standards?","options":["To replace the need for ISO 19011 audit guidance","To eliminate the requirement for internal audits","To ensure all ISO management system standards share a common core structure, terms, and concepts","To increase the cost of certification for organizations"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Annex SL provides a unified high-level structure with identical clause numbering, core text, and common terms across all ISO management system standards. This enables easier integration of quality (9001), environmental (14001), and OH&S (45001) management systems.\n\nAnnex SL为所有ISO管理体系标准提供统一的高层结构，具有相同的条款编号、核心文本和通用术语。这使得质量（9001）、环境（14001）和OH&S（45001）管理体系更易于整合。","related":[{"n":"5.1","t":"ISO 45001:2018"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A facility has three aboveground oil tanks: 10,000 gallons, 8,000 gallons, and 6,000 gallons. The engineer designs secondary containment to 110% of the largest tank. What is the required containment volume?","options":["8,800 gallons","11,000 gallons","13,200 gallons","26,400 gallons"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Containment = 110% × largest tank = 1.10 × 10,000 = 11,000 gallons. Note: SPCC requires at least the largest single tank plus freeboard; 110% is a common design factor. The aggregate-total 10% alternative (0.10 × 24,000 = 2,400 gal) is smaller, so 110% of the largest governs.\n\n围堵容积 = 最大罐的110% = 1.10 × 10,000 = 11,000加仑。注意：SPCC要求至少最大单个储罐加上超高；110%是常见的设计系数。总量10%的方案（0.10 × 24,000 = 2,400加仑）较小，因此按最大罐的110%执行。","related":[{"n":"14.4","t":"危险物质储存"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-14.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"ANSI/ASSP Z490.1 requires which combination of evaluation for EHS training?","options":["Both formative and summative evaluation","Kirkpatrick Level 1 only","Summative evaluation only","Formative evaluation only"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Z490.1 requires both formative evaluation (during development and delivery, to improve the program) and summative evaluation (at the end, to judge whether objectives were met). Relying on reaction data alone does not satisfy the standard. This dual requirement is what links evaluation to continuous improvement.\n\nZ490.1 要求同时进行形成性评估（在开发与交付期间进行，用于改进项目）和总结性评估（在结束时判断目标是否达成）。仅依赖反应数据不满足该标准。正是这一双重要求把评估与持续改进连接起来。","related":[{"n":"19.2","t":"ANSI/ASSP Z490.1"},{"n":"19.8","t":"形成性与总结性评估"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is a key requirement for rigging hardware used with cranes?","options":["Rigging hardware never needs inspection","Inspect before each shift and remove from service any sling with cracks, >10% wear, deformation, or damaged safety latches","Inspect once per year only","All slings may be used indefinitely if they look clean"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Rigging hardware (slings, shackles, hooks) must be inspected before each shift. Items with cracks, wear exceeding 10%, deformation, or missing/damaged safety latches must be removed from service. Damage thresholds and inspection frequency are tested on the CSP exam.\n\n索具硬件（吊索、卸扣、吊钩）必须在每次换班前检查。出现裂纹、磨损超过10%、变形或安全锁扣缺失/损坏的物品必须停用。损伤阈值和检查频率是CSP考试内容。","related":[{"n":"4.8","t":"物料搬运与储存"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An investigation's 5 Whys chain ends with the statement that the operator was careless and did not follow the procedure. Why is this an inadequate stopping point?","options":["Because it names a person rather than the system that allowed the deviation","Because carelessness is never a real factor in incidents","Because 5 Whys must reach exactly five levels of questioning","Because the operator should be interviewed a second time"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Stopping at individual blame produces a corrective action of retraining or discipline, which leaves the conditions that permitted the error fully intact. A useful root cause explains why the deviation was possible, for example an unclear procedure, missing interlock or production pressure. Human error can be a starting point for the analysis but not the end of it.\n\n止步于追究个人责任，最终只会得出“再培训”或“纪律处分”这类纠正措施，而使错误得以发生的条件原封不动。有效的根本原因要解释偏差为何可能发生，例如程序不清、缺少联锁或生产压力。人的失误可以作为分析的起点，但不能作为分析的终点。","related":[{"n":"7.5","t":"根源分析方法"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which control type relies the LEAST on human behavior or compliance?","options":["Written safety procedures","Engineering controls","Administrative controls","PPE"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Engineering controls provide protection through physical design (guards, ventilation, interlocks) and work regardless of whether the worker remembers to comply. Administrative controls, procedures, and PPE all depend on people following them correctly.\n\n工程控制通过物理设计（防护罩、通风、联锁）提供保护，无论工人是否记得遵守都能发挥作用。行政控制、程序和PPE都依赖于人们正确执行。","related":[{"n":"9.5","t":"控制层级"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An auditor finds that corrective actions for a serious fall hazard were recorded as complete, but fall protection is still missing at three of the five locations named in the original finding. How should this be classified?","options":["An opportunity for improvement","A minor nonconformity, because a corrective-action record exists","A conformity, because the corrective-action process was followed","A major nonconformity, because the corrective-action process failed systematically"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A finding is classified by its effect on the system, and here the corrective-action process accepted unverified closure on a serious hazard across most of the affected locations. That is a systemic failure affecting the system's ability to control risk, which makes it major rather than minor. The existence of a record proves paperwork, not closure, and the hazard remains.\n\n不符合的严重程度取决于其对体系的影响。此处纠正措施流程在严重坠落危害上接受了未经核实的关闭，且涉及多数受影响位置，属于影响体系控制风险能力的系统性失效，应判为严重不符合。有记录只能证明有纸面流程，不能证明危害已消除。","related":[{"n":"5.3","t":"ISO 19011 审核"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"An employer buys respirators, goggles, and gloves for every painter and hands them out at the start of the season, but has never documented a workplace hazard assessment. Which requirement of 29 CFR 1910.132(d) is unmet?","options":["The employer must provide PPE only after a physician's approval","The employer must replace PPE every 12 months","The employer must certify the hazard assessment in writing before selecting PPE","The employer must obtain employee consent before issuing PPE"],"correct":2,"explanation":"1910.132(d) requires the employer to assess the workplace for hazards that necessitate PPE and to certify that assessment in writing. Purchasing PPE without that documented assessment leaves no basis for selection or fit, and no evidence that higher-level controls were considered and found infeasible. The standard contains no annual replacement, consent, or physician-approval requirement.\n\n1910.132(d) 要求雇主评估需要 PPE 的工作场所危害，并以书面形式认证该评估。未做书面评估就采购 PPE，既无选型与贴合度的依据，也无法证明已考虑更高层级控制且其不可行。标准中没有年度更换、员工同意或医生批准的要求。","related":[{"n":"1.4","t":"行政控制与PPE"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"On a 5×5 risk matrix, what is the risk score for a hazard with Likelihood = 4 (Likely) and Severity = 3 (Moderate)?","options":["7","9","12","16"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Risk = 4 × 3 = 12. This falls in the high-risk (orange) region of the typical 5×5 matrix, indicating the need for prompt risk reduction measures.\n\n风险 = 4 × 3 = 12。这落在典型5×5矩阵的高风险（橙色）区域，表明需要及时采取风险降低措施。","related":[{"n":"9.4","t":"风险矩阵"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A competent person classifies excavation soil with unconfined compressive strength of 0.3 tons per square foot (tsf). This soil is classified as:","options":["Type A","Type B","Type C","Stable Rock"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Type C soil has unconfined compressive strength ≤ 0.5 tsf. Type B is > 0.5 tsf but < 1.5 tsf. Type A is ≥ 1.5 tsf. Given the 0.3 tsf value, this is Type C — the least stable classification, requiring the steepest slope (1.5:1 or 34°) and permitting only sloping or shielding (no benching allowed in Type C).\n\nC型土壤的无侧限抗压强度≤0.5 tsf。B型为>0.5 tsf但<1.5 tsf。A型为≥1.5 tsf。给定0.3 tsf数值，这是C型——最不稳定的分类，需要最陡的坡度（1.5:1或34°），仅允许放坡或防护（C型不允许台阶式开挖）。","related":[{"n":"4.6","t":"挖掘与沟槽"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"The \"Hot Work Permit\" PSM element (Element 9) applies to which operations?","options":["Any work inside a confined space","Routine production operations in the control room","Any maintenance operation on a covered process","Welding, cutting, brazing, grinding, or other spark-producing operations on or near a covered process"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The hot work permit is required before welding, cutting, brazing, grinding, or other spark/flame-producing operations on or near a covered process. It must be issued before work begins and specify the date, the object to be worked on, and the duration of validity.\n\n动火作业许可证必须在覆盖工艺上或附近的焊接、切割、钎焊、打磨或其他产生火花/火焰的作业前签发。必须在工作开始前签发，并注明日期、作业对象和有效期。","related":[{"n":"2.2","t":"PSM的14个要素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A three-day hazardous materials incident requires tracking of responder hours, rented heavy equipment, contractor invoices, and two injury claims. Which ICS section is responsible for this function?","options":["Finance and Administration","Planning","Logistics","Operations"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The Finance and Administration section tracks incident costs, timekeeping, procurement, contracts, and compensation or claims. Logistics obtains facilities, supplies, and services but does not own cost documentation, Operations directs tactical resources, and Planning develops the Incident Action Plan and maintains situation status. Cost recovery and claim documentation at a long incident are classic Finance and Administration duties.\n\n财务与行政处负责跟踪事故成本、考勤、采购、合同以及赔偿与索赔。后勤处负责获取设施、物资与服务，但不负责成本记录；行动处指挥战术资源；规划处制定事故行动计划并维护态势信息。长时间事故中的费用追偿与索赔记录正是财务与行政处的典型职责。","related":[{"n":"12.4","t":"事故指挥系统"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A hole cover installed to protect workers must be capable of supporting:","options":["1× the maximum expected load","2× the maximum expected load","5× the maximum expected load","100% of the weight of any single worker"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Hole covers must support twice the weight of the maximum expected load, must be secured against displacement, and must be marked \"HOLE\" or \"COVER.\" This 2× requirement is frequently tested.\n\n孔洞盖板必须能支撑最大预期负载的2倍重量，必须固定防止移位，并标记\"HOLE\"或\"COVER\"。这一2倍要求是高频考点。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"},{"n":"3.9","t":"CSP11常见工作场所危害"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"According to the hierarchy, PPE should be used as a control only when:","options":["Employees request it for comfort","The hazard was identified during a safety audit","It is the cheapest option available","Higher-level controls are not feasible or are being implemented"],"correct":3,"explanation":"PPE is the last line of defense. It is appropriate when elimination, substitution, engineering, and administrative controls are not feasible, or as a supplement while engineering controls are being installed. OSHA standards such as 1910.95 and 1910.134 codify this order.\n\nPPE是最后一道防线。当消除、替代、工程和行政控制不可行时，或作为工程控制安装期间的补充，才适合使用。1910.95和1910.134等OSHA标准对此顺序有明确规定。","related":[{"n":"1.1","t":"控制层级"},{"n":"1.5","t":"关键OSHA标准"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"What is the probability output of an OR gate with two independent basic events having probabilities of 0.1 and 0.2?","options":["0.28","0.12","0.02","0.3"],"correct":0,"explanation":"For an OR gate: P = P(A) + P(B) - P(A)xP(B) = 0.1 + 0.2 - (0.1 x 0.2) = 0.3 - 0.02 = 0.28. The subtraction prevents double-counting the intersection.\n\n对于或门：P = P(A) + P(B) - P(A)xP(B) = 0.1 + 0.2 - (0.1 x 0.2) = 0.3 - 0.02 = 0.28。减去交集部分以避免重复计算。","related":[{"n":"10.4","t":"FTA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"What is the maximum allowable capacity of a flammable liquid storage cabinet, and how many cabinets may be located in a single fire area (without additional sprinkler allowance)?","options":["120 gallons; 2 cabinets","60 gallons; 3 cabinets","60 gallons; 5 cabinets","120 gallons; 3 cabinets"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Per OSHA 1910.106 and NFPA 30, a flammable liquid storage cabinet may hold a maximum of 60 gallons of Class I and II flammable liquids. Not more than 3 cabinets may be located in a single fire area, unless the facility has an automatic sprinkler system (which may allow additional cabinets per the AHJ).\n\n根据OSHA 1910.106和NFPA 30，易燃液体储存柜最大可容纳60加仑Ⅰ类和Ⅱ类易燃液体。每个防火分区最多可放置3个柜子，除非设施有自动喷淋系统（可能允许更多，由AHJ决定）。","related":[{"n":"14.1","t":"SPCC泄漏预防控制与对策"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-14.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Management finalizes a mandatory cut-resistant glove policy and announces it the day it takes effect. Workers had no input and report that the gloves interfere with dexterity at the assembly fixture. Which ISO 45001 requirement was missed?","options":["Clause 7.2 competence","Clause 8.1.2 management of change","Clause 9.1 monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation","Clause 5.4 consultation and participation of workers"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Clause 5.4 requires the organization to establish processes for consultation and participation of workers at all applicable levels, including in the development and review of OH&S policies and in decisions on controls. Selecting PPE that workers must wear without consulting them on fit and task interference is the classic failure this clause targets. A change to PPE can also involve management of change, but the specific requirement violated here is consultation and participation.\n\n第5.4条要求组织建立员工协商与参与的机制，覆盖各相关层级，包括职业健康安全方针的制定与评审以及控制措施的决策。在未就贴合度与作业干扰征求意见的情况下强制推行手套，正是该条款针对的典型失误。更换PPE也可能涉及变更管理，但此处被违反的具体要求是协商与参与。","related":[{"n":"5.1","t":"ISO 45001 体系"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"The safety manager prepares and signs the annual management review, then circulates it to the plant manager for information. Which statement is correct?","options":["Acceptable, provided the review is repeated every year","Not acceptable, because management review must be conducted by top management","Not acceptable, because management review must be conducted by external auditors","Acceptable, because the safety manager owns the OH&S programme"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Clause 9.3 assigns management review to top management, which evaluates suitability, adequacy and effectiveness and commits resources. The safety professional prepares inputs and analysis but cannot substitute for top management's decision-making role. Annual frequency is good practice, but frequency does not fix the ownership problem, and external auditors have no role in the organization's management review.\n\n第9.3条把管理评审交给最高管理层，由其评价适宜性、充分性和有效性并作出资源承诺。安全专业人员负责准备输入与分析，但不能替代最高管理层的决策角色。每年开展是好做法，但频率无法弥补主体错位；外部审核员在管理评审中没有任何角色。","related":[{"n":"5.5","t":"管理评审"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"In a trench excavation greater than 4 feet deep, ladders or other means of egress must be provided so that no worker has to travel more than what distance laterally to reach a ladder?","options":["15 feet","20 feet","25 feet","50 feet"],"correct":2,"explanation":"OSHA requires that in trenches 4 feet or deeper, a ladder, stairway, or ramp must be located so that no employee must travel more than 25 feet laterally to reach the means of egress. This ensures that workers can exit the trench quickly in the event of a cave-in or other emergency. The ladder must extend at least 3 feet above the landing surface.\n\nOSHA要求，在4英尺或更深的沟槽中，梯子、楼梯或坡道的位置必须使任何员工到达逃生通道的横向距离不超过25英尺。这确保工人能在塌方或其他紧急情况下迅速撤离沟槽。梯子必须伸出着陆面至少3英尺。","related":[{"n":"4.6","t":"挖掘与沟槽"},{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘安全要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A convenience store employee is robbed at gunpoint by an unknown person. This is an example of which type of workplace violence?","options":["Type IV — Personal Relationship","Type I — Criminal Intent","Type II — Customer/Client","Type III — Worker-on-Worker"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Type I violence involves an offender with no legitimate business relationship, typically committing a crime (robbery, trespassing). This is the most common type of fatal workplace violence and disproportionately affects late-night retail.\n\n类型I暴力涉及与工作场所无合法业务关系的犯罪者，通常实施犯罪（抢劫、非法侵入）。这是最常见的致命工作场所暴力类型，对深夜零售影响尤为严重。","related":[{"n":"13.9","t":"职场暴力"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"An unguarded saw creates a hazard. Installing a blade guard is an example of which control?","options":["Administrative control","Elimination","Substitution","Engineering control"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A blade guard is an engineering control — it physically isolates the worker from the hazard without relying on behavior. The hazard (the saw blade) still exists, so it is not elimination.\n\n防护罩是工程控制——物理上将工人与危害隔离，不依赖行为。危害（锯片）仍然存在，所以不是消除。","related":[{"n":"9.5","t":"控制层级"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A facility uses red padlocks for LOTO, but the same padlocks are also used to secure tool cribs. Which LOTO device requirement is violated?","options":["Singular purpose: the devices may not be used for anything other than controlling energy","Substantial: the tag must be non-reusable and self-locking","Identifiable: the device must show the identity of the employee who applied it","Durable: the lock must withstand the environment for the duration of exposure"],"correct":0,"explanation":"1910.147(c)(5)(i)(E) requires lockout and tagout devices to be used only for controlling hazardous energy, so dual use for storage security is prohibited. Devices must also be durable, standardized within the facility, substantial, and identifiable as to the employee who applied them. Mixing purposes creates confusion about whether equipment is truly locked out.\n\n1910.147(c)(5)(i)(E) 要求上锁挂牌装置只能用于控制危险能量，因此兼作储物柜锁属于违规。装置还必须耐用、在设施内标准化、牢固，并能识别施加者。用途混用会造成设备是否真正已上锁的混淆。","related":[{"n":"4.5","t":"LOTO职责与程序"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Which GHS-style term describes a substance that causes birth defects or developmental abnormalities?","options":["Teratogen","Sensitizer","Carcinogen","Mutagen"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A teratogen causes birth defects (developmental malformations) — examples include thalidomide, alcohol, isotretinoin, and methylmercury. A mutagen causes DNA mutation; a carcinogen causes cancer; a sensitizer causes allergic reactions.\n\n致畸物导致出生缺陷（发育畸形）——示例包括沙利度胺、酒精、异维A酸和甲基汞。致突变物导致DNA突变；致癌物导致癌症；致敏物导致过敏反应。","related":[{"n":"17.3","t":"听力保护计划HCP"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A worker's 8-hour TWA is 98 dBA. The employer issues earmuffs labeled NRR 25. Applying the OSHA derating method, what is the estimated protected exposure, and is it adequate?","options":["91 dBA — adequate, below the 90 dBA PEL","89 dBA — not adequate; more attenuation is needed","73 dBA — adequate, but overprotection is a concern","84 dBA — adequate, below the 85 dBA level"],"correct":1,"explanation":"OSHA derating: protected level = TWA − (NRR − 7)/2 = 98 − (25 − 7)/2 = 98 − 9 = 89 dBA. Hearing protection must bring exposure below 85 dBA, so 89 dBA is still too high; a higher-attenuation protector or dual protection (earplugs under muffs) is needed. The derating is required because labeled NRRs overstate real-world protection.\n\nOSHA 降噪修正：受保护暴露 = TWA − (NRR − 7)/2 = 98 − (25 − 7)/2 = 98 − 9 = 89 dBA。听力防护必须把暴露降到 85 dBA 以下，89 dBA 仍然偏高，需要更高衰减量的防护器或双重防护（耳塞加耳罩）。标称 NRR 高估了实际防护效果，因此必须做修正。","related":[{"n":"17.2","t":"噪声计算"},{"n":"17.3","t":"听力保护计划"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d6.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A facility is already in full compliance with OSHA PSM. Which additional obligation arises from being an RMP Program 3 facility?","options":["Retaining PHA revalidation records for ten years instead of five","Submitting an RMP to EPA with off-site consequence analysis of release scenarios","Training operators every two years instead of every three","Installing additional relief valves on every covered process vessel"],"correct":1,"explanation":"RMP requires registration and submission to EPA of a risk management plan containing off-site consequence analysis, a prevention program, and an emergency response program. The prevention program largely mirrors PSM, so the new work is the consequence analysis, registration, and community coordination. RMP does not shorten PSM training intervals or mandate additional relief devices.\n\nRMP 要求向 EPA 注册并提交风险管理计划，内容包括厂外后果分析、预防计划与应急响应计划。预防计划与 PSM 大体对应，因此新增工作是后果分析、注册与社区协调。RMP 不会缩短 PSM 培训周期，也不强制增设泄压装置。","related":[{"n":"2.7","t":"EPA RMP"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A trainer wants learners to be able to compare and contrast different types of fall protection systems and recommend the most appropriate one for a given scenario. At what level of Bloom's Taxonomy is this objective?","options":["Apply","Analyze","Evaluate","Understand"],"correct":2,"explanation":"\"Compare, contrast, and recommend\" are evaluation-level verbs. At the Evaluate level (level 5), learners make judgments based on criteria and defend their choices. Analyze (level 4) involves breaking down information; Evaluate (level 5) goes further by making a judgment and recommendation.\n\n\"比较、对比和推荐\"是评价层次的动词。在评价层次（第5层），学习者依据标准做出判断并为其选择辩护。分析（第4层）涉及分解信息；评价（第5层）更进一步，做出判断和推荐。","related":[{"n":"19.1","t":"培训需求评估TNA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which OSHA violation classification applies when a hazardous condition has a substantial probability of causing death or serious harm AND the employer knew or should have known of it?","options":["De minimis","Other-than-serious","Serious","Willful"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A Serious violation exists when there is substantial probability of death or serious physical harm and the employer knew or should have known of the hazard. It carries a mandatory penalty. Other-than-serious would probably not cause serious harm; willful requires intent.\n\n当存在死亡或严重身体伤害的重大可能性，且雇主知道或应该知道该危害时，构成严重违规。它带有强制性处罚。非严重违规可能不会造成严重伤害；故意违规要求故意性。","related":[{"n":"8.8","t":"道德与法律"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A distribution center installs flashing warning lights and a mirror, and writes a rule requiring a spotter at a blind corner where forklifts meet pedestrians. No physical barrier is added because the fire code requires the aisle to stay open. What level are these controls, and what is their main weakness?","options":["Elimination, because the collision hazard is removed","Administrative controls that work only while people comply","Engineering controls that fail only when the lights burn out","PPE, because they protect only the individual"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Lights, a mirror, a spotter rule, and signage change how people work rather than physically separating them, so they are administrative controls. Their reliability depends on continuous human compliance: a driver who ignores the light or a spotter who leaves the post defeats them. The fire code restriction is what makes a physical barrier infeasible here, so choosing administrative controls is defensible.\n\n警示灯、反光镜、观察员规定与标识改变的是人的作业方式，而非物理隔离，因此属于行政控制。其可靠性取决于持续的人工遵守：司机无视灯光或观察员离岗，控制即失效。正是消防规范的限制使物理隔离在此不可行，因此选择行政控制是合理的。","related":[{"n":"1.4","t":"行政控制与PPE"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"What is the maximum spacing between intermediate vertical members (balusters) of a guardrail system?","options":["24 inches","36 inches","12 inches","19 inches"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Intermediate vertical members (balusters) must be spaced no more than 19 inches apart. This prevents a worker from slipping through the opening between the top rail and the walking surface.\n\n中间垂直构件（栏杆柱）间距不得超过19英寸。这防止工人从顶部横杆与行走表面之间的开口滑出。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A safety professional selects the \"worst-case\" day (highest production, all tasks running) for sampling. This strategy is:","options":["Invalid — sampling must be random","Conservative — appropriate for compliance screening because it represents the highest plausible exposure","Required by OSHA for all air sampling","Only used for noise dosimetry"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Worst-case sampling is a conservative strategy: if the highest-exposure scenario is below the OEL, then all other days are also below. It is well suited to compliance screening. Random sampling better supports statistical inference about the typical exposure distribution.\n\n最坏情况采样是保守策略：如果最高暴露场景低于OEL，则所有其他日子也都低于。它非常适合合规筛查。随机采样更好地支持对典型暴露分布的统计推断。","related":[{"n":"16.7","t":"暴露评估策略与统计分析"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-16.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A safety budget is built by taking last year's budget and increasing it by 3% across the board. This is an example of:","options":["Capital budgeting","Zero-based budgeting","Activity-based budgeting","Incremental budgeting"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Incremental budgeting uses the previous period's budget as a baseline and adjusts it by a percentage or increment. It is simple and stable but perpetuates historical inefficiencies and may not reflect current needs.\n\n增量预算以上期预算为基线并按百分比或增量调整。它简单稳定，但延续历史低效，可能不反映当前需求。","related":[{"n":"8.1","t":"预算"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Which OSHA standard requires role-specific training for entrants, attendants, and entry supervisors?","options":["1910.1200 Hazard Communication","1910.95 Hearing Conservation","1910.147 Lockout/Tagout","1910.146 Permit-Required Confined Spaces"],"correct":3,"explanation":"1910.146 (PRCS) requires role-specific training for entrants, attendants, entry supervisors, and rescue personnel — with retraining every 12 months or when duties change. Each role has distinct responsibilities and hazards.\n\n1910.146（PRCS）要求对进入者、监护者、进入主管和救援人员进行特定角色的培训——每12个月或职责变更时复训。每个角色有不同的职责和危害。","related":[{"n":"20.7","t":"OSHA培训要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"The primary benefit of a high near-miss reporting rate is that it:","options":["Increases the organization's TRIR","Allows proactive correction of hazards before they cause serious incidents","Satisfies OSHA mandatory reporting requirements","Eliminates the need for incident investigation"],"correct":1,"explanation":"High near-miss reporting allows the organization to identify and correct hazards before they produce serious incidents. Near-misses provide more, and earlier, data than rare serious incidents. They do not affect TRIR (not recordable) and do not replace investigation of actual incidents.\n\n高未遂事件报告率使组织能够在危害造成严重事故前识别并纠正。与罕见的严重事故相比，未遂事件提供更多、更早的数据。它们不影响TRIR（不可记录），也不取代对实际事故的调查。","related":[{"n":"7.6","t":"未遂事件报告与海因里希三角"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following is a typical INPUT to a management review?","options":["Policy approvals","Budget sign-offs","Decisions on resource allocation","OH&S performance data, audit results, and legal requirements"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Inputs to management review include status of previous actions, changes in context, OH&S performance data, audit results, adequacy of resources, and worker participation results. Decisions on resource allocation and policy approvals are OUTPUTS that result from the review.\n\n管理评审的输入包括以往措施的状况、环境变化、OH&S绩效数据、审核结果、资源充分性和员工参与结果。关于资源分配和政策审批的决策是评审产生的输出。","related":[{"n":"5.5","t":"管理评审"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"The Design phase of ADDIE produces which output?","options":["The attendance roster","The needs assessment report","The learning blueprint: objectives, assessment strategy, content sequence, and instructional strategies","The final slide deck"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The Design phase produces the instructional blueprint — learning objectives (using Bloom's taxonomy), assessment strategy, content sequencing, and instructional strategies. The Development phase then creates the actual materials (slides, handouts, exercises).\n\n设计阶段产出教学蓝图——学习目标（使用布鲁姆分类学）、评估策略、内容排序和教学策略。开发阶段随后创建实际材料（幻灯片、讲义、练习）。","related":[{"n":"19.5","t":"布鲁姆分类学"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is NOT a requirement of an OSHA LOTO tag?","options":["Warns of the hazard (e.g., \"DO NOT START\")","Contains the employee's social security number","Non-reusable and self-locking","Withstands at least 50 lbs of pull"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Tags must be durable, standardized, substantial (≥ 50 lb pull strength), non-reusable, self-locking, and must warn of the hazard. They must identify the employee who applied the device, but there is no requirement for a social security number — identification means name or other identifying information.\n\n标签必须耐用、标准化、牢固（≥50磅拉力）、不可重复使用、自锁并警告危害。必须标明施加装置的员工身份，但无社保号要求——身份标识指姓名或其他识别信息。","related":[{"n":"4.4","t":"上锁挂牌 (LOTO)"},{"n":"4.5","t":"LOTO人员职责与程序管理"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"On a cause-and-effect diagram using the 6M categories, inadequate lighting at a work station belongs in which category?","options":["Measurement","Man/People","Machine","Environment"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Lighting, temperature, noise, housekeeping and layout are environmental conditions, so they belong under Environment. Man/People covers training, fatigue and communication, Machine covers equipment condition and design, and Measurement covers inspection, monitoring and calibration. Correct categorization matters because it directs the team's brainstorming toward the right evidence.\n\n照明、温度、噪声、整洁和布局属于环境条件，应归入“环境（Environment）”分支。“人”涵盖培训、疲劳与沟通，“机”涵盖设备状态与设计，“测”涵盖检查、监测与校准。正确归类很重要，因为它把团队的头脑风暴引向相应的证据。","related":[{"n":"7.5","t":"根源分析方法"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A U-listed waste and a P-listed waste of the same chemical are being managed by a facility. Which statement is correct regarding their regulatory status?","options":["U-listed wastes are always more hazardous than P-listed wastes","Only U-listed wastes require a manifest","They are treated identically under RCRA","P-listed wastes are acutely hazardous with much lower quantity thresholds"],"correct":3,"explanation":"P-listed chemicals are acutely hazardous — the P-list triggers the 1 kg/month acute threshold that can classify a facility as an LQG, whereas the U-list (toxic) uses the standard 1,000 kg/month non-acute threshold. P-listed wastes have far lower quantity thresholds and stricter management requirements.\n\nP名录化学品属于急性危险品——P名录触发1公斤/月的急性阈值，可使设施被归类为LQG；而U名录（毒性）使用标准的1,000公斤/月非急性阈值。P名录废物数量阈值低得多，管理要求也更严格。","related":[{"n":"14.7","t":"危险物质运输与应急响应"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-14.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A Business Impact Analysis (BIA) primarily determines:","options":["Which hazards are present in a process","The impact of disruptions on critical business functions, including MTD and recovery priorities","The insurance premium for a facility","The fire extinguisher locations"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A BIA quantifies the consequences of disruptions on critical functions, identifies time-critical functions, and sets MTD and recovery priorities. It drives the RTO and RPO values used in continuity planning.\n\nBIA量化中断对关键职能的后果，识别时间关键职能，并设定MTD和恢复优先级。它驱动连续性规划中使用的RTO和RPO值。","related":[{"n":"12.9","t":"BIA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A hearing conservation program (1910.95) requires training at which exposure threshold?","options":["90 dBA TWA (PEL)","95 dBA TWA","80 dBA TWA","85 dBA TWA (action level)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Annual hearing conservation training is required when the 8-hour TWA equals or exceeds 85 dBA (the action level). At the action level, monitoring, audiograms, training, and free hearing protection are all required.\n\n当8小时TWA等于或超过85 dBA（行动水平）时，要求进行年度听力保护培训。在行动水平，监测、听力图、培训和免费听力保护都是必需的。","related":[{"n":"20.7","t":"OSHA培训要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A bow-tie for loss of containment credits two preventive barriers: a high-pressure alarm and an automatic shutdown. Both are implemented in the same PLC with a single power supply. What is the main weakness?","options":["Alarms are always mitigative rather than preventive barriers","A bow-tie requires at least three barriers on each side","Nothing, because two barriers always provide redundancy","Both share a PLC and power supply, so a single failure disables both"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Barrier independence is one of the four effectiveness criteria, and common-mode dependencies defeat it. If one PLC failure removes both the alarm and the shutdown, the left side of the bow-tie collapses to a single barrier. Adding a barrier that shares the same control platform does not add real protection.\n\n屏障独立性是四项有效性标准之一，共因依赖会破坏它。若一次 PLC 故障同时导致报警与停车失效，蝴蝶结左侧实际上只剩一道屏障。新增与原有屏障共用同一控制平台的措施，并不能带来真正的保护。","related":[{"n":"11.4","t":"蝴蝶结分析"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Two plants store the same flammable solvent. At Plant A, workers manually pour it from open drums in an occupied room. At Plant B, a closed transfer system is used and no one enters the room during transfer. Which statement is correct?","options":["The closed-system plant has a different hazard because the chemical is handled differently","Both plants carry identical risk because they store the same solvent","The hazard is the same at both plants, but the risk is lower where the closed transfer system prevents exposure","The closed-system plant has no hazard because the transfer is automated"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The intrinsic hazard, a flammable solvent, is identical at both sites. Risk depends on exposure and the probability of ignition, both of which the closed system greatly reduces, so the risk differs even though the hazard does not. Automation alone never removes a hazard; only eliminating the material would do that.\n\n易燃溶剂这一固有危害在两个厂区完全相同。风险取决于暴露与点火概率，密闭输送大幅降低二者，因此风险不同而危害相同。仅靠自动化并不能消除危害，只有消除物料本身才算消除。","related":[{"n":"9.1","t":"危害与风险的区别"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A company plans to replace a solvent-based parts cleaner with a water-based cleaner to eliminate VOC emissions. Under the pollution prevention hierarchy, this is an example of:","options":["Raw material substitution","Recycling","Dilution","End-of-pipe treatment"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Substituting a water-based cleaner for a solvent-based cleaner is raw material substitution — a source reduction measure under P2. It eliminates the pollutant at the source rather than treating or managing it after creation.\n\n用水性清洁剂替代溶剂型清洁剂属于原料替代——P2下的源头减量措施。它从源头消除了污染物，而不是在产生后再处理或管理。","related":[{"n":"14.6","t":"污染预防P2与BMP"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-14.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"ISO 45001 Clause 4 requires the organization to determine the external and internal issues that affect its OH&S management system. Which of the following is an EXTERNAL issue?","options":["Competence gaps among the site maintenance technicians","Worker morale and absenteeism trends inside the plant","New customer and supply-chain expectations for supplier OH&S performance","The maturity of the site safety culture"],"correct":2,"explanation":"External issues arise from the outside environment: legal, technological, market, cultural, social and economic conditions, including the expectations of customers and supply chains. Morale, culture maturity and internal competence gaps are all internal characteristics of the organization. Clause 4.1 requires both sets to be determined and then used to establish the scope and the risk planning in Clause 6.\n\n外部问题来自组织外部环境：法律、技术、市场、文化、社会与经济状况，以及顾客和供应链的期望。员工士气、安全文化成熟度和内部能力差距都属于组织内部问题。第4.1条要求同时确定内外部问题，并据此界定体系范围与第6条的风险策划。","related":[{"n":"5.1","t":"ISO 45001 体系"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A trainer asks experienced workers to share examples from their own jobs and connects new material to what they already know. Which andragogical assumption is being applied?","options":["Need to Know","Self-Concept","Experience","Motivation"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The \"Experience\" assumption recognizes that adults bring a rich reservoir of prior experience that serves as a learning resource. Drawing on learner experiences, group discussion, and connecting new material to prior knowledge applies this assumption.\n\n\"经验\"假设认识到成人带来了丰富的先前经验，可作为学习资源。利用学习者的经验、小组讨论以及将新材料与已有知识联系，就是应用这一假设。","related":[{"n":"20.1","t":"Knowles成人学习理论"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A worker servicing a conveyor must verify isolation after applying LOTO. The correct verification step is:","options":["Ask a coworker if the equipment is safe","Measure the voltage at the lock","Visually inspect the lock","Attempt to start the equipment, then return the start button/switch to OFF"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Verification of isolation is performed by attempting to operate the equipment (e.g., pressing the start button). This confirms the energy-isolating devices are effective. The start control must then be returned to the OFF position so the equipment cannot be started by the attempt itself.\n\n验证隔离通过尝试操作设备（如按下启动按钮）进行。这确认能量隔离装置有效。随后必须将启动控制恢复到OFF位置，以免验证尝试本身启动设备。","related":[{"n":"4.4","t":"上锁挂牌 (LOTO)"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Type C soil with a slope ratio requirement of 1.5:1 is being excavated. Which statement is correct?","options":["Benching is permitted in Type C soil","The slope must be 1.5 horizontal to 1 vertical (34°), and benching is NOT permitted in Type C","The slope must be 1.5 vertical to 1 horizontal","Type C soil needs no protection if the trench is dry"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Type C soil requires a 1.5:1 slope (1.5 horizontal to 1 vertical, ≈34°). Benching is NOT permitted in Type C soil — only sloping or shielding. Type A is 0.75:1, Type B is 1:1.\n\nC型土壤要求1.5:1放坡（水平1.5比垂直1，约34°）。C型土壤不允许台阶式开挖——只能放坡或防护。A型为0.75:1，B型为1:1。","related":[{"n":"4.6","t":"挖掘与沟槽"},{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘安全要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A worker's dose is 40% on the first day and 60% on the second day of a two-day exposure assessment. What is the average daily noise dose?","options":["50%","60%","100%","40%"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Average daily dose = (40% + 60%) / 2 = 50%. The 50% average equals the OSHA action level (85 dBA TWA). If the average dose were to exceed 100%, the worker would be overexposed on average. Averaging over multiple days is used when the standard deviation is small.\n\n平均日剂量 = (40% + 60%) / 2 = 50%。50%的平均值等于OSHA行动水平（85 dBA TWA）。如果平均剂量超过100%，则工人平均过度暴露。当标准差较小时，可对多日剂量取平均。","related":[{"n":"17.7","t":"剂量-效应关系与联合效应"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which characteristic distinguishes a spring-loaded safety relief valve from a rupture disc?","options":["The relief valve recloses below the set point; the disc must be replaced after bursting","The relief valve provides a zero-leakage seal during normal operation","The relief valve is used only upstream of a rupture disc in service","The relief valve responds faster to a pressure surge in the line"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A safety relief valve is spring-loaded and recloses automatically once pressure drops below the set point, so it can protect against repeated events. A rupture disc is non-reclosing and must be replaced after activation, but it responds faster and provides a zero-leakage seal. Discs are often installed upstream of a relief valve to isolate it from corrosive or fouling process fluid.\n\n安全泄压阀靠弹簧加载，压力回落到设定点以下会自动关闭，可重复保护。爆破片不可复位，爆破后必须更换，但响应更快且零泄漏。爆破片常装在泄压阀上游，使阀门与腐蚀性或易结垢的工艺介质隔离。","related":[{"n":"2.5","t":"机械完整性与泄压"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A trainer uses a real incident case study from the facility, then has learners practice the correct response in a simulated scenario. This approach aligns with which andragogical principle?","options":["Problem-centered orientation with immediate applicability","Extrinsic motivation only","Dependence on the instructor","Subject-centered learning"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Using real scenarios and hands-on practice reflects the \"Orientation to Learning\" principle — adults are problem-centered and want immediate applicability. The case study makes learning relevant; the simulation provides immediate application.\n\n使用真实场景和动手实践反映了\"学习取向\"原则——成人以问题为中心，希望立即应用。案例研究使学习相关；模拟提供即时应用。","related":[{"n":"19.7","t":"培训计划组成要素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Monthly recordable counts for eight months are 3, 4, 4, 6, 7, 9, 11, 14. What is the median?","options":["7.0","5.0","6.0","6.5"],"correct":3,"explanation":"With an even number of values the median is the average of the two middle values, here the fourth and fifth: (6 + 7) divided by 2 equals 6.5. The 6.0 and 7.0 values are the individual middle values rather than their average. The median is preferred over the mean when a few large values would distort the average.\n\n数值个数为偶数时，中位数是中间两个值（第4、第5个）的平均：（6 + 7）÷ 2 = 6.5。6.0 与 7.0 只是中间两个原始值而非其平均。当少数极端值会拉动均值时，中位数比均值更稳健。","related":[{"n":"6.6","t":"统计基础"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An employee requests exposure records that contain a trade-secret formulation. Under 29 CFR 1910.1020, the employer may:","options":["Provide the records only after the employee files a lawsuit","Delete the formulation from the record and provide nothing else","Require a signed confidentiality agreement but still disclose the exposure data","Refuse access because trade secrets are exempt from disclosure"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The access rule allows an employer to withhold specific trade-secret chemical identity only under limited conditions, and it may require a confidentiality agreement before releasing that portion; the exposure and medical information itself must still be provided. Refusing access outright, or stripping the record so it becomes useless, defeats the purpose of the standard. Employees and their designated representatives retain the right to the exposure data.\n\n查阅规则允许雇主仅在有限条件下对特定商业秘密的化学身份保密，并可在提供该部分前要求签署保密协议；暴露与医疗信息本身仍须提供。一概拒绝提供，或删减到记录失去用途，都背离了该标准的目的。员工及其指定代表仍保有获取暴露数据的权利。","related":[{"n":"8.9","t":"举报人保护"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under 29 CFR 1910.95, feasible engineering AND administrative controls are required when an employee's noise exposure equals or exceeds:","options":["90 dBA TWA (the PEL)","95 dBA TWA","100 dBA instantaneous","85 dBA TWA (the action level)"],"correct":0,"explanation":"At the PEL of 90 dBA (8-hour TWA), feasible engineering or administrative controls must be implemented. The 85 dBA action level triggers the Hearing Conservation Program (monitoring, audiometric testing, and available hearing protection), but controls are mandatory only at 90 dBA.\n\n在90 dBA（8小时TWA）的PEL水平，必须实施可行的工程或行政控制。85 dBA行动水平触发听力保护计划（监测、听力测试、提供听力防护），但只有达到90 dBA才强制要求控制措施。","related":[{"n":"1.5","t":"关键OSHA标准"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which safety culture maturity stage in the maturity model is characterized by \"safety is managed through systems and data collection\"?","options":["Pathological","Reactive","Calculative","Generative"],"correct":2,"explanation":"In the Safety Culture Maturity Model, the Calculative stage manages safety through systems, procedures, and data collection. The Generative stage is the highest, where safety is fully integrated and there is chronic unease about risk.\n\n在安全文化成熟度模型中，计算型阶段通过系统、程序和数据分析管理安全。生成型阶段是最高的，安全完全融入且对风险保持持续关注。","related":[{"n":"6.5","t":"安全文化测量"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"ISO 45001:2018 replaced which earlier standard as the international framework for OH&S management systems?","options":["OHSAS 18001","ISO 9001","ISO 14001","ANSI Z10.0"],"correct":0,"explanation":"ISO 45001:2018 replaced OHSAS 18001. It was the first ISO standard specifically for occupational health and safety management systems, published in March 2018. ANSI Z10.0 is the U.S. national standard; ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 cover quality and environment respectively.\n\nISO 45001:2018取代了OHSAS 18001。它是首个专门针对职业健康安全管理体系的ISO标准，于2018年3月发布。ANSI Z10.0是美国国家标准；ISO 9001和ISO 14001分别覆盖质量和环境。","related":[{"n":"5.1","t":"ISO 45001:2018"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Radon gas in a basement is a health concern primarily because:","options":["It causes hearing loss","It is highly flammable","Its alpha-emitting decay products can be inhaled and cause lung cancer","It displaces oxygen and causes asphyxiation"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Radon is a radioactive noble gas that seeps from soil into buildings. Its short-lived decay products (polonium-218, polonium-214) emit alpha particles; when inhaled, they deposit in the airways and are the second leading cause of lung cancer after smoking. Mitigation involves ventilation and sub-slab depressurization.\n\n氡是从土壤渗入建筑物的放射性惰性气体。其短寿命衰变产物（钋-218、钋-214）发射α粒子；吸入后在气道沉积，是仅次于吸烟的第二大肺癌原因。缓解措施包括通风和板下减压。","related":[{"n":"17.7","t":"剂量-效应关系与联合效应"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under OSHA's PPE standard (29 CFR 1910.132(d)), before relying on PPE as a control, the employer must:","options":["Conduct a written, certified hazard assessment of the workplace to determine if hazards require PPE","Purchase PPE from an approved vendor only","Obtain a waiver signed by each affected employee","Interview every employee about their PPE preferences"],"correct":0,"explanation":"1910.132(d) requires the employer to assess the workplace to determine if hazards are present (or likely to be present) that necessitate PPE, and to certify in writing that the assessment was performed. PPE is the last line of defense; a documented hazard assessment is the prerequisite.\n\n1910.132(d)要求雇主评估工作场所，确定是否存在（或可能存在的）需要PPE的危害，并书面认证评估已完成。PPE是最后一道防线；书面的危害评估是前提。","related":[{"n":"1.5","t":"关键OSHA标准"},{"n":"1.4","t":"行政控制与PPE"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"OSHA PSM (29 CFR 1910.119) requires Management of Change for:","options":["Only organizational restructuring","Changes that reduce production","All changes in every workplace","Changes to covered processes involving highly hazardous chemicals"],"correct":3,"explanation":"OSHA Process Safety Management (29 CFR 1910.119(l)) requires MOC for changes to processes covered by the standard — those involving specified highly hazardous chemicals. This is a regulatory driver of MOC in the process industries.\n\nOSHA工艺安全管理（29 CFR 1910.119(l)）要求对标准覆盖的工艺——涉及特定高度危险化学品的工艺——进行变更管理。这是流程行业MOC的法规驱动因素。","related":[{"n":"7.8","t":"变更管理 (MOC)"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which of the following is NOT a typical component of a risk register?","options":["Hazard description and risk rating","Existing controls and residual risk","Insurance premium calculations","Responsible person and review date"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A risk register tracks hazards, ratings (inherent/residual), controls, responsible persons, target dates, review dates, and status. Insurance premium calculations are a financial/underwriting function, not a risk register component.\n\n风险登记册跟踪危害、评级（固有/残余）、控制、负责人、目标日期、审查日期和状态。保险费计算是财务/承保职能，不是风险登记册组成部分。","related":[{"n":"9.8","t":"风险登记册"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A filter sample collects 0.45 mg of a contaminant over 960 L of air. What is the airborne concentration in mg/m³?","options":["0.047 mg/m³","0.0047 mg/m³","0.47 mg/m³","4.7 mg/m³"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Concentration = Mass / Volume = 0.45 mg / 960 L. Convert L to m³: 960 L = 0.96 m³. C = 0.45 / 0.96 = 0.47 mg/m³. Remember: 1 m³ = 1,000 L.\n\n浓度 = 质量 / 体积 = 0.45 mg / 960 L。将L换算为m³：960 L = 0.96 m³。C = 0.45 / 0.96 = 0.47 mg/m³。记住：1 m³ = 1,000 L。","related":[{"n":"16.4","t":"采样设备与方法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-16.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under PSM, Process Hazard Analyses (PHAs) must be updated and revalidated at least every:","options":["10 years","3 years","5 years","7 years"],"correct":2,"explanation":"PHAs must be updated and revalidated at least every 5 years (1910.119(e)(6)). Note the different frequencies: PHA revalidation = 5 years, refresher training = 3 years, compliance audits = 3 years. The CSP exam often tests these different time intervals, so it is important to keep them straight.\n\nPHA必须至少每5年更新和重新验证一次（1910.119(e)(6)）。注意不同的频率：PHA重新验证=5年，复训=3年，合规审核=3年。CSP考试经常考查这些不同的时间间隔，因此区分清楚非常重要。","related":[{"n":"2.2","t":"PSM的14个要素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Which of the following is a CORRECT example of a formative evaluation activity?","options":["An annual compliance audit","The final certification exam","A pilot test of new training materials with a small group before full rollout","A post-course knowledge test"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Formative evaluation occurs DURING development to improve the training — pilot testing, dry runs, and learner feedback loops. Final exams and certification tests are summative (judging the final result).\n\n形成性评估在开发过程中进行，以改进培训——试讲、预演和学员反馈循环。期末考试和认证测试是总结性的（判断最终结果）。","related":[{"n":"19.4","t":"持续改进模型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"To control ergonomic risk at a repetitive assembly task, a plant rotates each worker through four jobs every two hours. Which statement about this control is MOST accurate?","options":["It eliminates the ergonomic hazard because no worker performs one task all day","It is a PPE-level control and must be documented in the hazard assessment","It reduces the duration of exposure but the hazard at each station remains, so station redesign is still preferred","It removes the need for further controls because rotation is an engineering change"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Rotation redistributes exposure time among workers; it does not remove the awkward postures or forces at any station, and it can spread a musculoskeletal disorder across a larger group. It is an administrative control, so redesigning the workstation remains the higher-level fix. It is not PPE and it does not eliminate the hazard.\n\n轮岗只是在工人之间重新分配暴露时间，并未消除任一工位的别扭姿势或用力，甚至可能把肌肉骨骼疾患扩散到更多人。它属于行政控制，因此工位重新设计仍是更高层级的措施。它既不是 PPE，也不构成消除。","related":[{"n":"1.4","t":"行政控制与PPE"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A threat assessment team evaluates a report of an employee making threatening statements. Its approach should be:","options":["Ignoring reports until violence occurs","Immediate termination without investigation","Profiling based on demographic characteristics","Behavior-based assessment of the specific situation"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Threat assessment is behavior-based — evaluating the specific facts and behaviors, not profiling. The team assesses seriousness, develops intervention strategies, and manages the situation to prevent violence.\n\n威胁评估是基于行为的——评估具体事实和行为，而非画像分析。团队评估严重性、制定干预策略并管理情况以预防暴力。","related":[{"n":"13.9","t":"职场暴力"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Why should risk acceptance criteria be defined before the risk assessment begins?","options":["So ratings meet a consistent standard and decisions are defensible","To eliminate the need for monitoring, review, and reassessment","To guarantee that no residual risk remains after controls are applied","To replace consultation with the workforce during hazard identification"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Criteria set in advance tell the team what will count as acceptable, so ratings lead to consistent decisions and are not adjusted afterwards to fit a desired answer. They do not remove the need to monitor, cannot guarantee zero risk, and do not replace worker consultation. ISO 31000 treats risk criteria as an input to risk evaluation.\n\n事先设定标准，才能让评分对应一致的决策，避免事后为迎合结论而调整尺度。标准不能免除监控需要，也无法保证零风险，更不能替代与工人的协商。ISO 31000 将风险准则作为风险评估的输入。","related":[{"n":"9.2","t":"风险评估五步流程"},{"n":"9.6","t":"风险接受标准与ALARP"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In HAZOP, the guideword \"As Well As\" applied to a process parameter indicates:","options":["The opposite of the design intent","A quantitative increase in the parameter","A complete absence of the design intent","A qualitative increase — an additional component or impurity present"],"correct":3,"explanation":"\"As Well As\" indicates a qualitative increase — something extra is present in addition to what was intended (e.g., a contaminant in the flow, an impurity in the product). \"More\" indicates a quantitative increase.\n\n\"As Well As\"（以及）表示定性增加——除预期之外还有额外物质存在（如流体中的污染物、产品中的杂质）。\"More\"（更多）表示定量增加。","related":[{"n":"11.2","t":"引导词"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Participants rate a confined space course 4.8/5 for enjoyment and relevance, yet 45% fail the post-course written test. What is the MOST accurate interpretation?","options":["The test is invalid because learners enjoyed it","Level 1 reaction does not prove Level 2 learning","Repeat the course unchanged to raise scores","The course worked because reactions were high"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Level 1 measures satisfaction only; it is the weakest evidence of effectiveness and does not predict learning. A high reaction score with a high failure rate points to a Level 2 problem — objectives, content depth, practice time, or assessment alignment — and requires investigation. Invalidating the test or repeating the same course unchanged addresses nothing.\n\n第 1 级只衡量满意度，是有效性最弱的证据，不能预测学习效果。高满意度伴随高不及格率，说明第 2 级存在问题——目标、内容深度、练习时间或考核与内容不一致——需要调查。认定考试无效或原样重复课程都解决不了问题。","related":[{"n":"20.5","t":"柯氏四级评估"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A training plan includes: topics to be covered, target audience of 20 new hires, SMART objectives, a combination of classroom and hands-on instruction, a 3-day schedule, required equipment and instructor, and a written test plus skills demonstration. Which training plan component is MISSING from this description?","options":["Delivery method","Budget","Content outline","Scope"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Budget/financial resources are missing. While the plan covers scope (topics), audience (20 new hires), objectives (SMART), delivery method (classroom + hands-on), schedule (3-day), and evaluation (written test + skills demo), it does not address the budget or cost/resources component.\n\n预算/财务资源缺失了。虽然计划涵盖了范围（主题）、受众（20名新员工）、目标（SMART）、交付方式（课堂+实操）、时间安排（3天）和评估（笔试+技能演示），但没有涉及预算或成本/资源组成部分。","related":[{"n":"19.2","t":"ANSI/ASSP Z490.1标准"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Which set of RCRA subtitles correctly matches the waste or storage category it governs?","options":["Subtitle C for hazardous waste, Subtitle D for non-hazardous solid waste, Subtitle I for underground storage tanks","Subtitle C for solid waste, Subtitle D for hazardous waste, Subtitle I for underground tanks","Subtitle C for underground tanks, Subtitle D for hazardous waste, Subtitle I for solid waste","Subtitle C for hazardous waste, Subtitle D for underground tanks, Subtitle I for solid waste"],"correct":0,"explanation":"RCRA Subtitle C establishes the cradle-to-grave hazardous waste program, Subtitle D governs non-hazardous solid waste such as municipal landfills, and Subtitle I governs underground storage tanks. This structure explains why a hazardous waste facility permit is a Subtitle C permit while a used-oil or gasoline UST falls under Subtitle I. The other options swap the subtitles and would send a facility to the wrong regulatory program.\n\nRCRA C子章确立了危险废物“从摇篮到坟墓”的管理制度，D子章管辖城市垃圾填埋场等非危险固体废物，I子章管辖地下储罐。这一结构解释了为什么危险废物设施许可属于C子章许可，而废油或汽油地下储罐属于I子章。其他选项把子章对调，会把设施引向错误的监管体系。","related":[{"n":"14.5","t":"资源保护与回收法案"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d5.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A CSP is asked by an employer to sign a safety audit report that the CSP knows omits a serious noncompliance. According to the BCSP Code of Ethics, the CSP should:","options":["Sign it but note the omission verbally","Resign without comment","Sign it, since the employer is the client","Decline to sign and accurately report the finding, because honesty, objectivity, and the paramount duty to protect people override client wishes"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The BCSP Code of Ethics requires honesty and truthful public statements, and holds paramount the safety of people. Misrepresenting an audit finding is unethical. The CSP should report accurately even when it conflicts with client wishes.\n\nBCSP道德准则要求诚实和真实的公开声明，并将人员安全置于最高地位。歪曲审核发现是不道德的。即使与客户意愿冲突，CSP也应如实报告。","related":[{"n":"8.8","t":"道德与法律"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In the standard 5-step risk assessment process, after identifying hazards, the next step is to:","options":["Communicate findings to stakeholders","Evaluate risks against acceptance criteria","Monitor and review existing controls","Analyze risks by estimating likelihood and severity"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The 5-step process is: (1) Identify hazards, (2) Analyze risks (likelihood x severity), (3) Evaluate against criteria, (4) Monitor & review, (5) Communicate & consult. Analysis comes immediately after identification.\n\n五步流程为：(1) 识别危害，(2) 分析风险（可能性 x 严重性），(3) 对照标准评估，(4) 监控与审查，(5) 沟通与咨询。分析紧随识别之后。","related":[{"n":"9.2","t":"五步流程"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"What is the minimum clear opening width of an exit door under NFPA 101?","options":["28 inches","30 inches","32 inches","36 inches"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The minimum clear opening width of an exit door is typically 32 inches. This accommodates wheelchair passage and is a frequently tested baseline dimension.\n\n出口门的净开口宽度最小通常为32英寸。这考虑了轮椅通行，是常考的基准尺寸。","related":[{"n":"13.2","t":"疏散"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Management review must evaluate the continuing ___ of the OH&S management system. Which set of three criteria completes the requirement?","options":["efficiency, economy and elegance","suitability, adequacy and effectiveness","scope, severity and frequency","compliance, certification and profitability"],"correct":1,"explanation":"ISO 45001 Clause 9.3 and ANSI/ASSP Z10.0 both require top management to evaluate continuing suitability (still appropriate for the organization and its context), adequacy (sufficient in coverage and resources) and effectiveness (achieving intended results). Compliance and certification are separate conformity matters, while scope, severity and frequency are risk-assessment terms. These three words are the standard's own language and are frequently tested verbatim.\n\nISO 45001 第9.3条与 ANSI/ASSP Z10.0 都要求最高管理层评价体系的持续适宜性（是否仍适合组织及其环境）、充分性（范围与资源是否足够）和有效性（是否达成预期结果）。合规与认证属于另外的符合性问题，范围、严重度和频率则是风险评估术语。这三个词是标准原文表述，常被直接考查。","related":[{"n":"5.5","t":"管理评审"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An incident produced 18,000 dollars in direct costs. If indirect costs run about 4 times direct costs for this operation, what is the estimated total cost?","options":["22,500 dollars","4,500 dollars","90,000 dollars","72,000 dollars"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Indirect costs are 4 times 18,000, or 72,000, and total cost is direct plus indirect: 18,000 plus 72,000 equals 90,000 dollars. Equivalently, total equals 5 times direct. The 72,000 value is only the indirect portion, and 22,500 comes from dividing rather than multiplying.\n\n间接成本 = 4 × 18,000 = 72,000，总成本 = 直接 + 间接 = 18,000 + 72,000 = 90,000 美元，等价于直接成本的 5 倍。72,000 只是间接部分，22,500 则是用除法而非乘法得出的错误结果。","related":[{"n":"7.9","t":"事故成本"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A deluge system is credited as a mitigative barrier in a bow-tie, but it has not been flow-tested in four years and there is no test procedure. Which barrier effectiveness criterion is most clearly failing?","options":["Auditability","Adequacy","Independence","Cost-effectiveness"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Auditability asks whether barrier effectiveness can be verified by testing or inspection; no test procedure and a four-year gap fail that test. Adequacy asks whether the barrier addresses the specific consequence, and independence asks whether it shares a failure mode with other barriers. Cost is not one of the four criteria.\n\n可审核性考察屏障有效性是否可通过测试或检查验证；没有测试程序且四年未试验，显然不满足。充分性考察是否针对特定后果，独立性考察是否与其他屏障共因。成本不属于四项标准。","related":[{"n":"11.4","t":"蝴蝶结分析"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under 29 CFR 1910.212 (machine guarding), the primary method required to protect workers from point-of-operation hazards is:","options":["Engineering controls such as guards, barriers, and safety devices","Providing PPE and enforcing its use","Job rotation so workers spend less time at the machine","Safety training and warning signs"],"correct":0,"explanation":"1910.212 requires that one or more methods of machine guarding be provided to protect operators and others from point-of-operation, in-running nip points, rotating parts, and flying chips/sparks. Guards are engineering controls — the standard mandates them, not training or PPE.\n\n1910.212要求提供一种或多种机械防护方法，保护操作员和他人免受操作点、卷入点、旋转部件和飞屑/火花的伤害。防护装置是工程控制——标准强制要求防护装置，而非培训或PPE。","related":[{"n":"1.3","t":"工程控制"},{"n":"1.5","t":"关键OSHA标准"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In a risk register, \"residual risk\" is defined as:","options":["The risk that cannot be controlled under any circumstances","The risk transferred to an insurance provider","The risk level before any controls are applied","The risk level after existing controls are applied"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Residual (net) risk is what remains after existing controls. Inherent (gross) risk is the pre-control level. The residual risk is what the organization actually faces and must decide to accept or further reduce.\n\n残余（净）风险是现有控制后仍然存在的风险。固有（毛）风险是控制前的水平。残余风险是组织实际面临的风险，必须决定接受还是进一步降低。","related":[{"n":"9.8","t":"风险登记册"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Which of the following is the CORRECT pairing of a radiation unit with its quantity?","options":["Gray (Gy) — dose equivalent","Sievert (Sv) — absorbed dose","rem — dose equivalent","Becquerel — absorbed dose"],"correct":2,"explanation":"rem (and Sv) measure dose equivalent = absorbed dose × quality factor. Gray (Gy) and rad measure absorbed dose. Becquerel (Bq) and Curie measure activity (decay rate).\n\nrem（和Sv）测量剂量当量 = 吸收剂量 × 品质因子。Gray（Gy）和rad测量吸收剂量。Becquerel（Bq）和Curie测量活度（衰变率）。","related":[{"n":"17.4","t":"电离辐射"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A company has 3 lost-time injuries and 850,000 hours worked. What is the LTIFR (Lost Time Injury Frequency Rate)?","options":["0.71","3.53","1.41","7.06"],"correct":1,"explanation":"LTIFR = (lost time injuries × 1,000,000) / total hours worked = (3 × 1,000,000) / 850,000 = 3,000,000 / 850,000 = 3.53. Note that LTIFR uses a 1,000,000-hour base (unlike TRIR which uses 200,000). This is the international standard.\n\nLTIFR = (损失工时伤害数 × 1,000,000) / 总工时 = (3 × 1,000,000) / 850,000 = 3,000,000 / 850,000 = 3.53。注意LTIFR使用1,000,000工时的基数（不同于TRIR使用200,000）。这是国际标准。","related":[{"n":"6.2","t":"关键安全指标与公式"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A safety department was budgeted 250,000 dollars for the year and actually spent 287,500 dollars. What is the variance as a percentage of budget?","options":["15.0 percent over","37.5 percent over","12.5 percent under","13.0 percent over"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Variance equals actual minus budget, 287,500 minus 250,000 equals 37,500, divided by the budget of 250,000, giving 0.15 or 15 percent over budget. Dividing by actual spending instead would understate the variance at about 13 percent. The sign matters: an overrun of 15 percent must be explained in cost-per-unit or activity terms.\n\n差异 = 实际 − 预算 = 287,500 − 250,000 = 37,500，再除以预算 250,000 得 0.15，即超支 15%。若以实际支出作分母，会把差异低估为约 13%。方向很重要：15% 的超支必须用单位成本或活动量来解释。","related":[{"n":"8.1","t":"安全预算"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An organization hires an accredited certification body to evaluate its OH&S management system against ISO 45001 requirements. This is an example of what type of audit?","options":["Second-party (supplier) audit","Third-party (certification) audit","Regulatory compliance inspection","First-party (internal) audit"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A third-party audit is conducted by an independent, accredited certification body. It is independent of both the organization (unlike a first-party audit) and customers/suppliers (unlike a second-party audit). The purpose is typically certification or regulatory verification.\n\n三方审核由独立的认可认证机构实施。它既独立于组织（不同于一方审核），也独立于客户/供应商（不同于二方审核）。目的通常为认证或法规验证。","related":[{"n":"5.4","t":"审核类型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A worker is exposed to a chemical at the following concentrations during an 8-hour shift: 100 ppm for 3 hours, 160 ppm for 2 hours, and 0 ppm for the remaining 3 hours (breaks). What is the 8-hour TWA?","options":["77.5 ppm","100.0 ppm","76.3 ppm","86.7 ppm"],"correct":0,"explanation":"TWA = Σ(C × T) / 8 = (100×3 + 160×2 + 0×3) / 8 = (300 + 320 + 0) / 8 = 620/8 = 77.5 ppm.\n\n【中文】8 小时时间加权平均浓度（TWA）= Σ(浓度 × 时长) ÷ 8 = (100×3 + 160×2 + 0×3) ÷ 8 = 620 ÷ 8 = 77.5 ppm。注意休息时段的 0 ppm 也计入 8 小时总时长，分母固定为 8 而不是实际接触的 5 小时。","related":[{"n":"16.1","t":"AREC框架"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-16.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"What is the primary hazard of alpha-emitting radionuclides such as plutonium-239 in the workplace?","options":["Induced radioactivity in the body","External whole-body irradiation","Internal exposure if inhaled or ingested","Skin burns from contact"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Alpha emitters are primarily an INTERNAL hazard — they have a very short range but deposit large amounts of energy in tissue if inhaled or ingested (e.g., plutonium, radon progeny). External alpha exposure is negligible because the particles are stopped by the skin.\n\nα发射体主要是内部危害——它们的射程很短，但如果被吸入或摄入（如钚、氡子体），会在组织中沉积大量能量。外部α暴露可忽略，因为粒子被皮肤阻挡。","related":[{"n":"17.3","t":"听力保护计划HCP"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A lab technician knocks over a 1-quart bottle of 10 percent sulfuric acid. Two trained employees absorb it with a spill kit and neutralize the residue in about five minutes, with no injury and no release to the environment. How should this event be classified under 29 CFR 1910.120?","options":["An emergency response requiring full evacuation and National Response Center notification","An emergency response requiring a trained on-scene incident commander","An incidental release that does not require a HAZWOPER emergency response","An emergency response requiring a hazardous materials technician"],"correct":2,"explanation":"HAZWOPER excludes incidental releases of hazardous substances that can be absorbed, neutralized, or otherwise controlled at the time of release by employees in the immediate release area, or by maintenance personnel. A one-quart acid spill handled immediately with a spill kit is the textbook incidental release, so no emergency response organization, technician-level responder, or incident commander is required. Notification thresholds are also not met at this quantity and concentration.\n\nHAZWOPER不涵盖那种可由泄漏区域内员工或维修人员在泄漏当时吸收、中和或以其他方式控制的偶发泄漏。一夸脱酸液用泄漏处理包立即处理，正是教科书式的偶发泄漏，因此不需要启动应急响应组织、技术员级响应人员或事故指挥官。该数量与浓度也达不到通报阈值。","related":[{"n":"12.8","t":"危险废物作业与应急响应"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A safety net system used for fall protection may be installed no more than what maximum distance below the walking/working surface?","options":["30 feet","50 feet","15 feet","25 feet"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Safety nets must be installed as close as practicable under the walking/working surface but no more than 30 feet below it. They must extend outward from the edge per OSHA tables, and the maximum mesh size is 6 in × 6 in.\n\n安全网必须尽可能靠近行走/工作表面下方安装，但不得超过表面下方30英尺。必须按OSHA表格从边缘向外延伸，最大网孔尺寸为6英寸×6英寸。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"},{"n":"3.5","t":"附加坠落防护要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Under OSHA 1910.178 (Powered Industrial Trucks), operators must be evaluated and recertified at minimum every:","options":["2 years","3 years","5 years","1 year"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Forklift operators must complete formal instruction, practical training, and an evaluation. Recertification (refresher training + evaluation) is required every 3 years, or sooner after an accident, near-miss, unsafe observation, or assignment to different equipment.\n\n叉车操作员必须完成正式教学、实操培训和评估。每3年需要重新认证（复训+评估），或在事故、未遂事件、不安全观察或指派到不同设备后提前进行。","related":[{"n":"20.7","t":"OSHA培训要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"According to the 68-95-99.7 rule for a normal distribution, what percentage of observations fall within ±2 standard deviations of the mean?","options":["95%","99.7%","50%","68%"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The 68-95-99.7 rule states: 68% of data falls within ±1σ, 95% within ±2σ, and 99.7% within ±3σ. This is fundamental for understanding exposure data and control chart behavior.\n\n68-95-99.7法则：68%的数据落在±1σ内，95%在±2σ内，99.7%在±3σ内。这是理解暴露数据和控制图行为的基础。","related":[{"n":"6.6","t":"安全分析的统计基础"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"What is the primary focus of a Business Continuity Plan (BCP)?","options":["Evacuating employees from a building","Prosecuting offenders after an incident","Restoring IT systems from backups","Keeping the business running during and after a disruption"],"correct":3,"explanation":"BCP keeps critical BUSINESS functions operating through a disruption — via alternate sites, remote work, and alternate supply chains. Disaster Recovery restores IT specifically; EAP handles evacuation.\n\nBCP在中断期间保持关键业务职能运行——通过备用场所、远程办公和备用供应链。灾难恢复专门恢复IT；EAP处理疏散。","related":[{"n":"12.5","t":"BCP"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which of the following is a trigger for reviewing a risk assessment?","options":["The scheduled periodic review date","All of the above","An incident or near miss","A change in process or equipment"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Risk assessments should be reviewed on a scheduled basis AND triggered by events: incidents/near misses, process/equipment changes, new personnel or tasks, and discovered control failures. Risk assessments are living documents.\n\n风险评估应按计划定期审查，并因事件触发：事故/未遂、工艺/设备变更、新人员或任务、以及发现的控制失效。风险评估是动态文件。","related":[{"n":"9.9","t":"监控沟通"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A company integrates ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and ISO 45001 into a single management system. Which element is unique to the OH&S standard and cannot be satisfied by the quality system alone?","options":["Document control and record retention","Internal audit and management review","Competence and training records","Consultation and participation of workers"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Clause 5.4 of ISO 45001 requires consultation and participation of workers in OH&S decision-making, a requirement with no counterpart in ISO 9001. Document control, internal audit and management review are common Annex SL elements that can be integrated into one process serving all three standards. Integration works precisely because the shared elements are identical, while the discipline-specific requirements are kept distinct.\n\nISO 45001 第5.4条要求员工在职业健康安全决策中协商与参与，这在 ISO 9001 中没有对应要求。文件控制、内部审核和管理评审都是 Annex SL 的共同要素，可以通过同一套过程服务三项标准。整合之所以可行，正是因为共同要素文本一致，而各学科特有的要求仍保持独立。","related":[{"n":"5.7","t":"ISO 14000 整合体系"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"The HazCom label element \"P264 — Wash hands thoroughly after handling\" is an example of a:","options":["Hazard statement","Precautionary statement","Signal word","Product identifier"],"correct":1,"explanation":"P-statements (P-codes) are precautionary statements describing recommended measures to minimize or prevent adverse effects. H-statements (H-codes) describe the nature and degree of hazard. Signal words are \"Danger\"/\"Warning.\"\n\nP声明（P代码）是防范声明，描述为减少或防止不良影响而推荐的措施。H声明（H代码）描述危害的性质和程度。信号词是\"Danger\"/\"Warning\"。","related":[{"n":"14.8","t":"二次围堵容积计算"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-14.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A ventilation duct has a cross-sectional area of 2 square feet and carries air at 2,500 fpm. What is the volumetric flow rate?","options":["5,000 cfm","2,500 cfm","1,250 cfm","500 cfm"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Q = V × A = 2,500 fpm × 2 ft² = 5,000 cfm. This fundamental relationship (Q = VA) is used to calculate airflow in ducts, hoods, and stacks.\n\nQ = V × A = 2,500 fpm × 2 ft² = 5,000 cfm。这个基本关系式（Q = VA）用于计算管道、罩口和排气管中的气流量。","related":[{"n":"18.3","t":"人因工程风险因素与CTDs/MSDs"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-18.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A foundry that previously mixed its own molding sand now buys pre-blended sand delivered in sealed totes, so the dusty manual mixing step no longer exists anywhere on site. Which level of the hierarchy of controls has been achieved?","options":["Administrative control","Substitution","Engineering control","Elimination"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The mixing task and its dust exposure were removed from the site entirely, so the hazard no longer exists — that is elimination. Substitution still leaves a mixing step that uses a less hazardous material, and ventilation or a written procedure leaves the exposure in place. Elimination is the only level that removes risk completely.\n\n混砂作业及其粉尘暴露被整体从现场移除，危害已不复存在，属于消除。替代只是换用危害更小的材料、混砂工序仍在；通风或书面程序则让暴露继续存在。消除是唯一能完全移除风险的层级。","related":[{"n":"1.2","t":"消除与替代"},{"n":"1.1","t":"控制层级"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A 25-employee machine shop in a state with an approved consultation program wants public recognition and relief from programmed inspections but is not ready for VPP Star. Which program fits BEST?","options":["The OSHA Strategic Partnership Program for contractors","VPP Merit, because it is the entry level of the VPP track","SHARP, a small-employer program built on state consultation services","OSHA's Voluntary Protection Program Demonstration track"],"correct":2,"explanation":"SHARP recognizes small employers that use free on-site consultation and meet program criteria, and it carries an exemption from programmed inspections for the recognition period. VPP tracks, including Merit, require a comprehensive VPP-quality system and are a heavier lift for a 25-person shop. The Demonstration track is for worksites using alternative approaches, not a small-business entry point.\n\nSHARP 面向使用免费现场咨询并达到项目标准的小型雇主，并在认可期内免除计划性检查。包括 Merit 在内的 VPP 各轨道都要求达到 VPP 水准的完整体系，对 25 人的车间而言门槛过高。示范轨道面向采用替代方法的场所，不是小企业的入门通道。","related":[{"n":"8.7","t":"VPP 自愿保护"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"After an incident the damaged guard was replaced, the procedure was revised and an interlock was added. Which term describes replacing the guard alone?","options":["A correction","A corrective action","A management of change","A preventive action"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A correction fixes the immediate nonconformity, here the broken guard, while a corrective action addresses the cause so the problem does not recur, such as revising the procedure and adding the interlock. A preventive action addresses a potential problem that has not yet occurred. Management of change is the process used to control the modification itself.\n\n纠正（correction）消除眼前的不符合，此处即更换破损的防护罩；纠正措施针对原因，防止问题再次发生，例如修订程序并增设联锁。预防措施针对尚未发生的问题。变更管理则是控制改造本身的过程。","related":[{"n":"7.7","t":"纠正措施"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Excavated soil is being stockpiled beside a 7-foot-deep trench. Where must the spoil be placed?","options":["At least 2 feet back from the edge of the excavation","At least 6 inches back from the edge","Directly at the edge so it can be used for backfill quickly","On the opposite side of the trench from the access ladder only"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Spoil piles, equipment, and materials must be kept at least 2 feet from the edge of the excavation, because the surcharge load can trigger a collapse. The added weight and vibration are especially dangerous in Type C soil. Keeping the spoil close for convenience is a recognized contributing cause of trench fatalities.\n\n弃土、设备与材料必须距挖掘边缘至少 2 英尺，因为附加荷载可能诱发坍塌。在 C 型土中，附加重量与振动尤其危险。为图方便把弃土堆在坑边，是沟槽死亡事故的公认诱因之一。","related":[{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A company builds its safety budget by justifying every expense from scratch, without carrying over any amounts from the previous year. This approach is called:","options":["Zero-based budgeting","Performance-based budgeting","Incremental budgeting","Activity-based budgeting"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Zero-based budgeting (ZBB) starts from zero — every expense must be justified anew for the new period. Nothing is assumed or carried forward. This contrasts with incremental budgeting (starting from last year's budget and adjusting) and activity-based budgeting (building the budget around specific activities and their costs).\n\n零基预算(ZBB)从零开始——每项支出都必须为新期间重新论证。不假设或沿用任何东西。这与增量预算（从去年预算开始并调整）和作业基础预算（围绕特定活动及其成本构建预算）形成对比。","related":[{"n":"8.1","t":"预算"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"An engineer measures the maximum reach envelope of workers while they move tools along a bench. This measurement is an example of:","options":["Biomechanical load analysis","Cumulative trauma screening","Dynamic (functional) anthropometry","Static (structural) anthropometry"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Static or structural anthropometry uses fixed-position measurements such as standing height or arm length. Dynamic or functional anthropometry measures the body in motion, including reach envelopes and clearance during movement, which is what a moving task requires. Biomechanics deals with forces and moments, and CTD screening is a health-outcome tool, not a measurement of body dimensions.\n\n静态（结构）人体测量使用固定姿势的尺寸，如身高、臂长。动态（功能）人体测量则测量运动中的身体，包括可达范围和运动中的间隙，这正是移动性任务所需要的。生物力学关注力与力矩；CTD 筛查是健康结果工具，不是人体尺寸测量。","related":[{"n":"18.4","t":"人体测量学"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d6.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"According to OSHA, the OSHA 300 Log of injuries and illnesses must be retained for:","options":["1 year","5 years following the end of the calendar year","10 years","30 years"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The OSHA 300 Log must be retained for 5 years following the end of the calendar year that the log covers. This is distinct from exposure records (30 years) and medical records (employment + 30 years).\n\nOSHA 300日志必须在日志覆盖的日历年结束后保留5年。这不同于暴露记录（30年）和医疗记录（雇佣期+30年）。","related":[{"n":"6.3","t":"OSHA记录判定与记录保存"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"At a press brake the employer installs a light curtain that stops the ram when a hand enters the die area, plus an interlocked gate on the rear opening. A supervisor also adds a monthly refresher talk. How should the light curtain and gate be classified?","options":["PPE, because they protect the operator from the die area","Substitution, because the machine hazard is replaced","Engineering controls, because they stop the machine without worker action","Administrative controls, because a supervisor is responsible for them"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A light curtain and an interlocked gate are physical modifications that isolate the operator and act passively — the machine stops whether or not the worker is paying attention. The monthly talk changes worker behavior, so it is administrative. Substitution would require replacing the press or its process, and PPE protects only the individual.\n\n光幕与联锁门是物理改造，能被动隔离操作者——无论工人是否注意，机器都会停止，属工程控制。月度安全讲话改变的是工人行为，属行政控制。替代要求更换压力机或工艺，PPE 只保护个人。","related":[{"n":"1.3","t":"工程控制"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is an acceptable method of protecting workers in a trench 7 feet deep in Type B soil?","options":["Sloping at a 0.75:1 angle","A trench box (shielding)","No protection needed under 8 feet","Vertical walls with no support"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Type B soil requires sloping at 1:1 (not 0.75:1, which is Type A) OR benching, shoring, or shielding. A trench box is a valid protective system. Any excavation 5 feet or deeper needs a protective system; vertical walls with no support are never acceptable.\n\nB型土壤要求1:1放坡（不是0.75:1，那是A型）或台阶式、支撑、防护。沟槽箱是有效的防护系统。任何5英尺及以上的挖掘都需要防护系统；无支撑的垂直壁绝不可接受。","related":[{"n":"4.6","t":"挖掘与沟槽"},{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘安全要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A space must meet how many of the three defining criteria to be classified as a confined space under OSHA 1910.146?","options":["At least two of the three criteria","All three criteria","The criteria are evaluated on a case-by-case basis","Any one of the three criteria"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A space must meet ALL THREE criteria to be a confined space: (1) large enough to bodily enter, (2) has limited or restricted means of entry/exit, and (3) is not designed for continuous employee occupancy. Only one additional hazard characteristic is needed for the space to become a permit-required confined space.\n\n空间必须满足全部三项标准才算是密闭空间：(1) 足够大以身体进入，(2) 进出方式有限或受限，(3) 非为员工连续占用而设计。只需要一个额外的危害特征，空间就成为许可密闭空间。","related":[{"n":"4.1","t":"密闭空间"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"An underground storage tank is subject to RCRA Subtitle I requirements if what percentage of its volume (including piping) is underground?","options":["75%","25%","10%","50%"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A UST is defined as a tank and connected piping with at least 10% of its volume underground. Exemptions include farm/residential tanks ≤1,100 gal for non-commercial motor fuel and heating oil tanks used on the premises.\n\nUST定义为至少有10%体积（包括管道）位于地下的储罐。豁免包括农场/住宅≤1,100加仑的非商业机动燃料罐和现场供暖用油罐。","related":[{"n":"15.4","t":"清洁空气法与清洁水法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A plant completed its last PSM compliance audit 40 months ago and retained only that report. Which statement identifies the deficiencies?","options":["Only the interval is deficient; one report is sufficient","Neither is deficient, because the audit interval matches the PHA revalidation interval","Both are deficient: audits are required at least every three years and the two most recent reports must be kept","Only the retention is deficient; audits are required every five years"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Element 13 requires a compliance audit at least every three years, certified by a team that includes at least one person knowledgeable in the process, and retention of the two most recent audit reports. Forty months exceeds the three-year interval, and keeping only one report fails the retention requirement. The audit interval is independent of the five-year PHA cycle.\n\n要素 13 要求至少每三年做一次合规审核，由包含至少一名熟悉该工艺人员的团队认证，并保留最近两份审核报告。40 个月已超过三年周期，只保留一份报告也不符合保存要求。审核周期与五年一次的 PHA 复验周期相互独立。","related":[{"n":"2.2","t":"PSM十四要素"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A data center wants automatic sprinkler protection but cannot risk water discharge from a damaged head or a false trip. Which system requires both detection activation and individual head fusing before water enters the piping?","options":["Deluge","Wet pipe","Dry pipe","Pre-action"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A pre-action system holds water back at a pre-action valve and admits water only after a detection system operates, with the individual sprinkler head also needing to fuse before discharge. That two-event design protects water-sensitive spaces such as data centers, museums, and libraries. Wet pipe always contains water, dry pipe protects against freezing rather than accidental discharge, and deluge opens all heads at once.\n\n预作用系统由预作用阀挡水，只有在探测系统动作后才允许水进入管道，同时还需单个喷头感温元件动作才会喷水。这种“双事件”设计保护对水敏感的空间，如数据中心、博物馆和图书馆。湿式系统管道常年充水；干式系统主要用于防冻而非防误喷；雨淋系统则同时开启全部喷头。","related":[{"n":"13.6","t":"喷淋系统"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A 5,000-gallon vertical tank sits inside a rectangular containment berm measuring 30 ft by 20 ft. The facility designs containment to 110 percent of the largest tank volume. What effective berm depth is required, ignoring freeboard?","options":["1.1 ft","1.2 ft","2.4 ft","0.9 ft"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Required volume is 5,000 gallons times 1.10, or 5,500 gallons, which equals 5,500 divided by 7.48, or about 735 cubic feet. Dividing by the berm floor area of 30 times 20, or 600 square feet, gives about 1.2 feet of effective depth. The 1.1-foot value comes from using 100 percent of the tank volume, and 2.4 feet results from arithmetic or conversion errors.\n\n所需容积为5,000加仑 × 1.10 = 5,500加仑，换算为5,500 ÷ 7.48 ≈ 735立方英尺。再除以围堤底面积30 × 20 = 600平方英尺，得到约1.2英尺的有效深度。1.1英尺来自按储罐容积的100%计算，2.4英尺则源于计算或单位换算错误。","related":[{"n":"14.8","t":"二次围堵容积"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d5.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following best describes the \"good Samaritan\" rescuer effect in confined space incidents?","options":["Rescuers are always safe because they act quickly","Untrained coworkers who enter a space to rescue a victim become victims themselves, multiplying fatalities","The attendant should always enter first to rescue","Retrieval systems are never effective"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The \"good Samaritan\" effect refers to untrained coworkers entering a confined space to rescue a fallen worker and themselves being overcome by the same atmosphere, causing multiple-fatality incidents. The correct response is non-entry rescue and summoning trained rescuers.\n\n\"好撒玛利亚人\"效应指未受训的同事进入密闭空间救援倒下工人，自己被同样的气氛击倒，造成多人死亡。正确的做法是非进入救援并召唤受训救援人员。","related":[{"n":"4.3","t":"进入程序与救援"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A quarterly safety review presents three measures: near-miss reports per 100 workers, audit findings closed on time, and TRIR. Which of these are leading indicators?","options":["TRIR also qualifies, because it reflects the current year of experience","Near-miss reports per 100 workers and on-time closure of audit findings only","Near-miss reports and TRIR only","On-time closure of audit findings and TRIR only"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Near-miss reporting and timely closure of audit findings measure preventive activity and control strength before harm occurs, so both are leading. TRIR counts injuries that have already happened, which makes it lagging. Combining both types is good practice, but the classification of each measure does not change with how it is presented.\n\n未遂事件报告率和审核发现按期关闭率衡量的是伤害发生前的预防活动与控制强度，属于领先指标。TRIR 统计的是已经发生的伤害，属于滞后指标。两类指标结合使用是好做法，但单个指标的属性不因呈现方式而改变。","related":[{"n":"6.1","t":"领先与滞后指标"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A trench is 7 feet deep. A portable ladder will be used for egress. What minimum ladder length above the trench floor satisfies the requirement?","options":["8 feet","9 feet","10 feet","7 feet"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Ladders used for access must extend at least 3 feet above the landing, so a 7-foot-deep trench needs a ladder reaching at least 10 feet above the trench floor. A ladder flush with the top gives no handhold and is a common citation. Trenches over 4 feet deep also require egress within 25 feet of lateral travel.\n\n用于进出的梯子必须伸出落脚面至少 3 英尺，因此 7 英尺深的沟槽需要梯子高出沟底至少 10 英尺。梯子与坑口齐平则没有抓手，是常见的违规项。深度超过 4 英尺的沟槽还要求横向 25 英尺内可进出。","related":[{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘要求"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Which of the following materials provides the BEST shielding against alpha particles?","options":["A sheet of lead","A sheet of paper or dead skin layer","6 inches of concrete","A thin layer of water"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Alpha particles are the least penetrating — they are stopped by a sheet of paper or the dead outer layer of skin. Their hazard is primarily INTERNAL (inhalation or ingestion), not external. Lead is needed for gamma; plastic/aluminum for beta; water/paraffin for neutrons.\n\nα粒子穿透力最弱——被一张纸或皮肤死皮外层即可阻挡。其危害主要是内部（吸入或摄入），而非外部。铅用于γ；塑料/铝用于β；水/石蜡用于中子。","related":[{"n":"17.2","t":"噪声计算"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A worker using an impact wrench is measured at a peak sound pressure of 148 dB. The 8-hour TWA is only 84 dBA. What is the correct interpretation?","options":["No action is needed because the 8-hour TWA is below 85 dBA","The peak limit applies only to continuous noise, not impact tools","The reading is invalid because peak levels are measured in dBA","The 140 dB peak limit is exceeded, so feasible controls and hearing protection are required"],"correct":3,"explanation":"OSHA 1910.95 separately limits impulsive noise to a 140 dB peak, independent of the 8-hour TWA. A 148 dB peak is an overexposure even though the TWA is only 84 dBA, and it carries a risk of acoustic trauma. The employer must use feasible engineering and administrative controls and provide hearing protection; peak levels are indeed expressed in dB rather than dBA.\n\nOSHA 1910.95 对脉冲噪声单独规定 140 dB 峰值上限，与 8 小时 TWA 无关。即使 TWA 只有 84 dBA，148 dB 的峰值仍属过度暴露，存在声创伤风险。雇主必须采用可行的工程和行政控制并提供听力防护；峰值声压确实以 dB（而非 dBA）表示。","related":[{"n":"17.1","t":"噪声监管标准"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d6.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Which of the following is NOT one of the six criteria air pollutants regulated under the Clean Air Act?","options":["Methane (CH₄)","Lead (Pb)","Carbon monoxide (CO)","Nitrogen dioxide (NO₂)"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The six criteria pollutants are: CO, Pb, NO₂, O₃, PM (PM₁₀ and PM₂.₅), and SO₂. Methane (CH₄) is a greenhouse gas but is not one of the six criteria pollutants — although GHGs are regulated under the CAA following Massachusetts v. EPA (2007).\n\n六种标准污染物为：CO、Pb、NO₂、O₃、PM（PM₁₀和PM₂.₅）和SO₂。甲烷（CH₄）是温室气体，但不是六种标准污染物之一——尽管在马萨诸塞州诉EPA案（2007年）之后，温室气体也受CAA监管。","related":[{"n":"15.1","t":"RCRA废物产生者分类"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Chlorine gas transported by rail falls under which DOT hazard class?","options":["Class 8 (Corrosives)","Class 2 (Gases)","Class 3 (Flammable Liquids)","Class 6 (Toxic)"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Chlorine is a gas (Class 2), specifically Division 2.3 Toxic Gas — it has a white placard with a skull symbol. Its toxic nature affects the division within Class 2, but the class is 2 (Gases).\n\n氯是气体（第2类），具体为2.3项有毒气体——白色标牌带骷髅符号。其毒性影响第2类内的项别，但类别是2（气体）。","related":[{"n":"13.7","t":"DOT"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In Event Tree Analysis (ETA), the analysis:","options":["Analyzes only component failures","Calculates insurance premiums","Starts with the top event and works backward","Starts with an initiating event and works forward through safeguards to outcomes"],"correct":3,"explanation":"ETA is inductive: it starts from an initiating event and branches forward through each safeguard (success/failure) to all possible outcomes. It evaluates safeguard effectiveness and consequences.\n\nETA是归纳法：从初始事件开始，向前通过每个防护（成功/失败）分支到所有可能结果。它评估防护有效性和后果。","related":[{"n":"10.6","t":"ETA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Two independent basic events with probabilities 0.05 and 0.02 feed an OR gate. What is the exact output probability?","options":["0.069","0.07","0.001","0.049"],"correct":0,"explanation":"P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A)P(B) = 0.05 + 0.02 - 0.001 = 0.069. The subtracted term removes the double-counted case where both events occur. 0.07 is the rare-event approximation, acceptable when probabilities are very small but slightly high here.\n\nP(A 或 B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A)P(B) = 0.05 + 0.02 − 0.001 = 0.069。减去交集项，避免重复计算两者同时发生。0.07 是罕见事件近似值，概率极小时可用，此处略偏高。","related":[{"n":"10.4","t":"故障树分析FTA"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A plant removes a fixed guard from a conveyor transfer point because all operators have been trained to keep clear. Which principle does this decision violate?","options":["Machine guarding is only required for machines built after 1972","Guards may be removed whenever production requires it","Training must be repeated every year to remain valid","Training is administrative and cannot replace a feasible engineering control"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Training relies on behavior and ranks below a feasible guard, so removing the guard trades a passive engineering control for an administrative one. Under 29 CFR 1910.212, guarding must be provided where the point of operation exposes an employee to injury. Production convenience and training status do not justify removal.\n\n培训依赖人的行为，其层级低于可行的防护装置；拆掉防护罩等于用行政控制替换被动工程控制。依据 29 CFR 1910.212，操作点使员工面临伤害风险时必须设防。生产便利与培训状态都不能成为拆除防护罩的理由。","related":[{"n":"1.1","t":"控制层级"},{"n":"1.3","t":"工程控制"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"An FMEA of a cooling system with two pumps finds that no single component failure has a severe effect, so the team concludes overall risk is low. What important limitation applies to this conclusion?","options":["FMEA requires numerical probabilities for every basic event","FMEA applies only to software systems and controls","FMEA cannot assign severity ratings to failure modes","FMEA reviews modes one at a time, so it can miss combinations"],"correct":3,"explanation":"FMEA is a bottom-up, single-failure technique: each mode is judged on its own effect, so two independent failures occurring together, or one cause defeating both pumps, may not surface. A fault tree built around the loss-of-cooling top event would expose those combinations and minimal cut sets. FMEA does assign severity, and it does not require probabilities.\n\nFMEA 是自下而上的单点失效方法，逐条评估失效模式的影响，因此两个失效同时发生、或一个共因同时打掉两台泵的情形可能被漏掉。以失去冷却为顶事件建立故障树可以揭示这些组合与最小割集。FMEA 会评严重性，也不要求概率数据。","related":[{"n":"10.1","t":"失效模式与影响分析"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An employer transfers a worker to a less desirable shift after the worker reports a serious hazard to OSHA. Under the OSH Act, this action is:","options":["Lawful because the worker did not file a written complaint","Unlawful retaliation against protected activity under Section 11(c)","A matter for the workers' compensation system rather than OSHA","Lawful if the transfer is described as a business necessity"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Section 11(c) prohibits retaliation against employees for exercising rights such as filing a complaint, participating in an inspection or reporting an injury. A transfer, demotion or schedule change that punishes protected activity is retaliation regardless of the business justification offered. The worker must generally file a complaint with OSHA within 30 days of the retaliatory action.\n\n《职业安全健康法》第 11(c) 条禁止因员工行使投诉、参与检查或报告伤害等权利而实施报复。调岗、降职或改动班次只要是对受保护活动的惩罚，就构成报复，无论给出何种业务理由。员工通常须在报复行为发生后 30 天内向 OSHA 投诉。","related":[{"n":"8.9","t":"举报人保护"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which statement about FTA AND gates versus OR gates is correct?","options":["AND and OR gates produce the same result","AND gates increase probability because more events are involved","OR gates reduce probability because they exclude events","AND gates reduce probability (all events must occur) while OR gates increase it (any event suffices)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"AND gates multiply probabilities, so the output is smaller (all inputs must occur). OR gates add (minus intersection), so the output is larger (any input suffices). This mirrors redundancy logic: parallel (AND) = reliable; series (OR) = fragile.\n\n与门相乘概率，输出更小（所有输入都必须发生）。或门相加（减交集），输出更大（任一输入即可）。这对应冗余逻辑：并联（与）=可靠；串联（或）=脆弱。","related":[{"n":"10.4","t":"FTA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A fault tree has minimal cut sets {A, B} and {C}, with P(A)=0.02, P(B)=0.03 and P(C)=0.004. Using the rare-event approximation, what is the top event probability?","options":["0.0052","0.0006","0.004","0.0046"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Each minimal cut set probability is the product of its events: {A, B} = 0.02 x 0.03 = 0.0006, and {C} = 0.004. The rare-event approximation sums them: 0.004 + 0.0006 = 0.0046. The single-event cut set {C} dominates, so improving C gives the largest reduction.\n\n每个最小割集的概率为其事件概率之积：{A, B} = 0.02 × 0.03 = 0.0006，{C} = 0.004。罕见事件近似将二者相加：0.004 + 0.0006 = 0.0046。单事件割集 {C} 占主导，因此改进 C 收益最大。","related":[{"n":"10.5","t":"组合故障树计算"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Using the OSHA 5-dB exchange rate, a worker is exposed to 95 dBA. What is the maximum allowable exposure duration before exceeding the PEL?","options":["8 hours","4 hours","2 hours","1 hour"],"correct":1,"explanation":"OSHA uses a 5-dB exchange rate: each 5 dBA increase halves the allowed time. 90 dBA → 8 hours; 95 dBA → 4 hours; 100 dBA → 2 hours; 105 dBA → 1 hour. A worker at 95 dBA may be exposed for only 4 hours before the dose exceeds 100%.\n\nOSHA采用5-dB交换率：每增加5 dBA，允许时间减半。90 dBA→8小时；95 dBA→4小时；100 dBA→2小时；105 dBA→1小时。工人在95 dBA下仅可暴露4小时，否则剂量超过100%。","related":[{"n":"1.5","t":"关键OSHA标准"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"The three components of a \"means of egress\" under NFPA 101 are, in order:","options":["Exit, exit access, exit discharge","Exit access, exit, exit discharge","Exit discharge, exit, exit access","Corridor, stairwell, doorway"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The means of egress is: (1) exit ACCESS (path leading TO the exit), (2) the EXIT itself (protected portion like an enclosed stairwell), and (3) exit DISCHARGE (path from the exit to a public way). This order is frequently tested.\n\n疏散通道是：(1) 出口<em>通道</em>（通向出口的路径），(2) <em>出口</em>本身（如封闭楼梯间等保护部分），(3) <em>出口疏散点</em>（从出口到公共道路的路径）。此顺序常被测试。","related":[{"n":"13.2","t":"疏散"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"The \"experience rating\" of an insurance premium means the premium is adjusted based on:","options":["The age of the insurance company","The insured organization's loss history","The number of employees only","The weather in the region"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Experience rating adjusts premiums based on the organization's actual loss history — good safety performance lowers premiums; poor performance raises them. This links insurance cost to safety management effectiveness.\n\n经验费率根据组织的实际损失历史调整保费——良好的安全绩效降低保费；不良绩效提高保费。这将保险成本与安全管理有效性联系起来。","related":[{"n":"11.8","t":"保险概念"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Which of the following best describes the relationship between work, force, and distance?","options":["Work = Force × Distance × cos(θ)","Work = Force / Distance","Work = Power × Distance","Work = mass × velocity"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Work = Force × Distance × cos(θ), where θ is the angle between force and displacement. Power = Work / Time. This physics foundation applies to conveyor design, hoist sizing, and understanding muscular work in ergonomics.\n\n功 = 力 × 距离 × cos(θ)，其中θ是力与位移的夹角。功率 = 功 / 时间。这一物理基础适用于输送机设计、葫芦选型以及理解人因工程中的肌肉做功。","related":[{"n":"18.5","t":"化学封存量与物理核心概念"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-18.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A sampling pump is calibrated at 2.0 L/min and runs for 480 minutes on a high-flow particulate sample. What is the total sample volume?","options":["480 L","960 L","1,440 L","2,400 L"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Sample volume = Flow rate × Time = 2.0 L/min × 480 min = 960 L. This volume would then be used to convert the filter mass to an airborne concentration in mg/m³.\n\n采样体积 = 流速 × 时间 = 2.0 L/min × 480分钟 = 960 L。该体积随后用于将滤膜质量转换为空气中的浓度（mg/m³）。","related":[{"n":"16.2","t":"工业卫生危害因素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-16.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"In the context of incident investigation, a \"near miss\" that involved no injury or illness is:","options":["OSHA-recordable because it indicates a hazard","Always reported to OSHA within 24 hours","Not OSHA-recordable, but valuable for proactive corrective action","OSHA-recordable only if reported by a supervisor"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Near-misses are not OSHA-recordable because no injury or illness occurred — recordability requires an injury/illness meeting the recording criteria. However, near-misses are valuable learning opportunities and should be investigated for proactive corrective action.\n\n未遂事件不属于OSHA可记录范围，因为未发生伤害或疾病——可记录性要求发生符合记录标准的伤害/疾病。然而，未遂事件是宝贵的学习机会，应进行调查以采取主动纠正措施。","related":[{"n":"7.6","t":"未遂事件报告与海因里希三角"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is a required component of a Personal Fall Arrest System (PFAS)?","options":["Positioning belt, rope grab, and carabiner","Body belt, lanyard, and guardrail","Full-body harness, connector, and anchorage","Safety net, harness, and warning line"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A PFAS consists of three key components: (A) anchorage — a secure point of attachment, (B) full-body harness — body belts are PROHIBITED for fall arrest (they may only be used for positioning), and (C) connector — typically a lanyard or self-retracting lifeline (SRL) connecting the harness to the anchorage. Safety nets and warning lines are separate fall protection systems, not part of a PFAS.\n\nPFAS由三个关键组件组成：(A) 锚固点——安全的附着点，(B) 全身式安全带——防坠保护禁止使用身体腰带（仅可用于定位），(C) 连接器——通常为将安全带连接到锚固点的系索或自缩式救生索(SRL)。安全网和警示线是独立的坠落防护系统，不是PFAS的一部分。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A manufacturer has just finished writing a new all-hazards emergency plan and wants to validate the plan's logic and clarify roles before spending money on field operations. Which exercise type should be conducted FIRST?","options":["A tabletop exercise with the key players walking through a scenario","A full-scale exercise with role players and mutual-aid agencies","A functional exercise that deploys all response equipment","No exercise, because the plan cannot be tested until an actual emergency occurs"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Exercises are built as a progressive sequence: discussion-based tabletop exercises first test plan logic, roles, and decision points at low cost, then functional exercises test specific functions, and only then do full-scale exercises deploy people and equipment. Jumping straight to a full-scale exercise wastes resources on a plan whose gaps have not yet been found. A plan can and must be tested through exercises rather than waiting for a real event.\n\n演练应循序渐进：先做基于讨论的桌面演练，以低成本检验计划逻辑、角色与决策点；再做功能演练检验特定功能；最后才做全面演练、实际部署人员与设备。直接上全面演练会把资源浪费在尚未发现缺陷的计划上。计划必须通过演练来检验，而不是等真实事件发生。","related":[{"n":"12.6","t":"应急演练"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"An EPA RMP Program 3 facility must submit which of the following to EPA that is NOT required under OSHA PSM?","options":["Operating procedures","A Risk Management Plan including off-site consequence analysis (worst-case and alternative release scenarios)","Employee training records","A Process Hazard Analysis"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The unique RMP requirements are the off-site consequence analysis (worst-case release scenario and alternative release scenario), the registration submission to EPA, and the public/community disclosure of the RMP. Operating procedures, training, and PHA overlap with PSM.\n\nRMP独有的要求是厂外后果分析（最坏泄漏情景和替代泄漏情景）、向EPA的注册提交以及RMP的公众/社区披露。操作规程、培训和PHA与PSM重叠。","related":[{"n":"2.7","t":"与EPA风险管理计划的关系"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which HAZOP worksheet column lists the safety systems that exist to address a deviation?","options":["Causes","Safeguards","Recommendations","Guideword"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The Safeguards column records existing protection (alarms, relief valves, procedures, interlocks) that address the deviation. Recommendations record NEW actions; Causes records why the deviation happens.\n\n防护列记录现有保护（报警、泄压阀、程序、联锁）以应对偏差。建议记录新的行动；原因记录偏差为何发生。","related":[{"n":"11.3","t":"团队工作表"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Two sites report noise exposure data. Site A has a mean of 20 dBA above baseline with a standard deviation of 4; Site B has a mean of 50 with a standard deviation of 8. What is Site A's coefficient of variation?","options":["25 percent","80 percent","5 percent","20 percent"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The coefficient of variation equals the standard deviation divided by the mean, times 100: 4 divided by 20 equals 0.20, or 20 percent. Site B's coefficient is 8 divided by 50, or 16 percent, so Site A is actually more variable relative to its mean despite the smaller absolute standard deviation. This is why CV is used to compare variability across groups with different means.\n\n变异系数 = 标准差 ÷ 均值 × 100 = 4 ÷ 20 = 20%。B 场地的变异系数为 8 ÷ 50 = 16%，所以尽管 A 的绝对标准差更小，其相对离散程度反而更高。这正是用变异系数比较均值不同的群体变异性的原因。","related":[{"n":"6.6","t":"统计基础"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A forklift operator must be retrained (in addition to every 3 years) when:","options":["The warehouse changes its lighting","The forklift is purchased used","The operator asks for a raise","The operator is involved in an accident or near-miss, or is observed operating unsafely"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Retraining is required after an accident or near-miss, after observation of unsafe operation, or when assigned a different type of truck. Refresher training/evaluation is required at least every 3 years.\n\n在事故或未遂事件后、观察到不安全操作后，或分配到不同类型的叉车时，需要复训。至少每3年需要复训/评估。","related":[{"n":"4.8","t":"物料搬运与储存"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"What is the FIRST step in the Analysis phase of ADDIE?","options":["Writing the final exam","Conducting the needs assessment (organizational, task, person)","Selecting the delivery platform","Scheduling the training date"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The Analysis phase begins with the needs assessment — the three levels (organizational, task, person) — plus learner analysis and context analysis. Only after understanding the need can design (objectives, strategies) begin.\n\n分析阶段从需求评估开始——三个层面（组织、任务、人员）——加上学习者分析和情境分析。只有在理解需求之后，才能开始设计（目标、策略）。","related":[{"n":"19.8","t":"形成性评估与总结性评估"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"When conducting an incident investigation, which is the BEST approach to witness interviews?","options":["Interview witnesses separately, promptly, using open-ended questions","Interview only the injured worker","Delay interviews until the investigation is nearly complete","Interview witnesses together to compare accounts"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Best practice: interview separately (avoid groupthink), promptly (memory fades and witnesses talk), and with open-ended questions (elicit full narratives). Group interviews and delays contaminate or lose evidence.\n\n最佳实践：单独访谈（避免从众）、及时访谈（记忆消退且证人会相互交流）、使用开放式问题（引出完整叙述）。集体访谈和延迟会污染或丢失证据。","related":[{"n":"7.4","t":"证人访谈技巧"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which level of the Hierarchy of Controls is the ONLY one that completely removes risk so the hazard no longer exists?","options":["Engineering controls","Administrative controls","Substitution","Elimination"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Elimination is the only level that physically removes the hazard so it no longer exists, completely eliminating risk. All other levels either reduce the hazard (substitution), isolate the worker from it (engineering), change behavior around it (administrative), or protect only the individual (PPE) — but the hazard itself remains.\n\n消除是唯一通过物理移除危害使其不复存在、从而完全消除风险的层级。其他所有层级要么降低危害（替代）、隔离工人（工程控制）、改变行为（行政控制）或仅保护个人（PPE）——但危害本身仍然存在。","related":[{"n":"1.2","t":"消除与替代"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which ICS section is responsible for providing facilities, transportation, supplies, and equipment?","options":["Logistics","Command","Operations","Planning"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Logistics provides facilities, transportation, supplies, equipment, food, medical, and communications — the support backbone of the incident. Operations uses the resources; Planning plans; Finance tracks costs.\n\n后勤提供设施、运输、物资、设备、食品、医疗和通信——事故的支持骨干。行动使用资源；规划做计划；财务跟踪成本。","related":[{"n":"12.4","t":"ICS"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Halfway through a two-day course, the trainer notices that learners cannot interpret a permit form. She adds a worked example and a short practice exercise before moving to the next module. This is an example of:","options":["Formative evaluation","Kirkpatrick Level 4 evaluation","Phillips ROI analysis","Summative evaluation"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Formative evaluation happens during development and delivery to improve the training while it is still running — mid-course checks, learner feedback, and adjustments such as adding a worked example. Summative evaluation judges the finished program through a final exam or certification. Level 4 and ROI measure organizational results and financial return, which come much later.\n\n形成性评估发生在开发与交付过程中，目的是在培训仍在进行时加以改进——课程中检查、学员反馈，以及补充示例等调整。总结性评估通过期末考试或认证来评判已完成的项目。第 4 级和 ROI 衡量组织结果与财务回报，时间上要晚得多。","related":[{"n":"19.8","t":"形成性与总结性评估"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Risk is best defined as:","options":["The consequence of a failure event","The potential for an unwanted event","The combination of the probability of harm and its severity","Any condition that could cause injury"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Risk = probability (likelihood) × severity (consequence). It requires BOTH a hazard and exposure. A hazard is the potential; risk quantifies the potential in terms of likelihood and consequence.\n\n风险 = 概率（可能性）× 严重性（后果）。它需要危害和暴露同时存在。危害是潜力；风险以可能性和后果来量化该潜力。","related":[{"n":"9.1","t":"危害vs风险"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following is a LEADING indicator of safety performance?","options":["Number of near-miss reports submitted this month","Lost workday cases from the previous quarter","Workers' compensation costs for the fiscal year","Total Recordable Incident Rate (TRIR)"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The number of near-miss reports submitted is a leading indicator — it is proactive and predictive, measuring an activity that should improve future safety outcomes. TRIR, lost workday cases, and workers' compensation costs are all lagging indicators, measuring past outcomes.\n\n提交的未遂事件报告数量是领先指标——它是主动性和预测性的，测量的是应能改善未来安全结果的活动。TRIR、损失工作日案例和工伤保险费用都是滞后指标，测量的是过去的结果。","related":[{"n":"6.1","t":"领先指标与滞后指标"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A corporate safety scorecard tracks TRIR, DART and severity rate only. What is the principal weakness of this scorecard?","options":["It is all lagging, so it reports harm only after the fact","It cannot be compared across business units or years","It uses too many different measures for managers to follow","It mixes incidence and severity measures in a single view"],"correct":0,"explanation":"All three measures count outcomes that have already occurred, so the scorecard cannot show whether controls are weakening until injuries appear. Leading indicators such as audit closure, training currency and near-miss trends provide that earlier signal. The measures are in fact comparable across units, and combining incidence with severity is a strength rather than the weakness.\n\n这三项指标统计的都是已经发生的结果，因此在控制措施弱化时无法提前预警，只能等伤害出现后才知道。审核关闭率、培训时效和未遂趋势等领先指标可以提供更早的信号。这三项指标其实可以跨单位比较，而把发生率与严重度放在同一视图恰恰是优点。","related":[{"n":"6.1","t":"领先与滞后指标"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A worker dies from a work-related incident. According to OSHA, the employer must report this fatality to OSHA within:","options":["8 hours","24 hours","7 calendar days","30 days"],"correct":0,"explanation":"OSHA requires reporting of any work-related fatality within 8 hours. In-patient hospitalizations, amputations, and loss of an eye must be reported within 24 hours. Recording on the 300 Log (within 7 days) is a separate, slower discipline.\n\nOSHA要求任何与工作相关的死亡必须在8小时内报告。住院治疗、截肢和眼球丧失必须在24小时内报告。在300日志上记录（7天内）是另一项更慢的纪律。","related":[{"n":"6.3","t":"OSHA记录判定与记录保存"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In Event Tree Analysis (ETA), after an initiating event with probability 0.05, two independent safeguards succeed with probabilities 0.9 and 0.8 respectively. What is the probability that BOTH safeguards fail?","options":["0.05 x 0.1 x 0.2 = 0.001","0.9 x 0.8 = 0.72","0.05 x (0.1 + 0.2) = 0.015","0.05 x 0.9 x 0.8 = 0.036"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Both fail path: initiating event x P(S1 fails) x P(S2 fails) = 0.05 x 0.1 x 0.2 = 0.001. This is the worst-case scenario with the lowest probability.\n\n两者都失败路径：初始事件 x P(防护1失败) x P(防护2失败) = 0.05 x 0.1 x 0.2 = 0.001。这是概率最低的最坏情景。","related":[{"n":"10.6","t":"ETA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Which of the following is the MOST appropriate engineering control for reducing noise exposure at the source?","options":["Enclosing the noisy machine in a soundproof enclosure","Posting hearing protection required signs","Rotating workers through the noisy area","Providing double hearing protection"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Enclosing the noisy machine (engineering control at the source) is preferred over administrative controls (job rotation, signage) and PPE (hearing protection). The hierarchy of controls applies to noise just as to chemical hazards.\n\n将噪声机器封闭在隔音罩内（源头工程控制）优先于行政控制（岗位轮换、标志）和PPE（听力保护）。控制层级同样适用于噪声和化学危害。","related":[{"n":"17.7","t":"剂量-效应关系与联合效应"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A worker is treated for a minor cut with a non-prescription bandage and antiseptic. According to OSHA recordkeeping, this case is:","options":["Recordable because any treatment is medical treatment","Recordable only if the worker missed time","Recordable as an injury","Not recordable because first aid treatment does not make a case recordable"],"correct":3,"explanation":"First aid — including non-prescription medication and simple bandaging — does not make a case OSHA-recordable. Recordability requires medical treatment beyond first aid, days away, restricted work, transfer, loss of consciousness, or a significant diagnosed injury/illness.\n\n急救——包括非处方药和简单包扎——不使案例成为OSHA可记录。可记录性要求超出急救的医疗处理、缺勤、受限工作、转岗、意识丧失或重大确诊伤害/疾病。","related":[{"n":"6.3","t":"OSHA记录判定与记录保存"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Under EPCRA, which report covers the annual inventory of hazardous chemicals stored at a facility?","options":["Tier II Report (Sections 311/312)","Biennial Report","NPDES DMR","TRI Form R (Section 313)"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Tier II reports under EPCRA Sections 311/312 cover hazardous chemical inventory (what is stored on site — quantities, locations, hazards). TRI Form R (Section 313) covers releases of toxic chemicals to the environment. The Biennial Report is RCRA (LQGs), and NPDES DMR (Discharge Monitoring Report) is CWA.\n\nEPCRA第311/312条的二级报告涵盖危险化学品库存（现场储存了什么——数量、位置、危害）。TRI R表格（第313条）涵盖有毒化学品向环境的释放。双年度报告是RCRA的（LQG），NPDES DMR（排放监测报告）是CWA的。","related":[{"n":"15.1","t":"RCRA废物产生者分类"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"In a general-industry warehouse, a maintenance technician must replace a drive belt on a mezzanine platform whose walking surface is 5 feet above the concrete floor. Is fall protection required?","options":["No; mezzanines are exempt from fall protection requirements","Yes; general industry requires fall protection at 4 feet","Yes, but only because the task lasts more than 15 minutes","No; fall protection is not required below 6 feet"],"correct":1,"explanation":"29 CFR 1910.28 requires fall protection for general-industry walking-working surfaces 4 feet or more above a lower level, so 5 feet is covered. The 6-foot trigger applies to construction under 1926.501. The duration of the task does not change the trigger height.\n\n29 CFR 1910.28 规定一般工业行走-工作表面距下层 4 英尺及以上即需坠落防护，因此 5 英尺已适用。6 英尺的触发高度适用于建筑业的 1926.501。作业持续时间不改变触发高度。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"What is the OSHA action level for noise that triggers a hearing conservation program?","options":["95 dBA","80 dBA","85 dBA","90 dBA"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The 8-hour TWA action level is 85 dBA — at or above this level, the employer must implement a hearing conservation program (monitoring, audiograms, protectors at no cost, training). The PEL is 90 dBA (100% dose); the action level is 50% dose.\n\n8小时TWA行动水平为85 dBA——达到或超过此水平，雇主必须实施听力保护计划（监测、听力图、免费保护器、培训）。PEL为90 dBA（100%剂量）；行动水平为50%剂量。","related":[{"n":"17.5","t":"非电离辐射"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which PSM element requires written procedures for inspecting and testing pressure vessels, piping, relief devices, and emergency shutdown systems in accordance with recognized good engineering practices?","options":["Mechanical integrity","Compliance audits","Process hazard analysis","Management of change"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Mechanical integrity, Element 8, is the systematic preventive maintenance program that keeps covered equipment fit for service, with inspections and tests per RAGAGEP such as API 510, API 570, and API 653. The PHA identifies hazards and MOC manages changes; neither keeps equipment from deteriorating. Compliance audits check the system, not the metal.\n\n机械完整性（要素 8）是使受控设备保持可服役状态的系统性预防性维护计划，检验测试须遵循 RAGAGEP，如 API 510、API 570、API 653。PHA 识别危害，MOC 管理变更，都不能防止设备劣化。合规审核检查的是体系，而非设备本身。","related":[{"n":"2.5","t":"机械完整性与泄压"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A deluge system is characterized by:","options":["Pipes always full of water","Sprinkler heads with thermal elements","Open sprinkler heads that discharge water from ALL heads simultaneously when the detection system activates","A single sprinkler head activating independently"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Deluge systems have OPEN heads (no thermal element). When the detection system activates the deluge valve, water flows from ALL heads at once. Used in high-hazard areas expecting rapid fire spread.\n\n雨淋系统有<em>开启式</em>喷头（无热元件）。当探测系统启动雨淋阀时，水同时从所有喷头流出。用于预计火势迅速蔓延的高风险区域。","related":[{"n":"13.6","t":"喷淋"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Lithium batteries being shipped are classified as DOT:","options":["Class 4","Class 9 (Miscellaneous)","Class 8","Class 1"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Lithium batteries are Class 9 — Miscellaneous Dangerous Goods (as are dry ice and asbestos). They are hazardous for fire/thermal runaway reasons but do not fit the other classes.\n\n锂电池是第9类——杂项危险品（干冰和石棉也是）。它们因火灾/热失控风险而具有危险性，但不属于其他类别。","related":[{"n":"13.7","t":"DOT"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An auditor finds that a written LOTO procedure exists, but records do not demonstrate it was followed on a specific piece of equipment. This is an example of a:","options":["Nonconformity","Audit criterion","Conformity","An opportunity for improvement"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A nonconformity is a requirement not being met, evidenced by objective evidence. The requirement is that the LOTO procedure is implemented and followed; the lack of records demonstrating compliance means the requirement is not satisfied. This is a finding requiring corrective action.\n\n不符合是要求未得到满足，需有客观证据支撑。要求是LOTO程序被实施和遵守；缺少显示符合性的记录意味着要求未得到满足。这是需要纠正措施的发现。","related":[{"n":"5.3","t":"ISO 19011 — 管理体系审核指南"},{"n":"5.6","t":"审核、检查与评估 — 关键区别"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A plant manager asks the safety professional to sign a training roster for 20 workers who have not yet attended the required fall-protection class, so a customer audit can proceed. What should the CSP do?","options":["Sign the roster and schedule the class for the following month","Sign only for the workers who have had some prior training","Refuse to sign, and give the customer an accurate training status","Ask a supervisor to sign instead to avoid a personal ethics issue"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Signing a false training record is misrepresentation that endangers workers and violates the requirement to be honest and accurate in professional reports. The constructive path is to correct the status and give the customer truthful information, which also protects the employer from a much larger credibility failure. Routing the signature to someone else does not change the falsity of the record.\n\n在培训记录上签字属于不实陈述，会危及工人，并违反在专业报告中保持诚实准确的要求。建设性的做法是纠正状态并向客户提供真实信息，这也使雇主免于更大的信誉风险。把签字转给他人并不能改变记录虚假的事实。","related":[{"n":"8.8","t":"职业道德"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A near miss occurs on a packaging line. The supervisor asks for a full refresher course for all 42 operators. Training records show that 3 operators transferred in last month and never received the line-specific training. What is the BEST action?","options":["Train the 3 untrained operators and verify the others by observation","Take no action, because a near miss is not an injury","Repeat the training annually for everyone regardless of findings","Deliver the refresher to all 42 operators to be safe"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A person-level needs analysis identifies who actually has the gap. The records show that only three operators lack the required training, so targeted training closes the real gap and avoids the cost and credibility loss of blanket retraining. Observation then confirms whether the other 39 perform correctly; if they do not, the cause may be the procedure, tools, or supervision rather than knowledge. Blanket refreshers are a common but unsupported reaction to a single event.\n\n人员层面的需求分析确定真正存在差距的人。记录显示只有 3 名操作员缺少该岗位培训，因此针对性培训能弥补真实差距，避免全员复训的成本与信任损失。随后通过观察确认其余 39 人是否操作正确；若不正确，原因可能是程序、工具或监督而非知识不足。用全员复训应对单起事件很常见，但缺乏依据。","related":[{"n":"19.1","t":"培训需求评估"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A safety professional takes 36 air sampling measurements with a mean of 85 ppm and a known population standard deviation of 3 ppm. What is the 95% confidence interval for the true mean exposure?","options":["85 ± 3.00","85 ± 1.96","85 ± 0.50","85 ± 0.98"],"correct":3,"explanation":"CI = x̄ ± Z × (σ/√n) = 85 ± 1.96 × (3/√36) = 85 ± 1.96 × 0.5 = 85 ± 0.98. The margin of error is 0.98 ppm, giving an interval of [84.0, 86.0] ppm.\n\nCI = x̄ ± Z × (σ/√n) = 85 ± 1.96 × (3/√36) = 85 ± 1.96 × 0.5 = 85 ± 0.98。误差边际为0.98 ppm，区间为[84.0, 86.0] ppm。","related":[{"n":"6.7","t":"置信区间与t分布"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A permit space has an oxygen-deficient atmosphere that is corrected only by continuous forced-air ventilation. May the employer reclassify it as a non-permit confined space for the entry?","options":["No; ventilation controls the hazard rather than eliminating it","Yes, provided the entry lasts less than one hour","Yes, because the atmosphere is now acceptable for entry","Yes, if the entrant wears a personal oxygen monitor"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A permit space may be reclassified as non-permit only when all hazards are eliminated, not merely controlled. Forced-air ventilation keeps oxygen in range, but the deficiency returns if the ventilation stops, so the hazard is controlled rather than eliminated. Acceptable test results likewise do not by themselves eliminate the atmospheric hazard.\n\n只有当所有危害被消除（而非仅仅被控制）时，许可空间才可重新划分为非许可空间。强制通风虽能把氧含量维持在范围内，但一旦停风缺氧就会重现，因此危害只是被控制而非消除。检测结果合格本身也不等于消除大气危害。","related":[{"n":"4.1","t":"密闭空间"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Which statement BEST describes blended learning?","options":["Using only online training","Combining multiple methods (e.g., e-learning for theory + hands-on for practice) for comprehensive programs","Replacing instructors with AI","Delivering all training through toolbox talks"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Blended learning combines multiple delivery methods — typically e-learning for theory and instructor-led or hands-on sessions for practice. It is often the most effective overall approach for comprehensive training programs.\n\n混合式学习结合多种交付方法——通常在线学习用于理论，讲师主导或实操课程用于实践。对于综合培训项目，它往往是最有效的整体方法。","related":[{"n":"20.4","t":"培训交付方式"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"PSM is described as a management-system standard rather than a specification standard. What does that mean in practice?","options":["It replaces all other OSHA substance-specific health standards","It specifies exact equipment designs that must be installed","It requires defined management systems but leaves the methods to the employer","It applies only to companies with a corporate safety department"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A management-system standard tells the employer what systems must exist — hazard analysis, change management, audits — but not exactly how to build them, much like ISO management standards. That flexibility is why citations often turn on whether the system actually functioned rather than on a single specification. It does not prescribe equipment designs and does not replace other standards.\n\n管理体系标准规定必须建立哪些体系——危害分析、变更管理、审核——但不规定具体如何建立，类似 ISO 管理体系标准。因此处罚往往取决于体系是否真正运作，而非某一项规格。它不规定设备设计，也不取代其他标准。","related":[{"n":"2.1","t":"PSM概述"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under PSM, the incident investigation report must be retained for:","options":["2 years","3 years","5 years","10 years"],"correct":2,"explanation":"PSM incident investigation reports must be retained for 5 years (1910.119(m)(7)). This is the same retention period as... note that compliance audit reports retain only the two most recent. The investigation must start within 48 hours.\n\nPSM事故调查报告必须保留5年（1910.119(m)(7)）。这与合规审核报告（仅保留最近两份）不同。调查必须在48小时内启动。","related":[{"n":"2.2","t":"PSM的14个要素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under FAA Part 107, which of the following is a key requirement for commercial drone operations?","options":["The remote pilot must hold a Remote Pilot Certificate and maintain visual line-of-sight (VLOS)","Operations above 400 feet AGL are always permitted","A co-pilot is required for all flights","The drone must weigh over 100 lbs"],"correct":0,"explanation":"FAA Part 107 requires a Remote Pilot Certificate, drones ≤ 55 lbs, maintained visual line-of-sight (VLOS), operations below 400 ft AGL, and daylight operations (or with anti-collision lighting). Drones are increasingly used to eliminate working-at-height hazards.\n\nFAA第107部要求远程飞行员证书、无人机≤55磅、保持目视视线(VLOS)、在离地400英尺以下操作、白天操作（或配备防撞灯）。无人机越来越多地用于消除高处作业危害。","related":[{"n":"4.8","t":"物料搬运与储存"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In Fault Tree Analysis, an AND gate with two independent basic events having probabilities of 0.1 and 0.2 will have what output probability?","options":["0.28","0.02","0.12","0.3"],"correct":1,"explanation":"For an AND gate with independent events: P = P1 x P2 = 0.1 x 0.2 = 0.02. AND gates reduce probability because ALL inputs must occur for the output to occur.\n\n对于独立事件的与门：P = P1 x P2 = 0.1 x 0.2 = 0.02。与门降低概率，因为所有输入都必须发生输出才会发生。","related":[{"n":"10.4","t":"FTA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A facility stores 6,000 gallons of oil aboveground in containers no larger than 800 gallons each, has never had a reportable discharge, and has no direct pathway to navigable waters. The owner wants to avoid hiring a Professional Engineer. What is allowed?","options":["A Professional Engineer is always required, regardless of capacity","The plan may be self-certified by the owner or operator if it still meets 40 CFR 112 requirements","The plan may be replaced by a one-page spill response card approved by the fire department","No SPCC plan of any kind is needed at this capacity"],"correct":1,"explanation":"SPCC self-certification is available to facilities with an aggregate aboveground oil storage capacity of 10,000 gallons or less, no single discharge greater than 1,000 gallons to navigable waters, and no discharge to navigable waters in the preceding three years. At 6,000 gallons with no discharge history the facility qualifies, but the plan must still address containment, inspections, and countermeasures as 40 CFR 112 requires. Capacity above 1,320 gallons still triggers SPCC, so no plan at all is not an option.\n\nSPCC自认证适用于地上储油总容量不超过10,000加仑、单次向通航水域排放不超过1,000加仑、且此前三年内未向通航水域排放的设施。该设施总容量6,000加仑且无排放历史，符合自认证条件，但计划仍须按40 CFR 112满足围堵、检查与应急对策要求。容量超过1,320加仑仍会触发SPCC，因此“完全不需要计划”不成立。","related":[{"n":"14.1","t":"泄漏预防与控制对策"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d5.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In FTA, a rectangle symbol represents:","options":["An undeveloped event","A transfer symbol","A basic event","An intermediate event (output of a gate)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Rectangle = intermediate event (gate output). Circle = basic event (root cause). Diamond = undeveloped event. House = normal/expected event. Triangle = transfer.\n\n矩形 = 中间事件（门的输出）。圆形 = 基本事件（根本原因）。菱形 = 未展开事件。房形 = 正常/预期事件。三角形 = 转移。","related":[{"n":"10.4","t":"FTA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A supported scaffold platform is being erected for masons. Which combination of dimensions meets OSHA requirements for platform width and distance from the work face?","options":["At least 18 inches wide and within 24 inches of the face","At least 12 inches wide and within 14 inches of the face","At least 18 inches wide and within 14 inches of the face","At least 12 inches wide and within 24 inches of the face"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Scaffold platforms must be at least 18 inches wide unless a narrower platform is justified for a specific trade, and the platform must be no more than 14 inches horizontally from the work face (30 inches if outriggers are used). Greater gaps invite falls and dropped tools. Planks must also be fully decked with gaps no more than 1 inch.\n\n脚手架平台宽度至少 18 英寸（特定工种可使用更窄平台），且距作业面水平距离不超过 14 英寸（使用悬挑架时为 30 英寸）。间隙过大易导致坠落与落物。脚手板还须满铺，板间缝隙不超过 1 英寸。","related":[{"n":"3.6","t":"脚手架与梯子"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Who must perform the periodic inspection of a LOTO energy control procedure, and what must be documented?","options":["An authorized employee other than the one using the procedure, with a certification","The plant manager, with a memo sent to corporate safety for filing","The equipment manufacturer, with a warranty statement for the device","Any affected employee who works in the area, with a note in the shift log"],"correct":0,"explanation":"1910.147(c)(6) requires inspection at least annually by an authorized employee other than the one using the procedure, to correct deviations and review responsibilities. The certification must identify the machine or equipment, the date of inspection, the employees included, and the person performing the inspection. Self-inspection defeats the purpose.\n\n1910.147(c)(6) 要求至少每年由非使用该程序的授权员工进行检查，以纠正偏差并复核职责。认证记录须注明机器或设备、检查日期、涉及的员工以及检查人。由使用者自查则失去意义。","related":[{"n":"4.5","t":"LOTO职责与程序"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Hydrostatic testing of fire extinguishers is typically required every:","options":["6 months","1 year","5 or 12 years depending on type","25 years"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Hydrostatic testing is typically required every 5 or 12 years depending on the extinguisher type (e.g., stored-pressure dry chemical is 12 years; CO2 is 5 years). It verifies the pressure vessel integrity.\n\n水压试验通常根据灭火器类型每5或12年进行一次（如储压式干粉为12年；CO2为5年）。它验证压力容器的完整性。","related":[{"n":"13.5","t":"NFPA10灭火器"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"After a dust explosion, employees first learned about injuries at their own plant from a television news report broadcast before the company sent any internal message. What is the MOST important lesson for the crisis communication plan?","options":["The company should stop answering media questions until the cause is known","An internal notification system must deliver information to employees before external media do","Employees should be instructed to say nothing if reporters call them at home","All internal communication should wait until the investigation report is final"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A core crisis communication principle is that employees should hear about an incident from their own organization first; otherwise rumor and anxiety fill the gap and trust erodes. The fix is a rapid internal notification system with pre-drafted messages and clear channels, not silence. Waiting for the final investigation or refusing to speak to the media at all simply lengthens the information vacuum.\n\n危机沟通的核心原则之一是：员工应首先从自己的组织获知事故消息；否则谣言与焦虑会填补空白，信任随之流失。解决办法是建立快速内部通知系统，配合预先起草的信息和明确的渠道，而不是沉默。等到调查报告最终完成或完全拒绝与媒体沟通，只会延长信息真空。","related":[{"n":"12.7","t":"危机沟通"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following is the correct meaning of \"C\" in a RACI chart?","options":["Consulted — subject matter experts whose opinions are sought before the task is done","Communicated — everyone who should be told about the task","Controller — the person who enforces the deadline","Critical — the person who must complete the task first"],"correct":0,"explanation":"C = Consulted: people (typically subject matter experts) whose opinions are sought through two-way communication before the task is completed. I = Informed: people kept up-to-date through one-way communication after the task.\n\nC = 征询意见：在执行任务前通过双向沟通征询意见的人（通常是主题专家）。I = 知悉：在任务后通过单向沟通持续了解进展的人。","related":[{"n":"8.5","t":"RACI与项目"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which interviewing practice is MOST likely to bias a witness's account?","options":["Interviewing witnesses separately","Using open-ended questions","Asking leading questions such as \"So the guard was removed, right?\"","Conducting the interview promptly"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Leading questions suggest an expected answer and bias the witness's account. Investigators should use open-ended questions (\"What happened next?\") and interview separately and promptly to obtain accurate, uncontaminated accounts.\n\n诱导性问题暗示预期答案，会歪曲证人的陈述。调查者应使用开放式问题（\"接下来发生了什么？\"），并单独、及时访谈以获得准确、未被污染的陈述。","related":[{"n":"7.4","t":"证人访谈技巧"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A qualitative risk assessment produces:","options":["Annualized loss expectancy in dollars","Numerical probabilities and monetary values","Descriptive categories such as Low, Medium, High","Fault tree probability calculations"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Qualitative assessment ranks risk using descriptive categories (Low/Medium/High) based on judgment. Semi-quantitative uses scored scales (1-5). Quantitative produces numerical probabilities and monetary values.\n\n定性评估使用描述性类别（低/中/高）基于判断对风险排序。半定量使用评分量表（1-5）。定量产生数值概率和货币值。","related":[{"n":"9.9","t":"评估方法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A fall-protection anchor system costs 90,000 dollars and is expected to save 30,000 dollars per year in claim and downtime costs. What is the payback period?","options":["3.0 years","3.3 years","9.0 years","2.5 years"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Payback equals initial investment divided by annual savings: 90,000 divided by 30,000 equals 3.0 years. The 3.3-year figure inverts the ratio, and 9.0 years multiplies rather than divides. Payback measures how quickly the investment is recovered and is useful when management is focused on short-term cash exposure rather than total return.\n\n回收期 = 初始投资 ÷ 年节约额 = 90,000 ÷ 30,000 = 3.0 年。3.3 年是比率的倒数，9.0 年则是乘法而非除法。回收期衡量投资回收的速度，当管理层关注短期现金风险而非总回报时特别有用。","related":[{"n":"8.2","t":"ROI 与回收期"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"The WBGT index is used to assess which occupational hazard?","options":["Noise","Heat stress","Vibration","Radiation"],"correct":1,"explanation":"WBGT (Wet Bulb Globe Temperature) is the index for heat stress. It combines wet bulb (humidity), globe (radiant heat), and dry bulb (air temperature) readings. ACGIH uses WBGT to set work-rest cycle recommendations based on metabolic workload.\n\nWBGT（湿球黑球温度）是热应激指标。它综合湿球（湿度）、黑球（辐射热）和干球（气温）读数。ACGIH使用WBGT根据代谢负荷设定工作-休息循环建议。","related":[{"n":"17.6","t":"毒理学指标与进入途径"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is the correct first step in the 6-step Lockout/Tagout procedure?","options":["Prepare for shutdown","Notify affected employees","Shut down the equipment","Apply lockout/tagout devices"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The correct 6-step LOTO sequence is: (1) Prepare for shutdown — identify all energy sources, hazards, and proper shutdown sequence; (2) Notify affected employees; (3) Shut down equipment using normal procedure; (4) Isolate energy sources; (5) Apply LOTO devices; (6) Release/block/dissipate stored energy and verify isolation. Preparing first ensures the shutdown is done correctly and safely.\n\n正确的6步LOTO顺序是：(1) 准备停机——识别所有能量源、危害和正确的停机顺序；(2) 通知受影响员工；(3) 使用正常程序关闭设备；(4) 隔离能量源；(5) 施加LOTO装置；(6) 释放/阻断/消散储存能量并验证隔离。首先做好准备可确保停机正确安全。","related":[{"n":"4.4","t":"上锁挂牌 (LOTO)"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"What is the annual whole-body occupational dose limit for ionizing radiation?","options":["5 rem (0.05 Sv)","15 rem (0.15 Sv)","50 rem (0.5 Sv)","0.5 rem (0.005 Sv)"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The annual whole-body occupational dose limit (TEDE) is 5 rem (0.05 Sv). Other limits: lens of eye = 15 rem, skin/extremities = 50 rem, declared pregnant worker = 0.5 rem over gestation, general public = 0.1 rem (100 mrem) annually.\n\n年度全身职业剂量限值（TEDE）为5 rem（0.05 Sv）。其他限值：眼晶状体=15 rem，皮肤/四肢=50 rem，已申报怀孕工人=妊娠期0.5 rem，一般公众=每年0.1 rem（100 mrem）。","related":[{"n":"17.2","t":"噪声计算"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A sampling survey of 64 workers yields a mean exposure of 30 ppm with a population standard deviation of 12 ppm. What is the standard error of the mean?","options":["3.00 ppm","12.0 ppm","0.19 ppm","1.50 ppm"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The standard error of the mean equals sigma divided by the square root of n: 12 divided by 8 equals 1.5 ppm. The 3.00 value would come from dividing by the square root of 16, and 0.19 from dividing 12 by 64. The standard error describes how much a sample mean would vary from sample to sample, and it is the building block of the confidence interval.\n\n均值标准误 = σ ÷ √n = 12 ÷ 8 = 1.5 ppm。3.00 来自除以 √16，0.19 则是把 12 除以 64。标准误描述样本均值在不同抽样之间的波动程度，是构建置信区间的基础。","related":[{"n":"6.6","t":"统计基础"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A training evaluation measures a reduction in recordable injury rate attributed to a lockout/tagout training program. This is which Kirkpatrick level?","options":["Level 4 — Results","Level 1 — Reaction","Level 2 — Learning","Level 3 — Behavior"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Level 4 (Results) measures organizational impact — injury rate reduction, productivity gains, cost savings, or quality improvements. It is the highest level of evidence but the hardest to isolate from other variables.\n\n第4级（结果）衡量组织影响——伤害率降低、生产力提升、成本节约或质量改进。这是最高层级的证据，但也最难与其他变量分离。","related":[{"n":"20.5","t":"Kirkpatrick四级评估"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A plant recorded 4 lost-time injuries while working 500,000 hours. Using the international convention for lost time injury frequency rate, what is the LTIFR?","options":["16.0","1.6","4.0","8.0"],"correct":3,"explanation":"LTIFR equals (4 times 1,000,000) divided by 500,000, which equals 8.0. The value 1.6 comes from mistakenly using the 200,000-hour base, which would give a lost-time injury rate on the OSHA scale rather than an LTIFR. The 1,000,000-hour base represents roughly 500 full-time workers and is the international convention.\n\nLTIFR =（4 × 1,000,000）÷ 500,000 = 8.0。1.6 是误用 200,000 小时基数得到的 OSHA 尺度损失工时率，而非 LTIFR。1,000,000 小时基数约等于 500 名全职工人，是国际通行做法。","related":[{"n":"6.2","t":"TRIR/DART 公式"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In a fault tree, a top event is caused by an OR gate with inputs of 0.001 and 0.002. Using the rare-event approximation, the top event probability is approximately:","options":["0.003","0.001","0.000002","0.002002"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Rare-event approximation: P ≈ P1 + P2 = 0.001 + 0.002 = 0.003. The exact value would be 0.003 - 0.000002 = 0.002998, so the approximation is very close.\n\n罕见事件近似：P ≈ P1 + P2 = 0.001 + 0.002 = 0.003。精确值为0.003 - 0.000002 = 0.002998，近似非常接近。","related":[{"n":"10.4","t":"FTA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Course materials have been finalized and pilot-tested. The training manager is now booking rooms, scheduling shifts around production, enrolling learners in the LMS, and arranging equipment for the practical exercise. Which ADDIE phase is this?","options":["Evaluation: measuring results and impact","Analysis: needs assessment and context","Design: objectives and assessment plan","Implementation: scheduling and records"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Implementation covers scheduling sessions, arranging logistics (venue, equipment, materials), delivering the training, and managing attendance and records. Finalizing and pilot-testing materials belonged to Development; writing objectives and planning assessment belonged to Design. Evaluation comes after delivery and measures effectiveness.\n\n实施（Implementation）包括安排课程、协调后勤（场地、设备、材料）、交付培训以及管理出勤与记录。材料定稿与试讲属于开发阶段；编写目标和规划评估属于设计阶段。评估在交付之后进行，用于衡量效果。","related":[{"n":"19.3","t":"ADDIE模型"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"An insurance policy with a HIGHER deductible will typically have:","options":["No premium change","Broader coverage","A higher premium","A lower premium, because the insured retains more of the risk"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A higher deductible means the insured pays more out of pocket before the insurer pays, so the insurer's exposure is smaller — hence lower premiums. The deductible is a retention element within an insured risk.\n\n更高的免赔额意味着被保险人自付更多后保险人才赔付，因此保险人的风险敞口更小——故保费更低。免赔额是投保风险中的保留元素。","related":[{"n":"11.8","t":"保险概念"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In Fault Tree Analysis, what is a \"minimal cut set\"?","options":["A set of events that prevents the top event from occurring","Any set of events that can cause the top event","The smallest possible subset of events that will cause the top event, with no redundant events","The complete list of all possible basic events in the system"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A minimal cut set is a cut set containing no subset that is also a cut set. Remove any single event from a minimal cut set and the top event will NOT occur. Minimal cut sets represent critical failure pathways.\n\n最小割集是不包含任何也是割集的子集的割集。从最小割集中移除任何一个事件，顶事件将不会发生。最小割集代表关键失效路径。","related":[{"n":"10.4","t":"FTA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A crew starts a shift after a near miss in which a saw guard was found taped open. The supervisor wants a short, focused discussion of that specific hazard before work begins. What is the MOST appropriate method?","options":["A self-paced e-learning module this week","An annual refresher next quarter","A 15-minute toolbox talk at the point of use","A 40-hour HAZWOPER course for the crew"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A toolbox talk is a short (typically about 15 minutes), single-topic session used to reinforce training, address a recent incident, or cover a task-specific hazard at the point of use — exactly this situation. Attendance, topic, date, and presenter should be documented as part of the training record. A 40-hour course, a self-paced module, or a quarterly refresher is disproportionate and too late to shape behavior this shift.\n\n工具箱谈话是简短（通常约 15 分钟）、聚焦单一主题的活动，用于强化培训、应对近期事件或在作业现场讲解特定危害——正符合此情形。出勤、主题、日期和主讲人应作为培训记录的一部分予以保存。40 小时课程、自定进度模块或季度复训都不成比例，且对本班次的行为影响太迟。","related":[{"n":"20.4","t":"培训交付方式"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"In an indoor work area with no solar load, the wet-bulb temperature is 24 °C and the globe temperature is 40 °C. Using the indoor WBGT equation, what is the WBGT?","options":["26.4 °C","27.6 °C","31.2 °C","28.8 °C"],"correct":3,"explanation":"For indoor or no-sun conditions, WBGT = 0.7 × WB + 0.3 × GT = 0.7(24) + 0.3(40) = 16.8 + 12.0 = 28.8 °C. The outdoor equation adds a dry-bulb term (0.7 × WB + 0.2 × GT + 0.1 × DB), which would give a different value. The WBGT is then compared with the ACGIH TLV for the worker's metabolic rate and work/rest cycle.\n\n室内或无日照条件下，WBGT = 0.7 × WB + 0.3 × GT = 0.7(24) + 0.3(40) = 16.8 + 12.0 = 28.8 °C。室外公式还要加干球项（0.7 × WB + 0.2 × GT + 0.1 × DB），结果会不同。随后将 WBGT 与按代谢率和工作/休息周期查得的 ACGIH TLV 比较。","related":[{"n":"17.8","t":"热应激"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d6.html"}] },
  b: { title: '全真模拟 B', questions: [{"domain":"2","text":"A site has been accepted into VPP Star. A worker is killed in a forklift incident six months later. What happens?","options":["Only the insurance carrier investigates, because VPP sites self-investigate","OSHA still investigates the fatality, and the site must also report it within 8 hours","OSHA takes no action because VPP sites are exempt from enforcement","The site is automatically removed from VPP but no inspection occurs"],"correct":1,"explanation":"VPP removes a site from programmed inspection lists but does not exempt it from enforcement; OSHA investigates fatalities, catastrophes and valid complaints at VPP sites. The fatality must also be reported to OSHA within 8 hours under 29 CFR 1904.39. VPP status may be reviewed afterward, but it never displaces the regulatory duty.\n\nVPP 只把场所从计划性检查名单中移除，并不豁免执法；OSHA 仍会调查 VPP 场所的死亡、灾难和有效投诉。该死亡还须依 29 CFR 1904.39 在 8 小时内报告。事后 VPP 资格可能被复核，但它从不取代法规义务。","related":[{"n":"8.7","t":"VPP 自愿保护"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"At work sites over or adjacent to water, which of the following is required?","options":["At least 4 feet of clearance between workers","At least one Coast Guard-approved 30-inch ring buoy with 90 feet of line","A certified lifeguard on duty at all times","A SCBA for every worker"],"correct":1,"explanation":"OSHA requires at least one U.S. Coast Guard-approved 30-inch ring buoy with 90 feet of line at work sites over or adjacent to water. USCG-approved PFDs must be provided and worn where a drowning hazard exists.\n\nOSHA要求在水上或水体附近的工作场所至少配备一个美国海岸警卫队认证的30英寸救生圈，附带90英尺绳索。存在溺水危害时必须提供并穿戴USCG认证的PFD。","related":[{"n":"3.9","t":"CSP11常见工作场所危害"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which ISO 45001:2018 clause addresses internal audits and management review?","options":["Clause 9 — Performance Evaluation","Clause 10 — Improvement","Clause 6 — Planning","Clause 8 — Operation"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Clause 9 (Performance Evaluation) covers monitoring, measurement, internal audits, and management review. Clause 8 (Operation) covers operational controls; Clause 10 (Improvement) covers incident investigation, nonconformity, corrective action, and continual improvement.\n\n条款9（绩效评价）涵盖监控、测量、内部审核和管理评审。条款8（运行）涵盖运行控制；条款10（改进）涵盖事故调查、不符合、纠正措施和持续改进。","related":[{"n":"5.1","t":"ISO 45001:2018"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A janitorial crew stores sodium hypochlorite bleach next to an acid-based descaler in the same cabinet. What is the primary process-safety concern?","options":["Mixing will release chlorine gas, creating a toxic atmosphere","The two products will neutralize each other and clog the drain","Galvanic corrosion of the metal storage cabinet","Loss of product potency over time in storage"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Hypochlorite plus acid releases chlorine gas, a classic incompatible-mixing scenario that can injure or kill in an enclosed space. Compatibility and inadvertent-mixing hazards are part of the PSI hazard information and must be evaluated in the PHA. Segregating incompatible materials is the engineering-level fix.\n\n次氯酸盐遇酸会释放氯气，是典型的禁配混合情景，在封闭空间内可致伤致死。相容性与意外混合危害属于 PSI 危害信息，必须在 PHA 中评估。隔离存放不相容物料是工程层级的解决办法。","related":[{"n":"2.6","t":"化学相容性与构造材料"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"In the previous question (n = 36), which Z-value is used for a 95% confidence interval?","options":["2.576","3.00","1.645","1.96"],"correct":3,"explanation":"For a 95% confidence interval, Z = 1.96. For 90% use 1.645, for 99% use 2.576. Since n = 36 ≥ 30 and σ is known, the Z (normal) distribution is used.\n\n对于95%置信区间，Z = 1.96。90%用1.645，99%用2.576。由于n = 36 ≥ 30且σ已知，使用Z（正态）分布。","related":[{"n":"6.7","t":"置信区间与t分布"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A boiler explosion is expected once in 25 years, with total losses estimated at $5 million per event. What is the expected annual loss?","options":["$2,000,000","$50,000","$200,000","$250,000"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Expected annual loss = loss per event x annual frequency = $5,000,000 x (1/25) = $200,000 per year. This figure is compared against insurance premiums and control costs. $2,000,000 and $50,000 come from using the wrong divisor.\n\n预期年度损失 = 单次损失 × 年频率 = 5,000,000 × (1/25) = 200,000 美元/年。该数值用于与保费和控制成本比较。2,000,000 与 50,000 分别来自错误的除数。","related":[{"n":"11.6","t":"风险财务五大策略"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following lists the hierarchy of controls in the correct order from most to least effective?","options":["Engineering controls → Elimination → Administrative controls → PPE → Substitution","Elimination → Substitution → Engineering controls → Administrative controls → PPE","PPE → Administrative controls → Engineering controls → Substitution → Elimination","Substitution → Elimination → PPE → Administrative controls → Engineering controls"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The correct order is Elimination, Substitution, Engineering controls, Administrative controls, PPE. This ordering is explicitly emphasized by ANSI/ASSP Z10.0 and is heavily tested. Eliminating the hazard is always preferred over relying on administrative controls or PPE.\n\n正确顺序是消除、替代、工程控制、行政控制、PPE。这一顺序被ANSI/ASSP Z10.0明确强调并高频考查。消除危害始终优于依赖行政控制或PPE。","related":[{"n":"5.2","t":"ANSI/ASSP Z10.0"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following activities is characteristic of safety LEADERSHIP rather than safety management?","options":["Conducting audits","Walking the floor and communicating a safety vision","Tracking TRIR metrics","Writing procedures"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Safety leadership involves vision, culture, influence, and modeling — e.g., walking the floor, communicating vision, and building trust. Writing procedures, conducting audits, and tracking metrics are safety MANAGEMENT activities focused on systems and control.\n\n安全领导力涉及愿景、文化、影响力和示范——如现场巡视、传达愿景和建立信任。编写程序、开展审核和追踪指标是聚焦于系统和控制的安全管理活动。","related":[{"n":"8.4","t":"安全领导力"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Why is it important to define likelihood and severity scales BEFORE using a risk matrix?","options":["To make the matrix mathematically accurate","Because different users would otherwise interpret the levels differently, producing inconsistent ratings","To reduce the number of ratings needed","It is not important"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Without defined scales, \"high likelihood\" means different things to different people, making ratings subjective and inconsistent. Defining scales ensures repeatability, comparability, and defensible prioritization.\n\n没有定义的量表，\"高可能性\"对不同的人含义不同，使评级主观且不一致。定义量表确保可重复性、可比性和可辩护的优先级。","related":[{"n":"9.4","t":"风险矩阵"},{"n":"9.9","t":"评估方法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A degreasing operation releases solvent vapor at a steady 0.2 cfm. The target concentration is 100 ppm, the incoming air contains no solvent, and a safety factor K of 4 is applied. What dilution ventilation rate is required?","options":["800 cfm","2,000 cfm","8,000 cfm","80,000 cfm"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Q = (q × K × 10⁶) ÷ (C − C₀) = (0.2 × 4 × 1,000,000) ÷ (100 − 0) = 800,000 ÷ 100 = 8,000 cfm. The 10⁶ converts the ppm target into a volume fraction, and K provides margin for imperfect mixing. Dilution at this scale is acceptable only because the solvent is of low toxicity and released uniformly; a highly toxic or intermittent release would call for LEV.\n\nQ = (q × K × 10⁶) ÷ (C − C₀) = (0.2 × 4 × 1,000,000) ÷ (100 − 0) = 800,000 ÷ 100 = 8,000 cfm。10⁶ 用于把 ppm 目标值换算为体积分数，K 为混合不均提供余量。只有在溶剂低毒且释放均匀时，才可采用这种规模的稀释通风；高毒或间歇性释放应改用局部排风。","related":[{"n":"18.6","t":"通风一般原则"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d6.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Which of the following is TRUE about \"used oil\" under EPA regulations (40 CFR 279)?","options":["Used oil is managed under its own rule, not automatically as a hazardous waste","Used oil must be shipped with a RCRA manifest at all times","Used oil can be discharged to storm drains if treated","Used oil is always a RCRA hazardous waste"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Used oil is managed under its own standards (40 CFR 279) with separate requirements for generators, transporters, and processors. It becomes hazardous waste only if it exhibits a characteristic or is mixed with hazardous waste. Used oil is never discharged to storm drains.\n\n废油按自身的标准（40 CFR 279）管理，对产生者、运输者和加工者有不同的要求。只有在表现出特征性或与危险废物混合时才成为危险废物。废油绝不能排入雨水下水道。","related":[{"n":"15.4","t":"清洁空气法与清洁水法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Why is a bow-tie diagram particularly useful for training the workforce on barrier management?","options":["Because it replaces the need for written operating procedures","Because it links threats, barriers, and consequences on one page","Because it ranks failure modes by RPN for action","Because it calculates numerical probabilities for each threat"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The single-page diagram shows what can go wrong, which barriers prevent it, and which barriers limit the consequences, so workers can see where they fit. A bow-tie is qualitative and does not compute probabilities or produce RPNs, and it supports rather than replaces procedures.\n\n单页图清楚显示可能出什么错、哪些屏障防止发生、哪些屏障限制后果，工人因此能看到自己的位置。蝴蝶结是定性工具，不计算概率、不产生 RPN，而且是程序的补充而非替代。","related":[{"n":"11.4","t":"蝴蝶结分析"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which characteristic BEST distinguishes engineering controls from administrative controls?","options":["Engineering controls are always preferred by OSHA inspectors","Administrative controls are more effective than engineering controls","Engineering controls cost less to implement","Engineering controls do not depend on worker behavior — they work passively"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The defining difference is reliability: engineering controls work passively (a guardrail protects a worker who is not paying attention), while administrative controls depend on continued human compliance and fail when workers do not follow them.\n\n决定性区别是可靠性：工程控制被动工作（护栏能保护一个没注意的工人），而行政控制依赖持续的人为遵守，工人不遵守即失效。","related":[{"n":"1.3","t":"工程控制"},{"n":"1.4","t":"行政控制与PPE"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"What is the relationship between the absorbed dose in rad and the dose equivalent in rem?","options":["rem = rad × quality factor","rem = rad / quality factor","rem = rad for all radiation types","rem and rad are unrelated quantities"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Dose equivalent (rem) = absorbed dose (rad) × quality factor (QF). This is why 1 rad of alpha (QF=20) = 20 rem, while 1 rad of gamma (QF=1) = 1 rem. The quality factor accounts for the different biological effectiveness of each radiation type.\n\n剂量当量（rem）= 吸收剂量（rad）× 品质因子（QF）。这就是为什么1 rad的α（QF=20）= 20 rem，而1 rad的γ（QF=1）= 1 rem。品质因子反映了每种辐射类型不同的生物有效性。","related":[{"n":"17.6","t":"毒理学指标与进入途径"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A learning objective states: \"The employee will demonstrate proper donning of a full-face respirator within 2 minutes with no errors.\" This objective BEST exemplifies which type of objective?","options":["Open-ended objective","Affective objective","SMART objective","Subjective objective"],"correct":2,"explanation":"This is a SMART objective: it is Specific (donning a full-face respirator), Measurable (within 2 minutes, no errors), Achievable (a realistic skill), Relevant (to safety), and Time-bound (within 2 minutes).\n\n这是一个SMART目标：具体（佩戴全面罩呼吸器）、可衡量（2分钟内、无错误）、可实现（现实可行的技能）、相关（与安全相关）、有时限（2分钟内）。","related":[{"n":"19.1","t":"培训需求评估TNA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"In a LOPA study, which of the following is a true \"independent protection layer\"?","options":["The basic process control system, if the initiating event is a BPCS control loop failure","A safety relief valve that is separate from and not affected by the initiating event","Operator training, since it is documented and repeated","The plant alarm, if the initiating event is the alarm being ignored"],"correct":1,"explanation":"An IPL must be independent of the initiating event and other layers. A relief valve separate from the initiating event qualifies. If the initiating event IS a BPCS failure, that BPCS loop cannot count as an IPL. Training is not a quantifiable IPL; an alarm that is the initiating event cannot be its own safeguard.\n\nIPL必须独立于初始事件和其他层。与初始事件无关的泄压阀符合条件。如果初始事件本身就是BPCS失效，则该BPCS回路不能算作IPL。培训不是可量化的IPL；作为初始事件的报警不能作为其自身的防护。","related":[{"n":"2.4","t":"PHA与HAZOP深入"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A hygienist collects 49 personal noise dosimetry samples with a mean of 88.0 dBA. The population standard deviation is known to be 3.5 dBA. What is the 95 percent confidence interval for the true mean?","options":["88.0 plus or minus 1.96 dBA","88.0 plus or minus 3.50 dBA","88.0 plus or minus 0.50 dBA","88.0 plus or minus 0.98 dBA"],"correct":3,"explanation":"With a known population standard deviation, use the Z interval: CI equals mean plus or minus Z times sigma divided by the square root of n. The standard error is 3.5 divided by 7, or 0.5, and 1.96 times 0.5 equals 0.98, so the interval is 87.02 to 88.98 dBA. The 0.50 value is the standard error rather than the margin of error, and 1.96 ignores the sample size.\n\n总体标准差已知时用 Z 区间：CI = 均值 ± Z × σ/√n。标准误 = 3.5 ÷ 7 = 0.5，1.96 × 0.5 = 0.98，区间为 87.02～88.98 dBA。0.50 只是标准误而非误差幅度，1.96 则忽略了样本量。","related":[{"n":"6.7","t":"置信区间"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A worker performing maintenance on a roof edge will be attached to an anchor with a 6-ft lanyard. The anchor is at the worker's D-ring height (0 ft above D-ring). What is the free fall distance if the worker steps off the edge?","options":["12 feet","0 feet","6 feet","3.5 feet"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Free fall = anchorage to D-ring distance (0 ft) + lanyard length (6 ft) = 6 feet. This is exactly at the 6-ft maximum, so the system complies but has no margin — any higher anchor or longer connector would exceed the limit.\n\n自由坠落 = 锚固点到D型环距离（0英尺）+ 系索长度（6英尺）= 6英尺。这恰好处于6英尺上限，系统合规但没有余量——锚点更高或连接器更长就会超限。","related":[{"n":"3.4","t":"坠落间隙与PFAS计算"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A maintenance technician reached into a running conveyor to clear a jam and fractured her hand. Which 5 Whys ending identifies a system-level cause that a corrective action can address?","options":["Why was it running? Because no lockout step existed for clearing jams","Why did she reach in? Because she was careless about her own safety","Why was she hurt? Because she was simply unlucky that day","Why did it happen? Because conveyors are inherently dangerous equipment"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The system-level answer identifies a missing control, the absence of an energy-isolation step in the task procedure, which can be corrected by revising the procedure and adding a physical interlock. Carelessness, bad luck and inherent danger are dead ends that generate no actionable change. Effective root causes point to conditions management can control.\n\n系统层面的答案指出了缺失的控制措施——作业程序中没有能量隔离步骤，因而可以通过修订程序和增加物理联锁来纠正。粗心、运气不好、设备本身危险都是死胡同，产生不了可执行的改进。有效的根本原因指向管理层可以控制的条件。","related":[{"n":"7.5","t":"根源分析方法"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"What is the maximum allowable concentration of flammable gases/vapors (as a percentage of LEL) for entry into a confined space under OSHA standards?","options":["Less than 10% LEL","Less than 25% LEL","Less than 1% LEL","Less than 5% LEL"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The atmosphere inside a confined space must have flammable gas, vapor, or mist concentrations less than 10% of the lower explosive limit (LEL). Values at or above 10% LEL prohibit entry. Values at or above 10% but below 25% LEL allow continued monitoring only (no entry). At 25% LEL and above, the area is immediately dangerous to life and health (IDLH).\n\n密闭空间内的可燃气体、蒸气或雾的浓度必须低于爆炸下限(LEL)的10%。达到或超过10% LEL的值禁止进入。在10%到25% LEL之间的数值仅允许继续监测（不可进入）。25% LEL及以上，该区域为立即危及生命与健康(IDLH)。","related":[{"n":"4.2","t":"大气检测与监测"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Which statement about the Hazard Ranking System (HRS) is correct?","options":["It scores uncontrolled hazardous waste sites for possible NPL listing","It ranks industrial facilities for TRI reporting","It classifies wastes under the TCLP test","It sets the passing score for the CSP exam"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The Hazard Ranking System (HRS) is EPA's scoring tool used to evaluate the relative threat posed by uncontrolled hazardous waste sites. Sites scoring high enough are proposed for the National Priorities List (NPL) for Superfund cleanup.\n\n危害分级系统（HRS）是EPA的评分工具，用于评估失控危险废物场所的相对威胁。评分足够高的场所会被提议列入国家优先清理名单（NPL），进行超级基金清理。","related":[{"n":"15.5","t":"TSCA和EPCRA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A maintenance crew will apply a new epoxy coating inside a tank next week. The product is new to the site, the task is performed only once, and the crew has never used the application equipment. What should the safety professional do first?","options":["Complete a JHA with the crew before the task is first performed","Issue respirators and let the crew start as scheduled","File the new SDS and rely on the manufacturer's recommendations","Wait until the first application is finished and then observe the crew"],"correct":0,"explanation":"New, infrequent, high-hazard work is the top priority for a JHA, and the analysis must be done before the task starts with the workers who will perform it. Observing afterwards is reactive, and an SDS or a respirator alone does not identify task-specific hazards such as tank entry or solvent vapor accumulation. Worker involvement is what surfaces the real steps and shortcuts.\n\n新增、不常做、高风险作业是 JHA 的最高优先级，且必须在作业开始前、与实际作业人员共同完成。事后观察属被动；仅凭 SDS 或呼吸器无法识别进入储罐、溶剂蒸气积聚等任务特有危害。工人的参与才能揭示真实步骤与变通做法。","related":[{"n":"9.7","t":"作业危害分析JHA"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An internal audit is performed entirely by reviewing documents in a conference room, with no observation of work and no worker interviews. The MOST significant limitation is that the audit cannot:","options":["satisfy the confidentiality principle of ISO 19011","be classified as a first-party internal audit","be used as an input to the management review","verify that documented controls are actually implemented"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Document review shows what the system says should happen; only observation and interviews show what actually happens. An audit without verification at the point of work can confirm that procedures exist but cannot confirm implementation or effectiveness, which is the core of Clause 9.2. It remains a legitimate first-party audit and remains valid input to management review, and confidentiality is not compromised by document review.\n\n文件评审说明体系规定应当发生什么，只有现场观察与访谈才能说明实际发生了什么。缺少作业现场验证的审核可以确认程序是否存在，却无法确认其实施与有效性，而这正是第9.2条的核心。它仍是合法的第一方审核，也仍可作为管理评审输入，保密性也不因文件评审而受损。","related":[{"n":"5.3","t":"ISO 19011 审核"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Under RCRA, a facility that generates 1,200 kg of non-acute hazardous waste per month is classified as a:","options":["Conditionally Exempt Small Quantity Generator (CESQG)","Very Small Quantity Generator (VSQG)","Small Quantity Generator (SQG)","Large Quantity Generator (LQG)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"LQGs generate ≥1,000 kg/month of hazardous waste. 1,200 kg exceeds this threshold. SQG is 100–1,000 kg/month, and VSQG is ≤100 kg/month. Note that CESQG was renamed to VSQG in the 2016 Generator Improvements Rule.\n\nLQG每月产生≥1,000 kg危险废物。1,200 kg超过此阈值。SQG为100–1,000 kg/月，VSQG为≤100 kg/月。注意CESQG在2016年产生者改进规则中更名为VSQG。","related":[{"n":"15.1","t":"RCRA废物产生者分类"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A consultant's draft report shows a client site with a TRIR of 2.4 and a DART of 3.1. What is the MOST likely explanation?","options":["DART uses a 1,000,000-hour base while TRIR uses 200,000","One rate is miscalculated, since DART is a subset of TRIR","The site has an unusually severe injury profile","DART may legitimately exceed TRIR when cases are severe"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Every DART case is by definition also an OSHA-recordable case, so with the same denominator DART can never exceed TRIR. A DART above TRIR therefore signals a calculation or transcription error in one of the two rates. Changing the base would alter both rates consistently and cannot produce this inversion.\n\n按定义，每一个 DART 案例同时都是 OSHA 可记录案例，在分母相同的前提下 DART 永远不可能高于 TRIR。DART 高于 TRIR 只能说明其中一个率计算或转录有误。改变基数会同步影响两个率，因此不可能造成这种倒挂。","related":[{"n":"6.2","t":"TRIR/DART 公式"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Under the Hazard Communication Standard, which of the following is a required element?","options":["Safety Data Sheets (SDS) and employee training","All of the above","A written hazard communication program","Container labeling"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The HCS requires four elements: (1) a written hazard communication program, (2) container labeling, (3) Safety Data Sheets, and (4) employee training. All four are required for compliance.\n\nHCS要求四个要素：(1) 书面危险沟通计划，(2) 容器标签，(3) 安全数据表，和(4) 员工培训。合规需要全部四个。","related":[{"n":"13.8","t":"HazCom"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"The Brief & Scala model is used to:","options":["Calculate the sample volume for a low-flow pump","Calculate noise dose","Adjust occupational exposure limits for extended work shifts (e.g., 10-12 hours)","Determine respirator cartridge service life"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The Brief & Scala model adjusts OELs for extended shifts: Adjusted OEL = OEL × (8/h) × (24-h)/16, where h = hours worked. For a 12-hour shift, the adjustment factor is (8/12) × (12/16) = 0.5, meaning the TWA limit is halved.\n\nBrief & Scala模型用于延长班次的OEL调整：调整后OEL = OEL × (8/h) × (24-h)/16，其中h为工作小时数。对于12小时班次，调整系数为(8/12) × (12/16) = 0.5，即TWA限值减半。","related":[{"n":"16.4","t":"采样设备与方法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-16.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An investigator photographs a damaged guard with a phone, but no scale, date or machine identifier appears in the images. What is the main problem?","options":["The photographs must be taken by a certified evidence photographer","The images should be deleted once the written report is complete","The images lack context on scale, timing and location, weakening their value","Phone photographs are never acceptable as evidence in any case"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A photograph is evidence only when it can be tied to a place, a time and a size, so a scale reference, date and equipment identifier belong in the image or in a linked log. Without them the picture shows damage but cannot support specific measurements or rebut alternative explanations. Phone cameras are perfectly acceptable when the context is documented.\n\n照片只有在能与地点、时间和尺寸对应时才是证据，因此比例参照物、日期和设备标识应出现在画面中或附于关联日志。缺少这些信息，照片只能显示损坏，无法支持具体测量，也无法排除其他解释。只要记录了背景信息，手机拍摄完全可以接受。","related":[{"n":"7.3","t":"证据链"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Under CWA Section 404, permits for dredge and fill activities are issued by:","options":["The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA)","The US Army Corps of Engineers (USACE)","The Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA)","State departments of transportation"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The US Army Corps of Engineers issues Section 404 permits for discharges of dredged or fill material into waters of the U.S., with EPA providing veto authority and environmental guidance. Wetlands protection is a key part of Section 404.\n\n美国陆军工程兵团（USACE）对向美国水域排放疏浚物或填方物发放第404条许可证，EPA拥有否决权和环境指导。湿地保护是第404条的关键部分。","related":[{"n":"15.5","t":"TSCA和EPCRA"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A tabletop exercise is best described as:","options":["A full deployment of personnel and equipment simulating a real emergency","A discussion-based exercise where participants walk through a scenario verbally","A physical drill testing only evacuation procedures","A computer simulation requiring no human participants"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Tabletop exercises are discussion-based — participants talk through a scenario to test plans, policies, and coordination. No resources are deployed. They are the lowest-cost exercise type.\n\n桌面演练是基于讨论的——参与者口头演练情景以测试计划、政策和协调。不部署资源。这是成本最低的演练类型。","related":[{"n":"12.6","t":"演练"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"The Safety Case approach became mandatory for offshore installations in the UK following which disaster?","options":["Deepwater Horizon","Piper Alpha","Chernobyl","Bhopal"],"correct":1,"explanation":"After the Piper Alpha disaster (1988), the UK Health and Safety Executive made Safety Cases mandatory for offshore oil and gas installations. Deepwater Horizon (2010) was a later offshore disaster in the Gulf of Mexico; Chernobyl and Bhopal were industrial disasters in different sectors.\n\n在Piper Alpha灾难（1988年）之后，英国健康与安全执行局要求海上油气装置必须编制安全案例。Deepwater Horizon（2010年）是后来墨西哥湾的海上灾难；切尔诺贝利和博帕尔是其他行业的事故。","related":[{"n":"5.8","t":"系统安全分析技术"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"The most common MSD worldwide and the leading cause of work disability is:","options":["Tennis elbow","Thoracic outlet syndrome","Carpal tunnel syndrome","Low back pain"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Low back pain (LBP) is the most common musculoskeletal disorder and the leading cause of work disability worldwide. It is associated with heavy lifting, twisting, bending, whole-body vibration, and prolonged sedentary work.\n\n下背痛（LBP）是最常见的肌肉骨骼疾病，也是全球工伤致残的首要原因。它与重物提举、扭转、弯腰、全身振动和长时间久坐工作相关。","related":[{"n":"18.6","t":"通风一般原则"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-18.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A HAZOP study is led by a team leader whose main role is to:","options":["Be the most senior technical engineer","Facilitate the study and ensure the methodology is followed correctly","Make all final decisions on recommendations","Operate the plant during the study"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The HAZOP leader facilitates the study, keeps the team on method, and ensures guidewords are applied systematically. The leader need NOT be the most senior technical person — the team provides technical expertise.\n\nHAZOP负责人主持研究、让团队遵循方法、确保系统应用引导词。负责人不一定是最高级的技术人员——团队提供技术专长。","related":[{"n":"11.3","t":"团队工作表"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A risk assessment team calculates a residual risk score of 12 for a task. The site criterion states that any score above 9 is unacceptable. What is the correct next step?","options":["Record the score and continue, since evaluation is only advisory","Raise the acceptance criterion to 12 so the item can be closed","Implement additional controls and re-evaluate the residual risk before the task proceeds","Accept the risk because controls are already in place"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The evaluate step compares the analyzed risk with pre-set criteria; a residual of 12 against a limit of 9 means the risk is not acceptable, so further controls are required and the assessment is repeated. Accepting the score or moving the goalpost defeats the purpose of having criteria, and the evaluation drives real decisions rather than serving as advice.\n\n评估步骤是把分析出的风险与预定标准比较；残余 12 超过上限 9，说明风险不可接受，必须追加控制并重新评估。直接接受或修改标准会使标准失去意义；评估结论具有决策效力，而不是参考意见。","related":[{"n":"9.2","t":"风险评估五步流程"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A worker is exposed to 100 dBA for 1 hour, 95 dBA for 2 hours, and 85 dBA for 5 hours. What is the noise dose under OSHA?","options":["106%","119%","156%","131%"],"correct":3,"explanation":"D = 100 × Σ(C/T). Allowed times under the 5-dB rule: 100 dBA → 2 h; 95 dBA → 4 h; 85 dBA → 16 h. So D = 100 × (1/2 + 2/4 + 5/16) = 100 × (0.500 + 0.500 + 0.3125) = 131%. Because D > 100%, the worker is overexposed and feasible engineering/administrative controls plus hearing protection are required. Treating 85 dBA as an 8-hour allowance, instead of 16 hours, is the usual arithmetic error.\n\nD = 100 × Σ(C/T)。按 5 dB 交换率：100 dBA 允许 2 小时、95 dBA 允许 4 小时、85 dBA 允许 16 小时。故 D = 100 × (1/2 + 2/4 + 5/16) = 100 × (0.500 + 0.500 + 0.3125) = 131%。因 D 大于 100%，属过度暴露，必须实施可行的工程/行政控制并提供听力防护。把 85 dBA 的允许时间当作 8 小时而不是 16 小时，是最常见的算术错误。","related":[{"n":"17.2","t":"噪声计算"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d6.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A facility replaces a carbon steel gasket with a gasket made of a different, more expensive material — the dimensions are identical. Under PSM, this action:","options":["Requires only that the purchase be logged in maintenance records","Requires a new PHA to be conducted immediately","Is a \"replacement in kind\" and requires no further action","Triggers MOC because the material of construction changed, even though dimensions are identical"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A change in material of construction is NOT a replacement in kind — even if physical dimensions are identical, a chemically different material can alter corrosion behavior, pressure rating, and compatibility. MOC must be triggered. A new PHA is not required merely for a gasket change; MOC review suffices.\n\n构造材料的变化不是\"同类替换\"——即使物理尺寸完全相同，化学性质不同的材料也可能改变腐蚀行为、压力等级和相容性。必须触发MOC。仅更换垫片不需要重新进行PHA；MOC审查即可。","related":[{"n":"2.3","t":"关键PSM概念详解"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which of the following is an example of risk SHARING?","options":["Discontinuing a hazardous product line","Buying a general liability policy","A joint venture distributing risk among partners","Paying losses from the operating budget"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Risk sharing distributes the financial burden across multiple parties — joint ventures, risk pools, and consortiums. A liability policy is transfer; paying from budget is retention; stopping the product line is avoidance.\n\n风险分担将财务负担分配给多个当事方——合资企业、风险池和联合体。责任保险是转移；从预算支付是保留；停止产品线是规避。","related":[{"n":"11.6","t":"五大策略"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"According to RACI best practice, how many \"Accountable\" (A) roles should a task have?","options":["Exactly one","As many as possible for redundancy","None — A is optional","At least two, to share responsibility"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Each task should have exactly ONE Accountable (A) role. Multiple A's create confusion about who ultimately owns the task. Every task must also have at least one Responsible (R).\n\n每项任务应恰好有一个最终负责(A)角色。多个A会造成对谁最终拥有该任务的困惑。每项任务还必须至少有一个负责执行(R)角色。","related":[{"n":"8.5","t":"RACI与项目"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"In the Safety Case approach, risks must be demonstrated to have been reduced to what level?","options":["The insurance industry threshold","The industry average","Zero","ALARP (As Low As Reasonably Practicable)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The Safety Case requires demonstration that risks are reduced to ALARP — As Low As Reasonably Practicable. ALARP does not mean zero risk; it means further risk reduction would be grossly disproportionate in cost to the benefit gained. The three pillars are hazard identification, risk assessment, and risk management.\n\n安全案例要求证明风险已降低至ALARP——最低合理可行水平。ALARP不代表零风险；它意味着进一步降低风险的成本将与所得收益严重不成比例。三大支柱是危害识别、风险评估和风险管理。","related":[{"n":"5.8","t":"系统安全分析技术"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A Lifting Index (LI) greater than 3.0 indicates:","options":["Moderate risk — administrative controls may be needed","High risk — engineering controls strongly recommended","Very high risk — nearly all workers at elevated risk; engineering controls essential","The task is safe for all workers"],"correct":2,"explanation":"LI > 3.0 indicates very high risk where nearly all workers are at elevated risk of low back pain and engineering controls are essential. LI ≤ 1 = safe. 1 < LI ≤ 2 = moderate risk. 2 < LI ≤ 3 = high risk.\n\nLI > 3.0表示非常高风险，几乎所有工人的下背痛风险都较高，工程控制至关重要。LI ≤ 1 = 安全。1 < LI ≤ 2 = 中等风险。2 < LI ≤ 3 = 高风险。","related":[{"n":"18.1","t":"NIOSH修订版提举方程"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-18.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A nonconformity about missing machine guards was closed after guards were installed on the two machines cited. Six months later a guard is missing on a third machine of the same model. What does this indicate?","options":["The finding should have been classified as an opportunity for improvement","The audit scope was too narrow for the audit to be validly conducted","The correction was made, but the systemic cause was never addressed or verified","The correction was appropriate and the case should remain closed"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Installing guards on the two cited machines is a correction; a corrective action would have asked why guards were missing on that machine model and fixed the inspection, procurement or design cause. Clause 10.2 also requires reviewing the effectiveness of corrective action, which would have caught the recurrence. A recurrence on a third unit is evidence of an unresolved systemic cause, not evidence that the original closure was adequate.\n\n给两台被点名的设备安装防护罩属于纠正（correction）；纠正措施则应追问为什么该型号设备会缺失防护罩，并从检查、采购或设计环节消除原因。第10.2条还要求评审纠正措施的有效性，这一环节本可以发现复发。第三台设备再次出现同类问题，说明系统原因尚未解决，而非原关闭足够充分。","related":[{"n":"5.3","t":"ISO 19011 审核"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A site reports a TRIR of 2.1 against an industry average of 3.0, but the site denominator excludes about 30 percent of the hours worked at the facility because those hours belong to contractors. How should this comparison be viewed?","options":["Contractor hours are always excluded, so the comparison is exact","The comparison may be misleading, because exposure is understated","The site rate should be multiplied by the industry average first","The site is clearly better than the industry average"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A rate is only comparable when the numerator and denominator cover the same population; dropping contractor hours while contractor injuries still occur at the site distorts the result. Best practice is to define the boundary consistently and disclose it, or to report contractor and employee rates separately. No adjustment factor converts one population into another after the fact.\n\n只有当分子与分母覆盖同一人群时，率才具有可比性；把承包方工时剔除、却仍在该场所发生承包方伤害，会扭曲结果。最佳做法是统一界定边界并予以披露，或分别报告雇员与承包方的率。事后没有任何调整系数能把一个人群换算成另一个人群。","related":[{"n":"6.4","t":"基准比较"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which of the following is a required element of the Fire Prevention Plan (29 CFR 1910.39)?","options":["Procedures for controlling sources of ignition","A schedule of evacuation drills","A list of emergency contact phone numbers","Procedures for accounting for employees"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The FPP requires: a list of major fire hazards, procedures for handling/storing hazardous materials, procedures to control ignition sources, fire protection equipment types and maintenance, housekeeping procedures, and responsible persons. Evacuation and accounting belong to the EAP.\n\nFPP要求：主要火灾危害清单、危险材料处理/储存程序、控制点火源的程序、消防设备类型和维护、内务管理程序及负责人。疏散和清点属于EAP。","related":[{"n":"12.3","t":"FPP"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A trainer begins each safety module with a real incident case study from the facility to explain WHY the topic matters before teaching procedures. Which andragogical assumption is the trainer addressing?","options":["Need to Know","Orientation to Learning","Self-Concept","Readiness to Learn"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The \"Need to Know\" assumption states that adults need to understand why something is important before investing effort. Starting with a real incident establishes relevance and answers \"why should I care?\"\n\n\"学习需求\"假设指出，成人在投入精力之前需要理解为什么某事很重要。从真实事故出发建立了相关性，并回答了\"我为什么要在意？\"","related":[{"n":"20.1","t":"Knowles成人学习理论"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"ISO 14001:2015 is primarily concerned with:","options":["Occupational health and safety","Financial auditing","Quality management","Environmental management"],"correct":3,"explanation":"ISO 14001 is the international standard for Environmental Management Systems (EMS). It focuses on environmental aspects, impacts, compliance obligations, and lifecycle perspective. Occupational health and safety is covered by ISO 45001; quality by ISO 9001.\n\nISO 14001是环境管理体系（EMS）的国际标准。它关注环境因素、影响、合规义务和生命周期视角。职业健康安全由ISO 45001覆盖；质量由ISO 9001覆盖。","related":[{"n":"5.7","t":"ISO 14000系列"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Before excavating for a new storm drain, what must be done about underground utilities?","options":["Nothing, if the drawings are less than 10 years old","Call 811 only if the excavation will exceed 5 feet","Ask the utility company to be on site during the dig","Locate and mark all underground installations before digging"],"correct":3,"explanation":"1926.651(b) requires the estimated location of underground installations to be determined before digging, typically through the 811 one-call system, and the exact locations to be found by safe and acceptable means while the excavation is open. Stale drawings are not a substitute. Contact with a gas or electric line can be immediately fatal.\n\n1926.651(b) 要求开挖前查明地下设施的预估位置（通常通过 811 一键呼叫系统），并在开挖过程中用安全可靠的方法确认确切位置。过期图纸不能替代。挖破燃气或电力管线可能立即致命。","related":[{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘要求"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"In ISO 45001, requirements for Management of Change (MOC) are found in which clause?","options":["Clause 5 — Leadership","Clause 10 — Improvement","Clause 4 — Context","Clause 8 — Operation"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Management of change is part of Clause 8 (Operation), specifically 8.1.3 — ensuring planned changes are controlled, new hazards assessed, and risk controls determined before the change is implemented. MOC is a key operational control for preventing incidents during periods of change.\n\n变更管理属于条款8（运行），具体是8.1.3——确保计划中的变更受控、评估新危害并在实施前确定风险控制。MOC是防止变更期间发生事故的关键运行控制。","related":[{"n":"5.1","t":"ISO 45001:2018"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A construction safety manager wants one monthly number that will show whether field controls are weakening before injuries appear. Which candidate measure is the WEAKEST choice for that purpose?","options":["Number of pre-task plans reviewed by a supervisor before work starts","Percentage of identified hazards closed within 14 days","Number of safety meetings held per month","Percentage of workers with current fall-protection training"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Counting meetings measures activity, not whether the meetings changed conditions or behavior, so it can rise while risk stays flat. Closure of identified hazards, current training and verified pre-task planning are all tied to specific controls that prevent injury. A leading indicator should be measurable, actionable and linked to the risk it is meant to control.\n\n只统计会议次数衡量的是活动量，而不是会议是否改变了现场条件或行为，因此它可能在风险毫无下降时继续上升。隐患关闭率、培训有效性和作业前计划核查都直接绑定具体控制措施。领先指标应当可测量、可行动，并与它所要控制的危害相关。","related":[{"n":"6.1","t":"领先与滞后指标"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A learner who prefers to learn by reading SDS sheets, written procedures, and taking detailed notes would be classified under which VARK category?","options":["Kinesthetic","Visual","Auditory","Read/Write"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The Read/Write (R) preference is for text-based information — manuals, procedures, reports, SDS sheets, lists, and note-taking. Visual (V) is for graphical depictions; this distinction is important in VARK.\n\n读写（R）偏好是针对基于文字的信息——手册、程序、报告、SDS安全数据表、清单和记笔记。视觉（V）是针对图形化呈现；这一区别在VARK中很重要。","related":[{"n":"20.2","t":"VARK学习偏好"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Goal Structuring Notation (GSN) is primarily used to:","options":["Draw event trees","Represent safety cases graphically, showing how goals are supported by evidence","Calculate RPN values","Classify fire hazards"],"correct":1,"explanation":"GSN is a graphical notation for safety cases: goals (claims) decompose into sub-goals, ultimately supported by evidence (solutions). It makes the safety argument auditable and reviewable.\n\nGSN是安全案例的图形符号：目标（声明）分解为子目标，最终由证据（解决方案）支撑。它使安全论证可审计、可审查。","related":[{"n":"10.8","t":"Safety Case"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"In the four ISD strategies, \"Simplify\" is best exemplified by:","options":["Reducing the batch size of a toxic intermediate","Replacing a flammable solvent with a nonflammable one","Lowering the operating pressure of a reactor","Designing incompatible gas-line connections so they physically cannot be connected"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Simplify designs out human error — incompatible connections that cannot be made, keyed and color-coded fittings, error-proofing (poka-yoke). Lowering pressure is Moderate; reducing batch size is Minimize; replacing the solvent is Substitute.\n\n简化通过设计消除人为错误——无法连接的相容性接口、钥匙化与颜色编码的接头、防错设计。降低压力是缓和；减少批量是最小化；更换溶剂是替代。","related":[{"n":"1.7","t":"本质安全设计(ISD)"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following is the best definition of a \"root cause\"?","options":["The deepest underlying system deficiency that, if corrected, will prevent recurrence","The cause identified by the first witness","The first event in a chain of events","The most expensive cause to fix"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A root cause is the deepest underlying system deficiency whose correction prevents recurrence. It is not necessarily the first event or the most expensive to fix — it is the fundamental system weakness (e.g., missing procedure, design flaw, management failure).\n\n根本原因是最深的潜在系统缺陷，纠正后能防止再发生。它不一定是第一个事件或最贵的修复项——它是根本的系统弱点（如程序缺失、设计缺陷、管理失效）。","related":[{"n":"7.1","t":"事故调查的目的与基本概念"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"In ISO 19011 terms, which document sets out the objectives, scope, criteria, dates and audit team for one specific audit?","options":["The audit programme","The audit plan","The audit checklist","The audit report"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The audit programme is the set of arrangements for one or more audits planned over a period, while the audit plan describes the activities and arrangements for a single audit. The checklist is a working document derived from the plan, and the report is the output produced after the audit is conducted. Confusing programme with plan is a common exam trap when the question specifies 'one specific audit'.\n\n审核方案（audit programme）是针对一段时间内一项或多项审核的安排，而审核计划（audit plan）描述单次审核的活动与安排。检查表是由计划派生的工具文件，报告是审核实施后的输出。题干限定“某一次具体审核”时，正确答案是审核计划。","related":[{"n":"5.3","t":"ISO 19011 审核"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Which of the following is classified as a Universal Waste?","options":["Spent fluorescent lamps","Empty pesticide containers that have been triple-rinsed","Asbestos-containing floor tiles","Used oil"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Fluorescent lamps (including CFLs, HID, mercury vapor, and neon) are classified as Universal Waste because they contain mercury. Used oil is managed under the used oil standards (40 CFR 279), asbestos is regulated under NESHAP/OSHA, and triple-rinsed pesticide containers are generally not hazardous waste.\n\n荧光灯（包括CFL、HID、汞蒸气和霓虹灯）因含汞被归类为通用废物。废油根据废油标准管理（40 CFR 279），石棉受NESHAP/OSHA监管，三重冲洗过的农药容器通常不属于危险废物。","related":[{"n":"15.2","t":"通用废物"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Using the NIOSH recommended criterion (3-dB exchange rate), what is the allowable exposure time at 100 dBA?","options":["2 hours","30 minutes","15 minutes","1 hour"],"correct":2,"explanation":"NIOSH: T = 8 ÷ 2^((L − 85)/3) = 8 ÷ 2^(15/3) = 8 ÷ 2⁵ = 8 ÷ 32 = 0.25 hour = 15 minutes. The 3-dB rate reflects the true doubling of acoustic energy, so allowed time falls much faster than under OSHA's 5-dB rule, where 100 dBA still permits 2 hours. NIOSH values are recommendations, not enforceable limits.\n\nNIOSH：T = 8 ÷ 2^((L − 85)/3) = 8 ÷ 2^(15/3) = 8 ÷ 2⁵ = 8 ÷ 32 = 0.25 小时 = 15 分钟。3 dB 交换率反映声能的真实倍增，因此允许时间比 OSHA 的 5 dB 规则下降得快得多——在 OSHA 下 100 dBA 仍允许 2 小时。NIOSH 数值是建议值，不是强制限值。","related":[{"n":"17.2","t":"噪声计算"},{"n":"17.1","t":"噪声监管标准"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d6.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"OSHA cites an employer for a recognized serious hazard that is not covered by a specific standard. Which provision supports the citation?","options":["Section 11(c), the anti-retaliation provision","29 CFR 1904.7, the general recording criteria","29 CFR 1910.1020, access to employee records","Section 5(a)(1), the general duty clause"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Section 5(a)(1) requires each employer to furnish a workplace free from recognized hazards that are causing or likely to cause death or serious physical harm, and it is used when no specific standard applies. To support a general duty citation, OSHA must show a recognized hazard, a feasible means of abatement and employee exposure. The other provisions address retaliation and recordkeeping, not hazard abatement.\n\n第 5(a)(1) 条要求雇主提供不存在已知危害、且该危害正在或可能导致死亡或严重身体伤害的工作场所，在没有具体标准适用时据此开罚。要支持一般责任条款的罚单，OSHA 须证明危害已被认知、整改可行且员工确有暴露。其他条款涉及报复与记录保存，而非危害消除。","related":[{"n":"8.8","t":"职业道德"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A course has been delivered to 200 employees. Smile sheets average 4.7/5, but no post-test, no on-the-job observation, and no revision have occurred. Which ADDIE phase is incomplete?","options":["Analysis","Design","Development","Evaluation"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The Evaluation phase measures whether the objectives were met, using Kirkpatrick Levels 1–4, and feeds the findings back for improvement. Collecting only reaction data leaves Levels 2–4 untouched, so the program's effectiveness is unknown. Analysis, Design, and Development all occurred before delivery (needs assessment, objectives, materials and pilot), so the missing phase is Evaluation.\n\n评估（Evaluation）阶段用柯氏 1–4 级衡量目标是否达成，并把结果反馈用于改进。只收集反应数据，2–4 级完全缺失，项目有效性无从判断。分析、设计、开发都在交付前完成（需求评估、目标、材料与试讲），因此缺失的是评估阶段。","related":[{"n":"19.3","t":"ADDIE模型"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A 6-foot-deep sump with a 24-inch opening must be entered monthly to change a pump screen. Workers are inside about 20 minutes, the space is not ventilated, and hydrogen sulfide has been detected there before. How should it be classified?","options":["A permit-required space, because of limited access and a hazardous atmosphere","Not a confined space, because employees enter it regularly","A non-permit confined space, because the entries are routine","A confined space but not permit-required, because entries are short"],"correct":0,"explanation":"All three defining criteria are met — large enough to enter, limited means of entry and exit, and not designed for continuous occupancy — so it is a confined space. A potential hazardous atmosphere makes it permit-required regardless of entry duration or frequency. Routine entry does not downgrade the classification.\n\n三项定义标准全部满足——可身体进入、进出受限、非为连续占用设计——因此属于密闭空间。只要可能存在危险气氛，无论进入时长或频次如何，都属于许可要求的密闭空间。例行进入不会降低其分类。","related":[{"n":"4.1","t":"密闭空间"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which heat detection device responds to a rapid temperature increase of roughly 15 degrees F per minute and restores itself automatically after the temperature falls?","options":["Fixed-temperature heat detector","Rate-of-rise heat detector","Ionization smoke detector","Photoelectric smoke detector"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A rate-of-rise detector actuates when the temperature climbs faster than a preset rate, typically about 15 degrees F per minute, and self-restores when conditions normalize. A fixed-temperature detector waits for a specific absolute temperature such as 135 F, so it is slower for a fast-growing fire. Ionization and photoelectric detectors respond to smoke particles rather than to heat.\n\n差温探测器在温度上升速率超过预设值（通常约每分钟15华氏度）时动作，条件恢复正常后可自动复位。定温探测器则要等到某个绝对温度（如135华氏度）才动作，对快速发展的火灾响应更慢。离子式和光电式探测器响应的是烟雾颗粒而非热量。","related":[{"n":"13.3","t":"火灾报警"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following best illustrates a PREVENTIVE action?","options":["Paying higher insurance premiums after a claim","Installing guardrails on an edge after a fall occurred there","Identifying an unprotected edge during a risk assessment and installing guardrails before anyone falls","Investigating an incident and disciplining the worker"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A preventive action addresses a potential problem before it occurs — here, installing guardrails after identifying the hazard in a risk assessment. The first option is corrective (reacting to an actual fall); the others are not preventive actions.\n\n预防措施在问题发生前处理潜在问题——此处是在风险评估中识别危害后安装护栏。第一个选项是纠正性的（对实际坠落做出反应）；其他选项不是预防措施。","related":[{"n":"7.7","t":"纠正措施与预防措施"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An audit team assigned to an ammonia refrigeration facility has no experience with ammonia systems. Under ISO 19011, the BEST solution is to:","options":["add a technical expert to advise the team while the auditor retains responsibility for the audit","cancel the audit until a permanently employed auditor with that expertise is hired","let the refrigeration supervisor explain the process and sign off on the findings","limit the audit to a document review of the process safety management manuals"],"correct":0,"explanation":"ISO 19011 allows technical experts to support an audit team with specialized knowledge while the auditors remain responsible for the audit and its conclusions. The supervisor being audited cannot validate findings, and cancelling or narrowing the audit to documents defeats its purpose. Selecting the team must consider the competence needed for the specific scope, not just general auditing skill.\n\nISO 19011 允许技术专家为审核组提供专门知识，而审核员仍对审核及其结论负责。受审核的车间主管不能为自己的区域确认发现，取消审核或把审核缩成文件评审也失去了审核的意义。组队时必须考虑具体范围所需的能力，而不仅是通用审核技能。","related":[{"n":"5.3","t":"ISO 19011 审核"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A contractor's 3x3 matrix rates a fall from a 6 m platform as Medium. The host employer's 5x5 matrix rates the same exposure as High. What is the best explanation and action?","options":["The lower rating should be used to avoid conflict","The contractor is wrong, because a 5x5 matrix is always more accurate","The scales and criteria differ, so the ratings are not comparable; align them first","The two ratings should be averaged to settle the difference"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A risk matrix is semi-quantitative and its scales are defined by the organization, so a 3x3 Medium and a 5x5 High can describe the same exposure. Before comparing or ranking across organizations, the scales and acceptance criteria must be harmonized. Neither matrix is intrinsically more correct, and averaging or choosing the lower rating only hides the disagreement.\n\n风险矩阵是半定量工具，其量表由组织自行定义，因此 3×3 的“中”与 5×5 的“高”可能指同一暴露。跨组织比较或排序前必须先统一量表与接受标准。两种矩阵本身没有绝对对错；取平均或取低值只会掩盖分歧。","related":[{"n":"9.4","t":"风险矩阵"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Under ISO 45001 Clause 5 (Leadership), workers are expected to:","options":["Have no formal role in the OH&S management system","Be represented solely by a safety committee with no worker input","Take sole responsibility for regulatory compliance","Participate in and be consulted on OH&S decisions that affect them"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Clause 5 requires consultation and participation of workers and worker representatives. Workers participate in hazard identification, risk assessment, incident investigation, and decisions affecting their safety. This is a defining feature of ISO 45001's leadership clause.\n\n条款5要求与员工及员工代表协商并让其参与。员工参与危害识别、风险评估、事故调查以及影响其安全的决策。这是ISO 45001领导力条款的标志性特征。","related":[{"n":"5.1","t":"ISO 45001:2018"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In the 5-step process, the \"Evaluate\" step involves:","options":["Identifying all potential hazards","Comparing the analyzed risk level against risk acceptance criteria","Implementing new control measures","Calculating insurance premiums"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Evaluation compares the analyzed risk (L×S) against pre-established acceptance criteria to decide whether the risk is tolerable, needs more controls, or is unacceptable. This is where ALARP is applied.\n\n评估将分析出的风险（L×S）与预先设定的接受标准比较，以决定风险是否可容忍、需要更多控制还是不可接受。ALARP在此应用。","related":[{"n":"9.2","t":"五步流程"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A maintenance planner proposes replacing a pressure relief valve with a spare that has the same size and connections but a set pressure 25 psi higher. Which PSM requirements are triggered?","options":["Only a mechanical integrity inspection of the newly installed valve","Only a hot work permit issued for the maintenance turnaround","A management-of-change review plus an update of the relief design basis in the PSI","None, because the valve is a like-for-like replacement of the spare"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A different set pressure is not a replacement in kind: it changes the relief system design basis, which is required process safety information. MOC must review and authorize the change, and the PSI must be updated to reflect the new design basis. Mechanical integrity then inspects and tests the installed device.\n\n设定压力不同不属于同类替换：它改变了泄压系统设计依据，而设计依据属于必须维护的工艺安全信息。必须通过 MOC 审查批准，并更新 PSI 以反映新的设计依据。之后由机械完整性程序对该装置进行检验与测试。","related":[{"n":"2.3","t":"关键PSM概念"},{"n":"2.5","t":"机械完整性与泄压"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following hazard descriptions is NOT a required element of a PHA?","options":["The market price of the process chemicals","Hazards of the process","Facility siting considerations","Human factors"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A PHA must address: hazards of the process, previous incidents, engineering and administrative controls, consequences of control failure, facility siting, human factors, and qualitative evaluation of safety/health effects on employees. Chemical market pricing is not a hazard analysis subject.\n\nPHA必须涉及：工艺危害、以往事故、工程和行政控制、控制失效的后果、设施选址、人因工程以及对员工安全/健康影响的定性评估。化学品市场价格不属于危害分析内容。","related":[{"n":"2.4","t":"PHA与HAZOP深入"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Risk summation from multiple analyses is BEST described as:","options":["Summing all insurance claims","Adding RPN values to calculate FTA probabilities","Ignoring all results except the highest one","Aggregating individual risk analysis results into a comprehensive risk profile"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Risk summation aggregates results from FMEA, FTA, HAZOP, etc. into one risk picture for decision-makers — via simple summation, matrix consolidation, or probabilistic methods like Monte Carlo.\n\n风险汇总将FMEA、FTA、HAZOP等的结果聚合为一个供决策者使用的风险图景——通过简单汇总、矩阵整合或蒙特卡洛等概率方法。","related":[{"n":"10.8","t":"Safety Case"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"The PSM standard requires that operating procedures cover which operating phase?","options":["Only initial startup and normal shutdown","Only normal operations","Only emergency operations","Initial startup, normal operations, temporary operations, emergency shutdown, emergency operations, normal shutdown, and startup after turnaround"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Operating procedures must cover all operating phases: initial startup, normal operations, temporary operations, emergency shutdown, emergency operations, normal shutdown, and startup following a turnaround. They must also state operating limits, consequences of deviation, and steps to correct deviations.\n\n操作规程必须涵盖所有操作阶段：初始启动、正常运行、临时操作、紧急停车、紧急操作、正常停车和检修后启动。还必须说明操作限值、偏差后果和纠正偏差的步骤。","related":[{"n":"2.3","t":"关键PSM概念详解"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Change Analysis as an incident investigation technique is most closely associated with which safety management process?","options":["OSHA recordkeeping","Job Safety Analysis (JSA)","Safety training needs assessment","Management of Change (MOC)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Change Analysis examines what changed before the incident — new equipment, modified procedures, different materials, new personnel, etc. This directly aligns with Management of Change (MOC), which is the systematic process to evaluate and control risks from changes. Incidents often occur during periods of change that were not properly assessed through MOC.\n\n变更分析检查事故发生前发生了什么变化——新设备、修改的程序、不同的材料、新人员等。这与变更管理(MOC)直接对应，后者是评估和控制变更风险的系统化过程。事故经常发生在未通过MOC正确评估的变更期间。","related":[{"n":"7.5","t":"根源分析方法"},{"n":"7.2","t":"事故调查七步流程"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Which statement about \"toolbox talks\" is correct?","options":["They are only for construction workers","They are full-day certification courses","They are short (~15 min), focused, single-topic safety sessions for reinforcement between formal training","They replace annual OSHA-required training"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Toolbox talks are short (typically ~15 min), focused sessions on a single topic — used to reinforce formal training, address recent incidents, and maintain safety awareness. They do NOT satisfy annual regulatory training requirements (e.g., HAZWOPER refresher, respirator training).\n\n工具箱谈话是简短（通常约15分钟）、聚焦单一主题的课程——用于强化正式培训、应对近期事故和保持安全意识。它们不能满足年度法规培训要求（如HAZWOPER复训、呼吸器培训）。","related":[{"n":"20.4","t":"培训交付方式"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under excavation standards, when must the competent person inspect an excavation?","options":["Only when a complaint is filed","Only at the start of the project","Daily and after every rainstorm, vibration, or other hazard-increasing event","Weekly"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The competent person must inspect the excavation daily and after each rainstorm, earthquake, or other hazard-increasing occurrence, and before employees enter. The competent person must have authority to take prompt corrective measures.\n\n合格人员必须每日检查挖掘，并在每次暴雨、地震或其他增加危害的事件后、员工进入前检查。合格人员必须有权采取及时纠正措施。","related":[{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘安全要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under NFPA 70E, which of the following approach boundaries may ONLY be crossed by a qualified person with an approved, documented work plan and appropriate PPE?","options":["Arc Flash Boundary","Restricted Approach Boundary","Flash Protection Boundary","Limited Approach Boundary"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The Restricted Approach Boundary may only be crossed by qualified persons with a documented work plan and appropriate PPE. The Limited Approach Boundary can be crossed by unqualified persons if accompanied by a qualified person. The Prohibited Approach Boundary requires the same protection as direct contact. \"Flash Protection Boundary\" was the old NFPA 70E term, replaced by \"Arc Flash Boundary.\"\n\n限制区域边界仅可由具有书面工作计划和适当PPE的合格人员进入。限制接近边界可由有合格人员陪同的不合格人员进入。禁止接近边界需要与直接接触相同的防护。\"闪络防护边界\"是旧的NFPA 70E术语，已被\"弧闪边界\"取代。","related":[{"n":"3.2","t":"电气安全工作条件与许可证"},{"n":"3.1","t":"NFPA 70E概述"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Under OSHA PSM (29 CFR 1910.119), a process hazard analysis must be updated and revalidated at least every:","options":["5 years","10 years","1 year","3 years"],"correct":0,"explanation":"PSM requires revalidation of the process hazard analysis at least every 5 years, and also after a major incident or significant process change. HAZOP is a common PHA technique used to meet this requirement.\n\nPSM要求至少每5年再验证工艺危害分析，并在重大事故或重大工艺变更后同样需要。HAZOP是满足此要求的常用PHA技术。","related":[{"n":"11.3","t":"团队工作表"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Asbestosis is BEST described as:","options":["A form of skin cancer","An acute respiratory infection","An allergic reaction to asbestos fibers","A progressive, irreversible fibrosis of the lungs caused by asbestos exposure"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Asbestosis is a progressive, irreversible diffuse interstitial fibrosis caused by inhalation of asbestos fibers. It is distinct from asbestos-related cancers (lung cancer, mesothelioma). Mesothelioma is strongly associated with asbestos and has a 10-40+ year latency.\n\n石棉肺是吸入石棉纤维导致的进行性、不可逆的弥漫性间质纤维化。它与石棉相关癌症（肺癌、间皮瘤）不同。间皮瘤与石棉高度相关，潜伏期10-40年以上。","related":[{"n":"17.3","t":"听力保护计划HCP"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A functional exercise differs from a full-scale exercise primarily in that it:","options":["Simulates a specific function (e.g., EOC activation) without physical deployment of equipment","Requires no participants","Is more expensive","Uses more real equipment"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A functional exercise simulates a specific component (like the emergency operations center or communications) with simulated inputs and real coordination, but does NOT physically deploy equipment or personnel to the field.\n\n功能演练模拟特定组成部分（如应急运作中心或通信），使用模拟输入和实际协调，但不物理部署设备或人员到现场。","related":[{"n":"12.6","t":"演练"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which of the following is NOT one of the eight emergency types listed in CSP11 Domain 4.1?","options":["Severe weather","Cyber security","Construction scheduling delays","Fire"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The eight types are: fire, severe weather, nuclear incidents, natural disasters, terrorist attacks, chemical spills, utilities systems failure, and cyber security. Construction scheduling is a project-management concern, not an emergency type.\n\n八种类型是：火灾、恶劣天气、核事件、自然灾害、恐怖袭击、化学品泄漏、公用设施中断和网络安全。施工进度延误是项目管理问题，不属于紧急情况类型。","related":[{"n":"12.1","t":"紧急类型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"When selecting a training delivery method, which factor is MOST important for a high-hazard task like confined space entry rescue?","options":["The ability to provide realistic, hands-on practice without real-world risk","The shortest delivery time","The largest class size possible","Lowest cost per learner"],"correct":0,"explanation":"For high-hazard tasks (confined space rescue, emergency response), realistic simulation and hands-on practice are essential — training must develop actual skills, not just knowledge. Cost, speed, and class size should not override the need for practical competence.\n\n对于高风险任务（密闭空间救援、应急响应），逼真的模拟和动手实践至关重要——培训必须培养实际技能，而非仅仅知识。成本、速度和大班规模不应凌驾于实际能力培养之上。","related":[{"n":"19.6","t":"SMART培训目标"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A worker with wet skin has a body resistance of about 1,000 ohms and contacts a 120-V source. Using Ohm's law, what current flows through the body?","options":["1,200 mA","120 mA","1.2 mA","12 mA"],"correct":1,"explanation":"I = V/R = 120 / 1,000 = 0.12 A, or 120 mA. Currents in this range can cause ventricular fibrillation and are well above the let-go threshold of roughly 10 mA. This is why wet conditions are so dangerous: dry skin resistance of about 100,000 ohms would limit the same voltage to about 1.2 mA.\n\nI = V/R = 120 ÷ 1,000 = 0.12 A，即 120 mA。该量级电流可引起心室颤动，远高于约 10 mA 的摆脱阈值。这正是潮湿环境危险的原因：干燥皮肤电阻约 100,000 Ω，同一电压下电流仅约 1.2 mA。","related":[{"n":"3.2","t":"电气安全工作条件"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"In which situation is relying on PPE as the primary control MOST defensible?","options":["PPE protects all workers in the area equally well","Higher-level controls are infeasible and no alternative exists","PPE is the least expensive option available in the budget","Workers have requested PPE instead of a process change"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The hierarchy allows PPE when higher-level controls are infeasible or while they are being implemented — for example, short-duration emergency response or a task that cannot be engineered differently. Cost alone, worker preference, or a mistaken belief that PPE protects everyone are not acceptable justifications. PPE protects only the wearer and fails if it is not worn correctly.\n\n控制层级允许在更高层级控制不可行或正在实施时使用 PPE——例如短时应急响应，或无法通过工程手段改变的任务。单纯因为成本低、工人偏好，或误以为 PPE 能保护所有人，都不构成正当理由。PPE 只保护佩戴者，且佩戴不当即失效。","related":[{"n":"1.8","t":"控制措施选择"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which of the following is a BEST PRACTICE in crisis communication?","options":["Refuse to comment until all facts are known","Designate a single trained spokesperson and acknowledge the situation early","Let every employee speak to the media","Deny the incident occurred"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Best practice: one designated spokesperson, early acknowledgment, honest sharing of known facts, and scheduled updates. Silence (\"no comment\") is interpreted as guilt and allows rumors to fill the vacuum.\n\n最佳实践：一位指定发言人、尽早确认、诚实分享已知事实、并安排定期更新。沉默（\"无可奉告\"）被解读为有罪，让谣言填补真空。","related":[{"n":"12.7","t":"危机沟通"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is NOT one of the 14 elements of Process Safety Management under 29 CFR 1910.119?","options":["Management of Change (MOC)","Job Safety Analysis (JSA)","Pre-Startup Safety Review (PSSR)","Process Hazard Analysis (PHA)"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Job Safety Analysis (JSA), also called Job Hazard Analysis (JHA), is a general safety tool for analyzing individual job tasks — it is NOT a PSM element. The 14 PSM elements are: Employee Participation, PSI, PHA, Operating Procedures, Training, Contractors, PSSR, Mechanical Integrity, Hot Work Permit, MOC, Incident Investigation, Emergency Planning & Response, Compliance Audits, and Trade Secrets.\n\n工作安全分析（JSA），也称工作危害分析（JHA），是分析单个作业任务的通用安全工具——它不属于PSM要素。14个PSM要素是：员工参与、PSI、PHA、操作规程、培训、承包商、PSSR、机械完整性、动火作业许可证、MOC、事故调查、应急计划与响应、合规审核和商业秘密。","related":[{"n":"2.2","t":"PSM的14个要素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following best describes the purpose of an incident investigation?","options":["To identify root causes and implement corrective actions that prevent recurrence","To fulfill insurance claim documentation only","To determine which employee should be retrained","To assign blame and discipline the responsible worker"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The primary purpose of investigation is prevention — identify root causes and implement corrective actions so the incident does not recur. Blame-oriented investigations suppress reporting and hide system causes.\n\n调查的主要目的是预防——识别根本原因并实施纠正措施，使事故不再发生。以追责为导向的调查会抑制报告并掩盖系统原因。","related":[{"n":"7.1","t":"事故调查的目的与基本概念"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Which element is the WEAKEST indicator of whether safety training was effective?","options":["Level 3 on-the-job behavior observations","Level 4 injury rate reduction","Level 1 learner satisfaction scores","Level 2 post-test scores"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Level 1 (Reaction) — learner satisfaction — is the weakest indicator of effectiveness. Positive reactions do not guarantee learning occurred (Level 2), that behavior changed (Level 3), or that results improved (Level 4). Higher levels provide stronger evidence.\n\n第1级（反应）——学员满意度——是效果最弱的指标。积极的反应不能保证学习已发生（第2级）、行为已改变（第3级）或结果已改善（第4级）。更高层级提供更强的证据。","related":[{"n":"19.3","t":"ADDIE模型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"During a pre-shift inspection, a wire rope sling shows a broken safety latch on the hook and about 12% abrasion loss on one leg. What is the correct action?","options":["Return it to service if the load is less than half the rated capacity","Repair the latch with wire and continue using the sling today","Use the sling but shorten it to avoid the worn section of rope","Remove it from service; a damaged latch and wear beyond criteria require withdrawal"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Rigging hardware must be inspected before each shift and removed from service for cracks, deformation, missing or damaged safety latches, or wear beyond the removal criteria, commonly about 10% loss of the original dimension. A broken latch allows the load to slip off the hook. Field repairs and derating are not acceptable substitutes for removal.\n\n索具硬件必须在每班前检查，出现裂纹、变形、安全锁扣缺失或损坏、或磨损超过报废标准（通常为原始尺寸损失约 10%）时须停用。锁扣损坏会使荷载从吊钩滑脱。现场修补或降级使用都不能替代停用。","related":[{"n":"4.8","t":"物料搬运与储存"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"What is the correct order of Kolb's Experiential Learning Cycle?","options":["Abstract Conceptualization → Concrete Experience → Reflective Observation → Active Experimentation","Concrete Experience → Reflective Observation → Abstract Conceptualization → Active Experimentation","Active Experimentation → Abstract Conceptualization → Reflective Observation → Concrete Experience","Reflective Observation → Active Experimentation → Concrete Experience → Abstract Conceptualization"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Kolb's cycle: 1) Concrete Experience (doing), 2) Reflective Observation (watching/reviewing), 3) Abstract Conceptualization (thinking/forming principles), 4) Active Experimentation (applying), then back to Concrete Experience.\n\nKolb循环：1) 具体体验（做），2) 反思观察（观察/回顾），3) 抽象概念化（思考/形成原则），4) 主动实验（应用），然后回到具体体验。","related":[{"n":"20.3","t":"Kolb体验学习"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Which of the following correctly describes the relationship between GHS hazard categories and NFPA 704 ratings?","options":["GHS Category 1 is the most severe; NFPA 4 is the most severe","NFPA 1 is the most severe; GHS Category 1 is the least severe","They are identical systems and interchangeable","Both use Category 1 as the most severe"],"correct":0,"explanation":"GHS uses Category 1 as the most severe hazard (with higher numbers less severe), while NFPA 704 uses 4 as the most severe (with 0 as minimal). This is a common exam trap — the scale directions are opposite. They are different systems for different purposes (GHS = workplace labels/SDS; NFPA = emergency response).\n\nGHS使用类别1为最严重危害（数字越大越轻），而NFPA 704使用4为最严重（0为最小）。这是一个常见的考试陷阱——两者的等级方向相反。它们是不同目的的不同系统（GHS=工作场所标签/SDS；NFPA=应急响应）。","related":[{"n":"14.7","t":"危险物质运输与应急响应"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-14.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A job analysis yields a recommended weight limit of 30 lb for a lift, but the tote being handled actually weighs 45 lb. What is the lifting index, and how is it interpreted?","options":["LI = 0.67, indicating the lift is acceptable","LI = 15, indicating the load must be lifted by two people","LI = 1.5, indicating the lift is acceptable because the index is below 3.0","LI = 1.5, indicating increased risk of lifting-related injury"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Lifting index = load weight / RWL = 45 / 30 = 1.5. An LI above 1.0 indicates increased risk, and above 3.0 indicates significant risk for a substantial portion of the workforce. The fix is to reduce the load, improve the coupling, or bring the load closer to the body so the RWL increases.\n\n提举指数 = 荷载重量 ÷ RWL = 45 ÷ 30 = 1.5。LI 超过 1.0 表示风险升高，超过 3.0 表示对相当一部分劳动者构成重大风险。改进方向是减轻荷载、改善抓握条件，或让荷载靠近身体以提高 RWL。","related":[{"n":"4.8","t":"物料搬运与储存"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is TRUE about atmospheric testing in excavations?","options":["Required in all excavations regardless of depth","Required in excavations 4 feet or deeper where an oxygen-deficient or hazardous atmosphere could reasonably be expected","Required only in excavations deeper than 8 feet","Atmospheric testing is never required in excavations"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Atmospheric testing is required in excavations 4 feet or deeper where an oxygen deficiency or hazardous atmosphere could reasonably be expected. The 4-foot trigger parallels the general-industry fall protection height and is frequently tested.\n\n在深度4英尺及以上、且合理预期可能存在缺氧或危险气氛的挖掘中，需要进行大气检测。4英尺触发点与一般工业坠落防护高度平行，是高频考点。","related":[{"n":"4.2","t":"大气检测与监测"},{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘安全要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A training program's objectives are all at the \"Remember\" level of Bloom's Taxonomy, but the job requires workers to make safety judgments in novel situations. The primary deficiency is:","options":["The evaluation is too strict","The objectives are too difficult","The objectives are set at too low a cognitive level for the job requirements","The delivery method is wrong"],"correct":2,"explanation":"If the job requires judgment in novel situations (Evaluate/Create level), training objectives at the Remember level are insufficient — they will not develop the required decision-making skills. Objectives must match the actual cognitive demands of the job.\n\n如果工作需要在新情境中做判断（评价/创造层次），那么停留在记忆层次的培训目标是不够的——它们无法培养所需的决策能力。目标必须匹配工作的实际认知要求。","related":[{"n":"19.4","t":"持续改进模型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Pre-entry testing of a tank that was just purged with oxygen shows 24.5% O2, 0% LEL, and no toxics. What is the correct interpretation?","options":["The space is oxygen-enriched, which sharply increases the fire risk","The space is acceptable if the entry is kept short in duration","The space is safe because oxygen is well above the 19.5% minimum","The space is safe if the entrants wear a respirator during entry"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The acceptable oxygen range is 19.5% to 23.5%, so 24.5% is oxygen-enriched, and elevated oxygen makes clothing and materials burn violently. Entry must not proceed until the enrichment is corrected by ventilation and the space is re-tested. A high oxygen reading is never extra safe.\n\n可接受的氧含量范围为 19.5% 至 23.5%，24.5% 属于富氧，会使衣物与材料剧烈燃烧。必须通过通风并复测把氧含量纠正后才能进入。氧含量高绝不等于更安全。","related":[{"n":"4.2","t":"大气检测与监测"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"The maximum gap permitted between scaffold planks under OSHA is:","options":["2 inches","No gap is permitted","½ inch","1 inch"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Scaffold platforms must be fully planked, and the maximum gap between adjacent planks is 1 inch. Planks may not deflect more than 1/60 of their span.\n\n脚手架平台必须满铺，相邻脚手板之间的最大间隙为1英寸。脚手板挠度不得超过其跨度的1/60。","related":[{"n":"3.6","t":"脚手架与梯子安全"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Under 29 CFR 1910.1030, how long must an employer keep bloodborne pathogens training records?","options":["5 years","30 years","1 year","3 years"],"correct":3,"explanation":"1910.1030(h)(2)(i) requires training records to be kept for 3 years from the date the training occurred, and they must include the dates, a summary of contents, the names and qualifications of trainers, and the names and job titles of attendees. The 30-year figure applies to medical and exposure records under 1910.1020, not to BBP training records.\n\n1910.1030(h)(2)(i) 要求培训记录自培训之日起保存 3 年，内容包括培训日期、内容摘要、讲师姓名与资质、参训人员姓名与职务。30 年适用于 1910.1020 下的医疗与暴露记录，不适用于血源性病原体培训记录。","related":[{"n":"20.7","t":"OSHA培训要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Under OSHA, which classification of violation involves the employer intentionally and knowingly committing the violation?","options":["Other-than-serious violation","Willful violation","Repeat violation","Serious violation"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A willful violation occurs when the employer intentionally and knowingly commits the violation, or is aware a hazardous condition exists and makes no reasonable effort to eliminate it. Willful violations carry the highest penalties (up to $161,323 per violation) and can carry criminal penalties if a worker death results.\n\n故意违规发生在雇主故意且明知地实施违规行为，或意识到存在危险条件但未做出合理努力消除之时。故意违规处罚最高（每项违规最高$161,323），若导致工人死亡可追究刑事责任。","related":[{"n":"8.8","t":"道德与法律"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A learning management system (LMS) delivers self-paced modules and tracks completion. This delivery method is best suited for:","options":["Geographically dispersed workforce requiring consistent refresher training","One-on-one leadership coaching","Assessing complex psychomotor skills","Developing hands-on rescue skills"],"correct":0,"explanation":"E-learning via an LMS is ideal for geographically dispersed workforces, refresher training, and large-scale consistent rollout. It is NOT well-suited for hands-on skills (rescue, equipment operation) or complex psychomotor assessment.\n\n通过LMS的在线学习非常适合地理分散的员工队伍、复训和大规模一致推广。它不适合动手技能（救援、设备操作）或复杂的精神运动技能评估。","related":[{"n":"20.4","t":"培训交付方式"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A cook working a bank of deep fryers must know how far away the Class K extinguisher may be mounted. What maximum travel distance does NFPA 10 allow from the cooking appliance?","options":["45 ft","30 ft","75 ft","50 ft"],"correct":1,"explanation":"NFPA 10 limits the travel distance to a Class K extinguisher to 30 feet from cooking appliances, because a cooking-oil fire grows extremely fast and the appliance must be reached almost immediately. The 75-foot figure applies to Class A and Class D hazards, and 50 feet applies to Class B hazards up to 20-B; neither covers commercial cooking equipment. Faster access is the reason Class K distances are the shortest in the standard.\n\nNFPA 10规定到K类灭火器的行走距离不得超过距烹饪设备30英尺，因为食用油火灾蔓延极快，必须几乎立即到达设备。75英尺适用于A类和D类危害，50英尺适用于20-B及以下的B类危害；两者都不覆盖商用烹饪设备。正是这一更快速到达的要求，使K类的距离成为标准中最短的。","related":[{"n":"13.5","t":"便携式灭火器"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A failure mode is scored S=9, O=3, D=8. Which set of recommended actions is most consistent with FMEA practice?","options":["Reduce severity by rewriting the severity scale definitions","Lower the RPN action threshold until the item qualifies for action","Raise the detection rating to 10 so the item stands out in the ranking","Reduce occurrence by design change and improve detection with automated testing"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Recommended actions target occurrence (remove the cause) or detection (catch it earlier), because severity is usually fixed by the design. Rewriting scales or thresholds manipulates the numbers without reducing risk, and raising the detection rating makes the score worse, not better. A severity of 9 also requires action in its own right.\n\n建议措施针对发生度（消除原因）或检测度（更早发现），因为严重性通常由设计决定、难以改变。改量表或阈值只是操纵数字，并未降低风险；把检测评分提高到 10 反而使评分更差。严重性 9 本身也要求采取措施。","related":[{"n":"10.3","t":"FMEA工作表与行动"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"In the PDCA cycle of ISO 45001, which phase includes implementing the OH&S processes, providing resources, and ensuring worker competence?","options":["Plan","Do","Check","Act"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The \"Do\" phase is about implementation — putting the plans into action. This includes providing resources, ensuring competence and awareness, establishing communication processes, and operating the controls identified during the Plan phase.\n\n\"实施(Do)\"阶段是关于执行——将计划付诸行动。这包括提供资源、确保能力和意识、建立沟通过程以及运行在策划阶段确定的控制措施。","related":[{"n":"5.1","t":"ISO 45001:2018"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following best describes RAGAGEP as used in PSM Mechanical Integrity?","options":["A training requirement for all mechanical engineers","A government mandate to use only new equipment","Recognized and Generally Accepted Good Engineering Practices — the codes and standards used to guide inspection and testing (e.g., ASME BPV Code, API 510/570/653)","A random audit process for gas and pressure systems"],"correct":2,"explanation":"RAGAGEP stands for Recognized and Generally Accepted Good Engineering Practices. It includes codes and standards such as the ASME Boiler and Pressure Vessel Code, API 510 (vessels), API 570 (piping), and API 653 (tanks) that guide how inspections and tests are performed under Element 8.\n\nRAGAGEP指公认和普遍接受的优良工程实践。它包含诸如ASME锅炉压力容器规范、API 510（容器）、API 570（管道）和API 653（储罐）等规范和标准，指导要素8下如何进行检查和测试。","related":[{"n":"2.5","t":"机械完整性与泄压"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"In the seven-step incident investigation process, what immediately follows the collection of evidence and facts?","options":["Closing the investigation and filing the report","Analyzing the facts to determine causal factors","Reporting the case to OSHA within 8 hours","Implementing corrective actions and tracking them"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The sequence is to secure the scene and provide care, gather evidence and facts, analyze the facts to determine causal factors, then develop corrective actions and track them to closure. Analysis must precede corrective actions, otherwise the organization is guessing at remedies. Reporting obligations run in parallel from the moment of the incident but are not the next analytical step.\n\n正确的顺序是：保护现场并提供救治、收集证据与事实、分析事实以确定致因、制定并跟踪纠正措施直至关闭。分析必须先于纠正措施，否则组织只是在猜测补救办法。报告义务从事故发生时即并行启动，但不是分析流程的下一步。","related":[{"n":"7.2","t":"七步调查流程"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"ANSI/ASSP Z10.0 explicitly requires which approach as the primary method for reducing risks?","options":["Higher insurance coverage","The hierarchy of controls","Employee disciplinary action","Zero-harm pledges"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A distinguishing feature of Z10.0 is its explicit, prescriptive requirement to use the hierarchy of controls as the primary risk-reduction approach — starting with elimination and substitution before administrative controls and PPE. ISO 45001 references the hierarchy but Z10.0 mandates it as primary.\n\nZ10.0的标志性特征是其明确、规定性地要求将控制层级作为降低风险的主要方法——在行政控制和PPE之前先考虑消除和替代。ISO 45001引用控制层级，而Z10.0将其规定为主要方法。","related":[{"n":"5.2","t":"ANSI/ASSP Z10.0"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Under RCRA, which waste code designation applies to a waste that exhibits the characteristic of corrosivity?","options":["D001","D002","D003","F001"],"correct":1,"explanation":"D002 is the waste code for corrosivity (pH ≤2 or ≥12.5, or corrodes steel at >6.35 mm/year). D001 = ignitability, D002 = corrosivity, D003 = reactivity, F001 = listed waste (spent halogenated solvents).\n\nD002是腐蚀性的废物代码（pH≤2或≥12.5，或钢材腐蚀速率>6.35mm/年）。D001=可燃性，D002=腐蚀性，D003=反应性，F001=名录废物（废卤化溶剂）。","related":[{"n":"14.1","t":"SPCC泄漏预防控制与对策"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-14.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"NFPA 13 is the standard for:","options":["Life safety code","Portable fire extinguishers","Sprinkler system installation","Fire alarm systems"],"correct":2,"explanation":"NFPA 13 governs sprinkler system installation. NFPA 10 governs portable extinguishers; NFPA 72 governs fire alarms; NFPA 101 is the Life Safety Code.\n\nNFPA 13管辖喷淋系统安装。NFPA 10管辖便携式灭火器；NFPA 72管辖火灾报警；NFPA 101是生命安全规范。","related":[{"n":"13.6","t":"喷淋"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which step of the risk assessment process determines whether a risk is \"acceptable\" or requires action?","options":["Evaluation","Monitoring","Identification","Analysis"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Evaluation compares risk levels against acceptance criteria to judge acceptability. Identification finds hazards, analysis measures them, monitoring tracks changes — but judgment of acceptability happens in evaluation.\n\n评估将风险水平与接受标准比较来判断可接受性。识别找到危害，分析测量它们，监控跟踪变化——但可接受性判断发生在评估步骤。","related":[{"n":"9.2","t":"五步流程"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"What does the First Responder Awareness level under HAZWOPER authorize a responder to do?","options":["Recognize a hazardous release and notify authorities","Direct the response of other personnel","Plug a leaking drum","Contain a spill using dikes"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Awareness-level personnel are trained ONLY to recognize a hazardous release, notify the proper authorities, and take no further action. Defensive actions (containment) require Operations level; offensive actions (stopping) require Technician level.\n\n认知级人员仅接受培训以识别危险品泄漏、通知当局，不采取进一步行动。防御性行动（控制）需要操作级；进攻性行动（阻止）需要技术员级。","related":[{"n":"12.8","t":"HAZWOPER"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A process safety information (PSI) file for a covered process is being compiled. Which item is part of \"information on the technology of the process\"?","options":["The electrical area classification drawing","The P&ID showing all instruments","The maximum intended inventory of the process","The materials of construction of the reactor"],"correct":2,"explanation":"\"Technology of the process\" includes block flow diagrams, process chemistry, maximum intended inventory, and safe upper/lower operating limits. Materials of construction, P&IDs, and electrical classification are \"information on the equipment in the process.\"\n\n\"工艺技术\"包括方框流程图、工艺化学、最大预期存量以及安全上下限。构造材料、P&ID和电气分类属于\"工艺设备信息\"。","related":[{"n":"2.8","t":"工艺安全信息与流程图"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A safety professional wants to compare the lockout/tagout program against the best-in-class LOTO program in any industry. This is an example of:","options":["Functional benchmarking","Generic benchmarking","Internal benchmarking","Competitive benchmarking"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Functional benchmarking compares a specific function or process (like LOTO) against best-in-class performers, even from different industries. Competitive benchmarking compares against direct competitors. Internal benchmarking compares within the same organization. Generic benchmarking compares general processes.\n\n功能基准比较将特定功能或流程（如LOTO）与最佳表现者比较，甚至跨行业。竞争基准比较是与直接竞争对手比较。内部基准比较是在同一组织内比较。通用基准比较是通用流程的比较。","related":[{"n":"6.4","t":"基准比较"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"What type of insurance covers third-party bodily injury and property damage claims arising from business operations?","options":["Professional liability insurance","General liability insurance","Business interruption insurance","Workers' compensation insurance"],"correct":1,"explanation":"General liability insurance covers third-party claims for bodily injury, property damage, and personal injury. Workers' compensation covers employees (first party). Professional liability (E&O) covers professional negligence claims.\n\n一般责任险承保第三方人身伤害、财产损失和人身伤害索赔。工伤保险承保员工（第一方）。职业责任险（E&O）承保专业疏忽索赔。","related":[{"n":"11.7","t":"保险类型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A wastewater treatment sludge measures pH 12.8 on a calibrated meter. For RCRA purposes, how should the sludge be classified?","options":["Ignitable, because alkaline sludges can flash","Corrosive, because the pH is at or above 12.5","Reactive, because it will generate gas in the lagoon","Non-hazardous, because only acidic wastes are corrosive"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The corrosivity characteristic (D002) is met by aqueous wastes with pH less than or equal to 2, or greater than or equal to 12.5, or that corrode steel faster than 6.35 mm per year. A pH of 12.8 falls in the highly alkaline corrosive range. Ignitability is a flash-point or oxidizer property, reactivity covers instability and violent reaction, and corrosivity applies at both ends of the pH scale, not only to acids.\n\n腐蚀性特征（D002）适用于pH小于等于2或大于等于12.5的水性废物，或腐蚀钢材速率超过每年6.35毫米的废物。pH 12.8属于强碱性腐蚀范围。可燃性指闪点或氧化性，反应性指不稳定与剧烈反应，而腐蚀性在pH两端都适用，并非只针对酸性物质。","related":[{"n":"14.5","t":"资源保护与回收法案"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d5.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"At a hazardous waste site the atmosphere is immediately dangerous to life or health, but the contaminants are not absorbed through the skin. Which EPA/OSHA response PPE level provides the required protection?","options":["Level A, a fully encapsulating suit with SCBA","Level B, the highest level of respiratory protection with lesser skin protection","Level C, an air-purifying respirator with chemical-resistant clothing","Level D, ordinary work clothing with a hard hat and safety glasses"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Level B combines the highest available respiratory protection, such as SCBA or supplied air, with chemical-resistant clothing that provides less skin protection than a fully encapsulating suit. It is selected when the highest respiratory protection is needed but there is no significant skin absorption or splash hazard. Level A adds a fully encapsulating chemical protective suit, Level C uses an air-purifying respirator and is never acceptable in an IDLH atmosphere, and Level D is only a baseline work uniform.\n\nB级防护将可获得的最高呼吸防护（如自给式呼吸器或供气式呼吸器）与化学防护服相结合，但由于不是全封闭防护服，皮肤防护程度低于A级。当需要最高呼吸防护但不存在明显皮肤吸收或喷溅危害时选用B级。A级增加了全封闭化学防护服；C级使用过滤式呼吸器，绝不能用于IDLH环境；D级仅为基本工作服。","related":[{"n":"12.8","t":"危险废物作业与应急响应"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is a required PSI (Element 2) document that shows all piping, instruments, valves, control loops, and safety devices in detail?","options":["Site general arrangement drawing","Block Flow Diagram (BFD)","Process Flow Diagram (PFD)","Piping and Instrumentation Diagram (P&ID)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The P&ID is the most detailed diagram — it shows all piping, instruments, valves, control loops, and safety devices, and is essential for HAZOP, mechanical integrity, and troubleshooting. The PFD shows major equipment and balances; the BFD is a simplified block overview.\n\nP&ID是最详细的图——显示所有管道、仪表、阀门、控制回路和安全装置，对HAZOP、机械完整性和故障排除至关重要。PFD显示主要设备和平衡；BFD是简化的方框总览。","related":[{"n":"2.8","t":"工艺安全信息与流程图"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"In the context of legal liability, \"due diligence\" refers to:","options":["Conducting daily safety inspections only","Documenting every safety decision in writing","Taking all reasonable steps to prevent harm, which serves as a defense to negligence","Paying all insurance premiums on time"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Due diligence is exercising the level of judgment, care, prudence, and activity reasonably expected in the circumstances. In safety, demonstrating due diligence (reasonable prevention steps) is a defense against charges of negligence.\n\n尽职调查是尽到在特定情况下被合理期望的判断、注意、审慎和行动水平。在安全领域，证明尽到尽职调查（合理的预防措施）是针对过失指控的辩护理由。","related":[{"n":"8.8","t":"道德与法律"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A damaged sling was removed from the scene, stored in an unlocked maintenance cabinet, and handed to a testing lab two days later with no signatures recorded. What is the MOST significant consequence?","options":["The lab results will be inadmissible in every jurisdiction","The whole investigation must restart from the beginning","The chain of custody is broken, so the evidence can be challenged","The sling can no longer be tested by the laboratory"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Chain of custody is the documented, unbroken record of who handled the evidence, when, and for what purpose. Without signatures the sling could have been substituted, altered or contaminated, so its evidentiary weight collapses even if testing is still possible. Testing remains feasible and the investigation continues, but the physical evidence is now open to challenge.\n\n证据链是记录“谁在何时为何目的接触过证据”的连续书面记录。缺少签名意味着吊带可能被调换、改动或污染，即使仍可检测，其证据价值也已崩塌。检测依然可行、调查也应继续，但该物证已可被质疑。","related":[{"n":"7.3","t":"证据链"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which emergency type requires EVACUATION rather than shelter-in-place?","options":["An earthquake","A tornado approaching","A fire inside the building","An external chemical plume"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Fire inside the building always requires evacuation. A tornado requires shelter-in-place (interior room); an external chemical plume may require shelter-in-place with HVAC shut down; an earthquake requires drop-cover-hold, not evacuation.\n\n建筑物内火灾始终需要疏散。龙卷风需要就地避难（内部房间）；外部化学羽流可能需要关闭HVAC就地避难；地震需要伏地、掩护、抓牢，而非疏散。","related":[{"n":"12.1","t":"紧急类型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"The \"5\" in a likelihood scale labeled \"Almost Certain\" typically means the event occurs:","options":["Once in a lifetime","Once in 10 years","Multiple times per year","Once in 50 years"],"correct":2,"explanation":"A common 1-5 likelihood scale: 1 = less than once in 10 years, 2 = once in 5-10 years, 3 = once in 1-5 years, 4 = once per year, 5 = multiple times per year. Exact definitions vary by organization but must be defined before matrix use.\n\n常见1-5可能性量表：1 = 10年内少于一次，2 = 5-10年一次，3 = 1-5年一次，4 = 每年一次，5 = 每年多次。确切定义因组织而异，但使用矩阵前必须定义。","related":[{"n":"9.7","t":"JHA"},{"n":"9.4","t":"风险矩阵"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A designer is locating manual fire alarm pull stations in a new building. What are the maximum travel distances to the nearest pull station?","options":["75 ft in an unsprinklered building and 150 ft in a sprinklered building","100 ft in an unsprinklered building and 200 ft in a sprinklered building","400 ft in an unsprinklered building and 200 ft in a sprinklered building","200 ft in an unsprinklered building and 400 ft in a sprinklered building"],"correct":3,"explanation":"NFPA 72 permits up to 200 feet of travel to the nearest manual pull station in an unsprinklered building, and up to 400 feet where the building is protected by sprinklers because the sprinklers provide the primary detection. The shorter distances in the other options are not the code values, and the last option reverses the two figures. The logic is that a sprinklered building can tolerate longer travel because suppression begins automatically.\n\nNFPA 72允许在无喷淋建筑中到最近手动报警按钮的行走距离最远200英尺；在有喷淋保护的建筑中可放宽到400英尺，因为喷淋系统本身提供了主要探测功能。其他选项中的较短距离并非规范值，最后一个选项还把两个数字颠倒了。其逻辑是：有喷淋的建筑因自动灭火已启动，可容许更长的行走距离。","related":[{"n":"13.3","t":"火灾报警"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A failure mode has Severity = 5, Occurrence = 10, and Detection = 2. What is the RPN?","options":["500","100","50","17"],"correct":1,"explanation":"RPN = 5 x 10 x 2 = 100. Occurrence of 10 (almost inevitable) dominates this score. Note the trade-off: high occurrence with good detection (low D) still yields a high RPN.\n\nRPN = 5 x 10 x 2 = 100。发生频率10（几乎不可避免）主导了该得分。注意权衡：高发生频率配合良好检测（低D）仍产生高RPN。","related":[{"n":"10.2","t":"RPN"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"After implementing a corrective action in FMEA, what should the team do?","options":["Only update the severity rating","Nothing further is required","Close the FMEA immediately","Recompute the RPN to verify the risk is reduced"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The team recalculates the RPN after the action (\"revised RPN\") to verify effectiveness. If the revised RPN is still above threshold, further action is needed. Verification is a required FMEA step.\n\n团队在措施后重新计算RPN（\"修订后的RPN\"）以验证有效性。如果修订后的RPN仍高于阈值，需要进一步行动。验证是FMEA的必要步骤。","related":[{"n":"10.3","t":"工作表"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"What is the CORRECT order of the Continuous Improvement model stages (per Yates)?","options":["Materials → Design → Analysis → Delivery → Evaluation","Performance Analysis → Instructional Design → Materials Acquisition → Delivery → Evaluation & Feedback","Delivery → Evaluation → Analysis → Design → Materials","Design → Analysis → Evaluation → Materials → Delivery"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The Yates 5-step continuous improvement process is: (1) Performance Analysis, (2) Instructional Design, (3) Materials Acquisition, (4) Delivery, (5) Evaluation & Feedback — which loops back to Performance Analysis. This is the CI framework applied to EHS training.\n\nYates五步持续改进流程是：(1) 绩效分析，(2) 教学设计，(3) 材料获取，(4) 交付，(5) 评估与反馈——反馈回到绩效分析。这是应用于EHS培训的CI框架。","related":[{"n":"19.3","t":"ADDIE模型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which of the following is a MITIGATIVE (recovery) barrier in a bow-tie?","options":["A preventive maintenance program","Corrosion-resistant pipe material","Operator training on procedures","An emergency isolation/depressurization system activated after a leak"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Emergency isolation/depressurization acts AFTER the top event (loss of containment) to reduce consequences — a mitigative barrier. Corrosion-resistant material, training, and maintenance all act BEFORE the top event to prevent it.\n\n紧急隔离/泄压系统在顶事件（围堵失效）之后起作用以减轻后果——减缓性屏障。耐腐蚀材料、培训和维护都在顶事件之前起作用以预防它。","related":[{"n":"11.4","t":"Bow-Tie"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Under the OSHA noise standard (5-dB exchange rate), what is the maximum allowable exposure time at 105 dBA?","options":["1 hour","0.5 hour","2 hours","4 hours"],"correct":0,"explanation":"T = 8 ÷ 2^((L − 90)/5) = 8 ÷ 2^(15/5) = 8 ÷ 2³ = 8 ÷ 8 = 1 hour. Every 5 dBA above 90 dBA halves the allowed time: 90 dBA gives 8 h, 95 dBA 4 h, 100 dBA 2 h, and 105 dBA 1 h. The 2-hour option is the value for 100 dBA, and 0.5 hour would correspond to 110 dBA.\n\nT = 8 ÷ 2^((L − 90)/5) = 8 ÷ 2^(15/5) = 8 ÷ 2³ = 1 小时。90 dBA 以上每增加 5 dBA，允许时间减半：90 dBA 为 8 小时、95 dBA 为 4 小时、100 dBA 为 2 小时、105 dBA 为 1 小时。2 小时对应的是 100 dBA，0.5 小时对应 110 dBA。","related":[{"n":"17.2","t":"噪声计算"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d6.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A 12-inch diameter duct carries air at 2,000 fpm. What is the volumetric flow rate?","options":["24,000 cfm","15,700 cfm","3,140 cfm","1,570 cfm"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Q = V × A. Radius = 6 inches = 0.5 ft. Area = π × r² = 3.1416 × 0.25 = 0.7854 ft². Q = 2,000 fpm × 0.7854 ft² = 1,571 cfm (approximately 1,570 cfm). Convert diameter to radius in feet first.\n\nQ = V × A。半径 = 6英寸 = 0.5英尺。面积 = π × r² = 3.1416 × 0.25 = 0.7854平方英尺。Q = 2,000 fpm × 0.7854平方英尺 = 1,571 cfm（约1,570 cfm）。先将直径转换为以英尺为单位的半径。","related":[{"n":"18.3","t":"人因工程风险因素与CTDs/MSDs"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-18.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A worker must tie off to a structural steel beam, and the lanyard will contact the beam's edge during a fall. What must the safety professional verify?","options":["That the lanyard is rated for sharp edges, or an edge protector is used","That the lanyard is made of wire rope instead of webbing","That the worker uses a body belt rather than a harness","That the anchorage is at least 12 feet above the D-ring"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Standard webbing can be cut by a sharp edge under fall loads, so the connector must be certified for sharp-edge conditions or protected with an abrasion-resistant cover. Wire rope is not automatically acceptable, and body belts are prohibited for fall arrest. Anchorage height affects free fall and clearance, not edge protection.\n\n普通织带在坠落荷载下可能被锐边割断，因此连接器必须通过锐边条件认证，或加装耐磨护套。钢丝绳并不自动符合要求，身体腰带则禁止用于防坠。锚点高度影响自由坠落与净空，与锐边防护无关。","related":[{"n":"3.4","t":"坠落间隙与PFAS计算"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following is NOT an element of the chain of custody?","options":["The value of the damaged equipment","Unique identifier for each evidence item","Documented transfers with signatures and dates","Secure storage of evidence"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Chain of custody elements include unique identifiers, documented transfers, signatures, dates, and secure storage. The value of damaged equipment is relevant to cost estimation, not to evidence integrity.\n\n证据链要素包括唯一标识符、文件化移交、签名、日期和安全保管。受损设备的价值与成本估算相关，与证据完整性无关。","related":[{"n":"7.3","t":"证据收集与证据链"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"In a Bow-Tie diagram, the \"top event\" represents:","options":["The final consequence","The initiating event","The root cause","The moment when control over the hazard is lost"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The top event is the central \"knot\" — the loss-of-control moment (e.g., loss of containment, structural collapse). Threats lead INTO it; consequences flow OUT of it. It is not a cause or a consequence.\n\n顶事件是中心\"结\"——失控时刻（如围堵失效、结构坍塌）。威胁导向它；后果从它流出。它不是原因或后果。","related":[{"n":"11.4","t":"Bow-Tie"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A worker is exposed to 91 dBA. Using the NIOSH formula (3-dB exchange rate), what is the allowable exposure time?","options":["8 hours","6 hours","4 hours","2 hours"],"correct":2,"explanation":"T = 8 / 2^((91-85)/3) = 8 / 2^(6/3) = 8 / 2^2 = 8/4 = 4 hours. Note that NIOSH is more protective — OSHA would allow T = 8 / 2^((91-90)/5) = 8/2^0.2 ≈ 7 hours.\n\nT = 8 / 2^((91-85)/3) = 8 / 2^(6/3) = 8 / 2^2 = 8/4 = 4小时。注意NIOSH更具保护性——OSHA允许T = 8 / 2^((91-90)/5) = 8/2^0.2 ≈ 7小时。","related":[{"n":"17.1","t":"噪声监管标准"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"The biggest drop-off in training effectiveness typically occurs between which two Kirkpatrick levels?","options":["Level 4 and Level 5","Level 1 and Level 2","Level 2 and Level 3","Level 3 and Level 4"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The greatest drop-off is between Level 2 (Learning) and Level 3 (Behavior). Learners acquire knowledge in training, but without management reinforcement, coaching, and a supportive culture, the behavior never transfers to the job.\n\n最大衰减发生在第2级（学习）和第3级（行为）之间。学习者在培训中获得了知识，但没有管理层强化、辅导和支持性文化，行为就无法转移到工作中。","related":[{"n":"20.5","t":"Kirkpatrick四级评估"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A post-training test shows 95% of participants passed, but observations 3 months later show workers are not following the trained procedures. The MOST likely explanation is:","options":["The training was too long","The instructor was unqualified","The test was too difficult","Learning (Level 2) occurred but did not transfer to behavior (Level 3)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"This is the classic Level 2 → Level 3 gap: learning occurred (test passed) but behavior did not change on the job. Causes include lack of management reinforcement, no coaching, workplace culture, or inadequate tools/resources. The training evaluation must measure behavior, not just knowledge.\n\n这是典型的第2级→第3级差距：学习发生了（测试通过）但工作行为没有改变。原因包括缺乏管理强化、无辅导、工作场所文化或工具/资源不足。培训评估必须衡量行为，而不仅仅是知识。","related":[{"n":"19.6","t":"SMART培训目标"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"An organization decides to stop producing a hazardous chemical product line entirely. This is an example of which risk strategy?","options":["Risk transfer","Risk retention","Risk avoidance","Risk sharing"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Stopping the activity that generates the risk is risk avoidance — the most definitive strategy, equivalent to elimination in the hierarchy of controls. The hazard and its risk are removed entirely.\n\n停止产生风险的活动是风险规避——最彻底的战略，相当于控制层级中的消除。危害及其风险被完全移除。","related":[{"n":"9.5","t":"控制层级"},{"n":"9.6","t":"ALARP与风险接受"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which fire detector is MOST appropriate for a commercial kitchen where smoke detectors cause nuisance alarms?","options":["Fixed-temperature heat detector","UV flame detector","Ionization smoke detector","Photoelectric smoke detector"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Heat detectors (fixed temperature or rate-of-rise) are used where smoke detectors would give nuisance alarms — kitchens, dusty areas, garages. A fixed-temperature detector activates only when the temperature reaches its set point.\n\n热探测器（定温或差温）用于烟雾探测器会误报的区域——厨房、多尘区域、车库。定温探测器仅在温度达到设定点时启动。","related":[{"n":"13.3","t":"NFPA72"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following belongs to the equipment information block of process safety information?","options":["Piping and instrumentation diagrams and the area electrical classification","The flash point and boiling point of the process chemical","The maximum intended inventory of the process","The process chemistry and the reaction kinetics"],"correct":0,"explanation":"PSI has three blocks: chemical hazard information, process technology information, and equipment information. P&IDs, materials of construction, electrical classification, relief system design basis, and safety systems belong to the equipment block. Flash point, inventory, and reaction chemistry belong to the chemical and technology blocks.\n\nPSI 分为三块：化学品危害信息、工艺技术信息与设备信息。P&ID、构造材料、电气分类、泄压系统设计依据与安全系统属于设备信息块。闪点、最大预期存量与反应化学属于化学品与工艺技术块。","related":[{"n":"2.8","t":"工艺安全信息与流程图"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Under OSHA 1910.1030 (Bloodborne Pathogens), retraining is required:","options":["Only at initial hire","Every 3 years","Annually","Every 5 years"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Bloodborne pathogens training is required at the time of initial assignment and annually thereafter. It must cover epidemiology, the exposure control plan, PPE, the HBV vaccine, and post-exposure procedures.\n\n血源性病原体培训要求在上岗时进行，此后每年一次。必须涵盖流行病学、暴露控制计划、PPE、HBV疫苗和暴露后程序。","related":[{"n":"20.7","t":"OSHA培训要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"In the Continuous Improvement model for training (per Yates/CSP11), which stage comes FIRST?","options":["Instructional design","Materials acquisition","Delivery","Performance analysis"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The Yates 5-step continuous improvement process begins with Performance Analysis — identifying performance gaps through data (incident rates, audits, observations, regulatory changes) and determining whether training is the correct solution. Only then does instructional design begin.\n\nYates五步持续改进流程从绩效分析开始——通过数据（事故率、审核、观察、法规变更）识别绩效差距，并确定培训是否是正确的解决方案。只有在此之后才开始教学设计。","related":[{"n":"19.2","t":"ANSI/ASSP Z490.1标准"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-19.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"Under SPCC, monthly visual inspections of oil storage containers and piping must be documented and records maintained for how long?","options":["3 years","5 years","1 year","2 years"],"correct":0,"explanation":"SPCC requires monthly visual inspections with records maintained for 3 years. Other recordkeeping periods to remember: noise exposure records = 2 years; audiometric test records = duration of employment plus 30 years.\n\nSPCC要求每月目视检查并保存记录3年。其他需记住的记录保存期：噪声暴露记录=2年；听力测试记录=雇佣期加30年。","related":[{"n":"14.7","t":"危险物质运输与应急响应"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-14.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"A reporter obtains the personal mobile number of the shipping supervisor and calls him directly for comment on a chemical release. The supervisor knows only that a tank was being unloaded when the alarm sounded. What should he do?","options":["Politely refer the reporter to the designated spokesperson and say nothing further","Hang up without speaking and report the call to security","Give his personal account of what he saw so the company appears responsive","Speculate about the likely cause but ask not to be quoted by name"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Only the designated, trained spokesperson is authorized to speak for the organization, and all other employees refer media inquiries to that person. A supervisor who improvises or speculates can create statements the company must later retract and can prejudice the incident investigation or legal position. A polite referral with no further comment follows the protocol; hanging up or offering personal speculation does not.\n\n只有被指定并受过培训的发言人有权代表组织发言，其他员工应把媒体询问转交给他。主管若即兴发言或猜测，会产生公司日后不得不撤回的表述，并可能影响事故调查或法律立场。礼貌转交且不再多说符合规定；直接挂断或提供个人猜测都不符合。","related":[{"n":"12.7","t":"危机沟通"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Which of the following is an engineering control for reducing MSD risk?","options":["Providing ergonomics training","Installing a mechanical lift assist device","Requiring workers to stretch before shifts","Job rotation among workers"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A mechanical lift assist (hoist, scissor lift, articulated arm) is an engineering control that physically removes the manual lifting hazard. Job rotation, training, and stretching are administrative controls. Engineering controls are preferred per the hierarchy.\n\n机械提升辅助装置（葫芦、剪叉式升降机、关节臂）是工程控制，物理消除人工提举危害。岗位轮换、培训和拉伸是行政控制。根据控制层级，工程控制优先。","related":[{"n":"18.3","t":"人因工程风险因素与CTDs/MSDs"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-18.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A construction contractor decides not to use GFCIs on temporary 120-V, 15-A and 20-A receptacles and instead implements an assured equipment grounding conductor program. What does that program require?","options":["Daily visual inspection plus continuity tests at least every three months","A grounding audit only after an employee reports a shock","Monthly visual inspection and annual continuity testing of cords","Continuity testing of every cord set once per year by the supplier"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The assured equipment grounding conductor program is the regulatory alternative to GFCIs and requires daily visual inspection of cord sets and plug-connected equipment plus continuity testing at intervals not exceeding three months. It also requires a written description of the program and recorded test results. Monthly or incident-driven testing does not meet the interval.\n\n“确保设备接地导体计划”（AEGCP）是 GFCI 的法规替代方案，要求对电源线组与插接设备每日目视检查，并至少每三个月做一次连续性测试，同时需有书面程序与测试记录。每月测试或事故后才测试不符合周期要求。","related":[{"n":"3.2","t":"电气安全工作条件"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"According to Herzberg's Two-Factor Theory, workplace safety is classified as:","options":["A self-actualization need at the top of the motivational hierarchy","A motivator (satisfier) that drives workers toward excellence","A hygiene factor (dissatisfier) — its absence causes dissatisfaction, but its presence alone does not motivate","Neither a hygiene factor nor a motivator — safety is outside Herzberg's framework"],"correct":2,"explanation":"In Herzberg's theory, safety (like working conditions, salary, and job security) is a hygiene factor. Its absence causes dissatisfaction, but simply providing a safe workplace does not actively motivate workers. To motivate, organizations must add motivators like recognition, responsibility, and meaningful involvement in safety.\n\n在赫茨伯格的理论中，安全（如同工作条件、薪资和工作保障）属于保健因素。其缺失会导致不满足，但仅提供安全的工作场所并不能主动激励工人。要激励，组织必须加入认可、责任和有意义的参与等激励因素。","related":[{"n":"8.3","t":"管理理论"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A process holds 1,700 gallons of a flammable liquid with a specific gravity of 0.75. Water weighs 8.34 lb per gallon. Is the process covered by PSM?","options":["Yes, because the inventory is about 10,600 lb, above the 10,000-lb threshold","No, because the inventory is about 8,000 lb, below the threshold","No, because the inventory is about 4,400 lb, below the threshold","Yes, but only if the liquid is stored above its normal boiling point"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Mass = 1,700 gal x 8.34 lb/gal x 0.75 = 10,634 lb, which exceeds the 10,000-lb threshold for flammable liquids in one location. Coverage depends on quantity; storage temperature matters only for the separate exception for atmospheric tanks kept below the boiling point. The process is therefore covered.\n\n质量 = 1,700 加仑 × 8.34 磅/加仑 × 0.75 = 10,634 磅，超过单一位置易燃液体 10,000 磅的阈限量。适用性取决于数量；储存温度只与常压储罐低于沸点储存的例外有关。因此该工艺适用 PSM。","related":[{"n":"2.1","t":"PSM概述"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which of the following ranking principles is correct for FMEA action priorities?","options":["Address highest RPN first, and always treat Severity = 9 or 10 as requiring action regardless of RPN","Address lowest RPN first to prevent failures","Severity is never considered in action priority","Only the RPN value matters"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Prioritize by RPN, but give special attention to any failure mode with Severity 9 or 10 (hazardous severity), which warrants action on its own. RPN alone can mask high-severity modes with low occurrence.\n\n按RPN排序，但特别关注任何严重性9或10（危险严重性）的失效模式，其本身就需要行动。仅凭RPN可能掩盖低发生频率的高严重性模式。","related":[{"n":"10.3","t":"工作表"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An ventilation upgrade costs 120,000 dollars and is expected to reduce respiratory claims and lost productivity by 45,000 dollars per year for five years. What is the five-year ROI?","options":["37.5 percent","75.0 percent","87.5 percent","187.5 percent"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Total benefit is 45,000 times 5, or 225,000 dollars. ROI equals (225,000 - 120,000) / 120,000, which is 105,000 divided by 120,000, or 87.5 percent. The 187.5 percent value divides total benefits by cost without subtracting the investment, and 37.5 percent divides the net gain by total benefits instead of by cost.\n\n总收益 = 45,000 × 5 = 225,000 美元。ROI =（225,000 − 120,000）÷ 120,000 = 105,000 ÷ 120,000 = 87.5%。187.5% 是用总收益除以成本而未扣除投资；37.5% 则是用净收益除以总收益而非除以成本。","related":[{"n":"8.2","t":"ROI 与回收期"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A factory loses $30,000 per day in revenue when shut down after a fire. The policy covering this lost income is:","options":["Workers' compensation","Property insurance","Business interruption insurance","General liability insurance"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Business interruption insurance covers lost income and continuing expenses when operations are suspended due to a covered event (like a fire). It is critical for business continuity planning.\n\n业务中断险承保因承保事件（如火灾）导致运营中断时的收入损失和持续费用。它对业务连续性规划至关重要。","related":[{"n":"11.7","t":"保险类型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"In a group lockout, each crew member should:","options":["Rely on the primary authorized employee's single lock","Affix their own personal lock to a group lockout mechanism (hasp or lockbox)","Place a tag on the equipment only","Leave the area without locking out"],"correct":1,"explanation":"In group LOTO, each authorized employee affixes their own personal lock to a group lockout device. The primary authorized employee applies the group lockout and verifies isolation. Individual crew members attach/detach their personal locks before/after their portion of the work. This ensures no one is exposed by a coworker's removal of the lock.\n\n在群体LOTO中，每名授权员工将个人锁具附加到群体上锁装置上。主要负责人施加群体锁具并验证隔离。各成员在工作开始前附上、结束后摘除个人锁具。这确保没有人因同事摘除锁具而暴露。","related":[{"n":"4.4","t":"上锁挂牌 (LOTO)"},{"n":"4.5","t":"LOTO人员职责与程序管理"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"What limitation do administrative controls and PPE share?","options":["Both are considered elimination-level controls","Both are ineffective for airborne exposures","Both are prohibited where engineering controls exist","Both depend on human behavior and fail when people do not comply"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Both rely on people doing something — following a procedure, or donning and maintaining equipment — so both degrade under time pressure, fatigue, and poor supervision. That shared dependence is why both rank below engineering controls. PPE additionally protects only the wearer, which administrative controls do not necessarily do.\n\n两者都依赖人去执行——遵守程序，或穿戴并维护装备——因此在时间压力、疲劳与监督不足时都会退化。这种对人的共同依赖，正是二者层级都低于工程控制的原因。PPE 还只保护佩戴者个人，行政控制则未必如此。","related":[{"n":"1.4","t":"行政控制与PPE"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"In a confined space entry, the attendant (authorized entrant monitor) may enter the space to attempt rescue ONLY when:","options":["The entrant calls for help","The attendant is trained, equipped, and has been relieved by another attendant","The space atmosphere is within acceptable limits","The entry supervisor verbally approves"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The attendant must remain outside the space and may never enter to attempt a rescue unless they are properly trained, equipped, and relieved by another attendant. Non-entry rescue (retrieval systems) is preferred. Untrained rescue attempts are the leading cause of multiple-fatality confined space incidents.\n\n监护员必须留在空间外，除非经过适当培训、配备装备并被另一名监护员接替，否则绝不得进入尝试救援。非进入救援（救援系统）是首选。未经培训的救援尝试是密闭空间多人死亡事故的首要原因。","related":[{"n":"4.3","t":"进入程序与救援"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-04.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A plant completed a risk assessment eight months ago and is now converting a batch mixing line to continuous operation. No incident has occurred and the insurance policy renews in June. What review action is required?","options":["No review until the insurance policy renews in June","A review only if the regulator or insurer requests one","Only the annual scheduled review, because no incident has occurred","A triggered review, because the process change can introduce hazards that were not assessed"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A change in process, equipment, or materials is a classic trigger for reviewing a risk assessment, independent of the annual cycle. A batch-to-continuous conversion changes inventories, control philosophy, and operator tasks, so new hazards are likely. Incident history, insurance dates, and regulator requests are not the controlling criteria.\n\n工艺、设备或材料变更本身就是复审风险评估的典型触发条件，与年度周期无关。间歇改连续会改变物料存量、控制方案和操作任务，很可能引入新危害。事故史、保险日期和监管要求都不是这里的决定因素。","related":[{"n":"9.9","t":"监控与沟通"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"The difference between inherent risk and residual risk is that:","options":["Inherent risk is measured before controls; residual risk is measured after controls","They are identical measurements","Residual risk is always higher than inherent risk","Inherent risk is measured after controls; residual risk is measured before controls"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Inherent (gross) risk is rated before considering existing controls; residual (net) risk is rated after accounting for existing controls. Residual risk should be lower than inherent risk when controls are effective.\n\n固有（毛）风险在考虑现有控制前评级；残余（净）风险在计入现有控制后评级。当控制有效时，残余风险应低于固有风险。","related":[{"n":"9.8","t":"风险登记册"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A manufacturer audits a key supplier's safety program before awarding a contract. This is an example of a:","options":["Second-party audit","Third-party audit","Management review","First-party audit"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A second-party audit is conducted by an organization on its suppliers, contractors, or other external parties. Its purpose is to evaluate supplier capability and ensure the supply chain meets safety expectations before contracts are awarded or renewed.\n\n二方审核由组织对其供应商、承包商或其他外部方实施。其目的是在授予或续签合同前评估供应商能力并确保供应链符合安全期望。","related":[{"n":"5.4","t":"审核类型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"What is the minimum required frequency for a permit-space rescue team to practice actual permit space rescues?","options":["Once every six months","Once every two years","At least once every 12 months","Once every three months"],"correct":2,"explanation":"1910.146(k)(2)(iv) requires rescue team members to practice permit space rescues at least once every 12 months, using the actual configuration and equipment. Practice must simulate a real rescue rather than a walkthrough. Non-entry rescue with a retrieval system is preferred whenever it is feasible.\n\n1910.146(k)(2)(iv) 要求救援队成员至少每 12 个月进行一次许可空间救援演练，并使用实际的空间配置与装备。演练必须模拟真实救援，而不是走流程。在可行时应优先采用救援绳系统的非进入救援。","related":[{"n":"4.3","t":"进入程序与救援"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A cold storage facility keeps more than the threshold quantity of anhydrous ammonia in its refrigeration system. Which Clean Air Act requirement applies?","options":["A Premanufacture Notice to EPA before the ammonia is first delivered","Registration under RCRA Subtitle I as an underground storage tank","A Title V operating permit only, with no separate risk program","A Risk Management Program with hazard assessment, prevention, and emergency response elements submitted to EPA"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Section 112(r) of the Clean Air Act and 40 CFR 68 require facilities holding more than a threshold quantity of a regulated substance such as anhydrous ammonia to develop a Risk Management Program covering hazard assessment including worst-case release analysis, a prevention program, and an emergency response program, and to submit it to EPA with periodic updates. A Title V permit addresses air emissions rather than accidental release prevention. The Premanufacture Notice belongs to TSCA for new chemicals, and Subtitle I applies to underground storage tanks.\n\n《清洁空气法》第112(r)条与40 CFR 68要求，持有超过阈值数量的受管物质（如无水氨）的设施必须建立风险管理计划，包括危害评估（含最坏情形泄漏分析）、预防计划和应急响应计划，并提交EPA且定期更新。第五章运营许可证针对的是大气排放，而非事故性泄漏预防。制造前通知属于TSCA对新化学品的要求，I子章适用于地下储罐。","related":[{"n":"15.4","t":"清洁空气法与清洁水法"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d5.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"An arc flash is best described as:","options":["A short circuit that is always harmless below 120 volts","A direct electrical shock through the body","An extreme heat and light event from an electrical fault that ionizes the air into a conducting arc","A lightning strike on the facility"],"correct":2,"explanation":"An arc flash is the heat and light produced by an electrical fault that ionizes the air into a conducting arc. Incident energy (in cal/cm²) determines the burn severity and required PPE. Arc blast is the pressure wave that can follow.\n\n弧闪是电气故障电离空气形成导电电弧时产生的热和光。入射能量（cal/cm²）决定烧伤严重性和所需PPE。弧爆是可能随之而来的压力波。","related":[{"n":"3.1","t":"NFPA 70E概述"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following is an example of a \"vital few\" finding from a Pareto analysis?","options":["Reporting all hazards to the regulatory agency","Applying the same inspection frequency to every department","A safety program focusing equally on all 20 hazard categories","Identifying that 80% of injuries stem from 3 of 15 hazard categories and targeting those first"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Pareto analysis identifies the \"vital few\" causes (often 20% of causes producing 80% of effects). Targeting those few causes first maximizes the impact of limited safety resources — this is the purpose of the 80/20 principle.\n\n帕累托分析识别\"关键少数\"原因（通常是20%的原因产生80%的结果）。首先针对少数原因可在有限的安全资源下实现最大影响——这就是80/20原则的目的。","related":[{"n":"6.8","t":"帕累托分析与数据展示"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A chemical plant conducts a PHA using HAZOP on a reactor system. For each deviation identified, the team must document all of the following EXCEPT:","options":["Likely causes of the deviation","Consequences of the deviation","Existing safeguards that prevent or mitigate the deviation","The salary grades of the team members involved"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A HAZOP records causes, consequences, existing safeguards, risk ratings, and recommended actions for each deviation. Personnel salary is not relevant to hazard analysis documentation.\n\nHAZOP对每个偏差记录原因、后果、现有防护措施、风险等级和推荐行动。人员薪资与危害分析记录无关。","related":[{"n":"2.4","t":"PHA与HAZOP深入"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"According to McGregor, Theory X managers assume that workers:","options":["Should participate in all safety decisions","Are self-motivated and seek responsibility","Inherently dislike work, need close supervision, and are motivated by punishment/reward","Are always motivated by recognition"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Theory X assumes workers inherently dislike work, need close supervision, and respond to punishment/reward — leading to authoritarian management. Theory Y assumes workers are self-motivated and seek responsibility — leading to participative management.\n\nX理论假设工人天性厌恶工作、需要密切监督、由惩罚/奖励驱动——导致专制式管理。Y理论假设工人自我激励并寻求责任——导致参与式管理。","related":[{"n":"8.3","t":"管理理论"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following is TRUE about a VPP-approved worksite?","options":["It no longer needs to keep OSHA injury records","It receives automatic ISO 45001 certification","It is exempt from all OSHA inspections forever","It is removed from OSHA's programmed inspection list, but OSHA still responds to complaints, fatalities, and catastrophes"],"correct":3,"explanation":"VPP sites are removed from programmed (routine scheduled) inspection lists, but OSHA still investigates complaints, fatalities, and catastrophes. VPP does not exempt the site from recordkeeping or from responding to OSHA inquiries.\n\nVPP场所从计划（例行安排）检查列表中移除，但OSHA仍会调查投诉、死亡和灾难。VPP不免除现场的记录义务或对OSHA问询的回应义务。","related":[{"n":"8.7","t":"VPP"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-08.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"What is a key limitation of transferring risk through insurance?","options":["Insurance completely eliminates the hazard from the workplace","Insurance transfers financial responsibility but not legal liability or reputational consequences","Insurance is only available for workers' compensation claims","Insurance transfers the legal obligation to provide a safe workplace"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Risk transfer shifts the financial burden of losses but NOT the moral/legal responsibility for safety, regulatory consequences (OSHA citations), or reputational damage. The organization remains accountable for safety regardless of coverage.\n\n风险转移转移了损失的财务负担，但不转移安全方面的道德/法律责任、监管后果（OSHA处罚）或声誉损害。无论覆盖范围如何，组织仍对安全负责。","related":[{"n":"11.7","t":"保险类型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"A trainer lets each crew choose which of two incident scenarios to work through and how to divide the roles, and asks them to set their own practice goals. Which andragogical assumption is being applied?","options":["Self-concept: self-directed learning","Need to know: relevance comes first","Readiness: timing to a real need","Orientation: problem-centered content"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Self-concept states that adults prefer to be self-directed rather than dependent, so effective design offers choices, involves learners in planning, and uses discovery. Need to know concerns explaining why the topic matters; readiness concerns timing relative to a real need; orientation concerns problem-centred content. Offering choice and self-set goals is the hallmark of self-direction.\n\n自我概念假设认为成人倾向于自我导向而非依赖，因此有效设计应提供选择、让学习者参与规划并采用发现式活动。学习需求涉及解释主题为何重要；学习准备度涉及与实际需求出现的时机；学习取向涉及以问题为中心的内容。提供选择和自设目标正是自我导向的标志。","related":[{"n":"20.1","t":"成人学习理论"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d7.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A guardrail top rail must withstand a force of at least 200 pounds applied:","options":["Only at the mid-point of the rail","Within 2 inches of the top edge, in any outward or downward direction","At any point along the rail, in any direction including upward","Only at the posts where the rail is attached"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The top rail must withstand at least 200 pounds of force applied within 2 inches of the top edge, in any outward or downward direction, without deflecting below 39 inches. This ensures the rail functions as a barrier even under a fall load.\n\n顶部横杆必须能承受在顶部边缘2英寸内、沿任意向外或向下方向施加的至少200磅力，且不得偏斜至39英寸以下。这确保横杆在坠落载荷下仍能发挥屏障作用。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which of the following is an example of a STRUCK-BY hazard?","options":["A worker is hit by a swinging crane load","A worker falls through an unprotected skylight","A worker contacts an energized conductor","A worker is trapped in a trench cave-in"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Struck-by means being hit by a flying, falling, swinging, or rolling object — a swinging crane load is a classic example. Trench cave-in is caught-in/between; a skylight fall is a fall hazard; contact with energized parts is electrocution.\n\n撞击指被飞行、坠落、摆动或滚动的物体击中——摆动的起重机负载是典型示例。沟槽坍塌是卷入/挤压；天窗坠落是坠落危害；接触带电部件是触电。","related":[{"n":"3.9","t":"CSP11常见工作场所危害"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Why is a rupture disc sometimes installed immediately upstream of a safety relief valve?","options":["To isolate the valve from corrosive or fouling fluid and provide a tight seal","To raise the relief valve's set pressure above the vessel design pressure","To allow the relief valve to reclose faster after it has lifted","To eliminate the need for mechanical integrity inspection of the valve"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The disc shields the valve internals from corrosive, polymerizing, or solids-laden fluid and gives a bubble-tight seal, which extends valve life and reduces leakage. The trade-off is that the disc must be replaced after it bursts and the combination must be sized as a system. It does not change the set pressure or remove inspection obligations.\n\n爆破片保护阀门内部免受腐蚀性、易聚合或含固介质影响，并提供严密密封，从而延长阀门寿命、减少泄漏。代价是爆破后必须更换，且组合系统需整体定尺。它不改变设定压力，也不能免除检验义务。","related":[{"n":"2.5","t":"机械完整性与泄压"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which statement is MOST appropriate for the findings section of an incident investigation report?","options":["The incident was unavoidable given the tight production schedule","The operator failed to follow the written procedure because he is careless","The jam-clearing task had no isolation step, and 2 of 5 operators cleared jams live","The department has a poor safety culture overall, which explains it"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Findings should state verifiable facts, including the condition found and the supporting evidence, so that corrective actions can be traced to them. Blaming an individual, labeling culture and declaring an event unavoidable are conclusions without evidence that close off analysis. Quantified observations such as two of five operators interviewed also show the condition is systemic rather than isolated.\n\n发现部分应陈述可核实的事实，包括所发现的条件及其支撑证据，使纠正措施可以追溯到这些事实。指责个人、给文化贴标签、宣称事故不可避免，都是缺乏证据的结论，会切断后续分析。诸如“访谈的5名操作工中有2人”这样的量化描述，还能说明该条件是系统性的而非孤例。","related":[{"n":"7.2","t":"七步调查流程"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Which of the following is considered a lagging indicator of safety performance?","options":["Number of hazard assessments completed","Workers' compensation claim rate","Number of employees attending safety training","Percentage of work orders completed safely"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Workers' compensation claim rate is a lagging indicator — it measures the outcome of past incidents. Completing work orders, hazard assessments, and safety training are all leading indicators that measure proactive activities.\n\n工伤保险索赔率是滞后指标——它衡量过去事故的结果。完成工作单、危害评估和安全培训都是衡量主动活动的领先指标。","related":[{"n":"6.1","t":"领先指标与滞后指标"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"The LD50 of a chemical is 4 mg/kg. This substance would be classified as:","options":["Super toxic","Very toxic","Moderately toxic","Extremely toxic"],"correct":0,"explanation":"LD50 < 5 mg/kg = super toxic (超毒). The classification scale: super toxic <5, extremely toxic 5-50, very toxic 50-500, moderately toxic 500-5,000, slightly toxic 5,000-15,000, practically non-toxic >15,000 (all mg/kg).\n\nLD50 < 5 mg/kg = 超毒。分类尺度：超毒<5，极毒5-50，剧毒50-500，中等毒性500-5,000，微毒5,000-15,000，基本无毒>15,000（单位均为mg/kg）。","related":[{"n":"17.5","t":"非电离辐射"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Construction workers are on a low-slope roof doing roofing work. The employer uses a warning line system as fall protection. At what minimum distance from the roof edge must the warning line be erected?","options":["15 feet","4 feet","6 feet","10 feet"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Warning lines for roofing work on low-slope roofs must be erected at least 6 feet from the roof edge. When mechanical equipment is in use, the warning line must be at least 6 feet from the roof edge in the direction the equipment is being operated, and 10 feet from the edge perpendicular to that direction. The warning line must be flagged every 6 feet and must withstand 16 pounds of force.\n\n低坡度屋顶屋面工作的警示线必须设立在距屋顶边缘至少6英尺处。使用机械设备时，在设备操作方向，警示线必须距屋顶边缘至少6英尺，垂直方向距边缘10英尺。警示线必须每6英尺挂旗标识，必须承受16磅力。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"},{"n":"3.5","t":"附加坠落防护要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A worker is exposed to two solvents with similar target organ effects. The TWA concentrations are 60 ppm for Solvent A (PEL = 100 ppm) and 25 ppm for Solvent B (PEL = 50 ppm). Using the mixture formula, does this exceed the PEL?","options":["Yes, E_m = 1.10 — exceeds the limit","No, E_m = 0.60 — within the limit","Yes, E_m = 1.25 — exceeds the limit","No, E_m = 0.85 — within the limit"],"correct":0,"explanation":"E_m = C_A/PEL_A + C_B/PEL_B = 60/100 + 25/50 = 0.60 + 0.50 = 1.10. Since E_m > 1.0, the mixture exceeds the permissible exposure limit, even though each substance individually is below its PEL.\n\nE_m = C_A/PEL_A + C_B/PEL_B = 60/100 + 25/50 = 0.60 + 0.50 = 1.10。由于E_m > 1.0，混合物超过了允许暴露限值，即使每种物质单独来看都低于各自的PEL。","related":[{"n":"16.2","t":"工业卫生危害因素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-16.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"An auditor samples 60 of 240 training files and finds that 9 files are missing the annual refresher record. If the sample is representative, what is the sample nonconformity rate and the projected number of deficient files in the full population?","options":["9 percent, about 22 files","15 percent, about 36 files","25 percent, about 60 files","6 percent, about 14 files"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The sample rate is 9 divided by 60, which equals 0.15 or 15 percent. Projecting to the population: 0.15 times 240 equals 36 deficient files. Nine percent is the raw count reported as a percentage, and 25 percent is the fraction of the population sampled, not the error rate.\n\n样本不符合率 = 9 ÷ 60 = 0.15，即15%；推算总体 = 0.15 × 240 = 36 份。9% 是把发现数量直接当百分比，25% 是抽样比例而非错误率。抽样结论只有在样本具有代表性时才能外推，这一点应在报告中说明。","related":[{"n":"5.4","t":"审核类型"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A welder on a steel beam wears a body belt attached to a short lanyard so he can lean back and use both hands while working. Is this acceptable?","options":["Yes; a body belt may serve as the fall arrest system if the lanyard is 2 feet or shorter","No; body belts are prohibited in all construction work","No; body belts may only be used with a self-retracting lifeline","Yes, for positioning, provided a separate fall arrest system protects him against a fall"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Body belts are prohibited for fall arrest but may still be used for positioning, which supports a worker with both hands free. Because positioning systems are not designed to arrest a fall, a separate fall arrest system or other fall protection is required. A belt plus a short lanyard alone is not fall protection.\n\n身体腰带禁止用于防坠，但可用于定位，使工人双手自由作业。定位装置并非为制动坠落而设计，因此必须另有防坠系统或其他坠落防护。仅靠腰带加短系索不构成防坠落保护。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"},{"n":"3.4","t":"坠落间隙与PFAS计算"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A facility wants to measure personal exposure to a solvent vapor using passive diffusion badges. The work area has large circulation fans that keep air moving across the workers at roughly 150 fpm. What is the PRIMARY concern?","options":["Badges only measure peak concentrations, not averages","Badges require a pump, which the fans would disturb","Air movement alters the uptake rate, so results may be biased","Badges cannot be worn in areas with organic vapors"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Passive badges rely on diffusion at a rate derived from Fick's law, calibrated for a quiescent air boundary layer. High face velocity can thin that layer and change the uptake rate, biasing the result, so active pump sampling is preferred in drafty areas. Badges need no pump, and they integrate exposure over time rather than measuring peaks.\n\n被动式徽章依靠菲克定律的扩散速率工作，标定时假设存在静止空气边界层。高面风速会减薄该边界层、改变吸收速率，使结果产生偏差，因此在气流大的区域应改用主动泵采样。徽章不需要泵，且是对时间积分而非测峰值。","related":[{"n":"16.4","t":"采样设备与方法"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d6.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which statement about the eight emergency types and the all-hazards approach is correct?","options":["The ERP is only required for nuclear facilities","The ERP cannot cover multiple emergencies","The ERP only needs to address fire","The ERP must address all applicable hazards using an all-hazards approach"],"correct":3,"explanation":"CSP11 requires the ERP to address all applicable emergency types — fire, severe weather, nuclear, natural disasters, terrorism, chemical spills, utilities, and cyber. This is the all-hazards approach; focusing only on fire is insufficient.\n\nCSP11要求ERP处理所有适用的紧急情况类型——火灾、恶劣天气、核、自然灾害、恐怖主义、化学品泄漏、公用设施和网络。这就是全灾害方法；只关注火灾是不够的。","related":[{"n":"12.1","t":"紧急类型"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-12.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Under the ALARP framework, a risk in the \"intolerable\" region requires:","options":["Only regular monitoring","Controls only if cost-effective","The activity must be stopped or mandatory controls implemented regardless of cost","No action because the risk is acceptable"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The intolerable region sits at the top of the ALARP triangle. Risks there cannot be justified under any circumstances — the activity must cease, or controls must be implemented regardless of cost. Tolerable-region risks require cost-benefit balancing.\n\n不可容忍区域位于ALARP三角形顶部。该区域的风险在任何情况下都无法合理化——活动必须停止，或必须不顾成本实施控制。可容忍区域的风险需要成本效益平衡。","related":[{"n":"9.6","t":"ALARP与风险接受"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-09.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A 4-foot-wide trench crosses a walkway that employees use to reach a warehouse. What is required?","options":["Nothing, because the trench is less than 5 feet deep","Only a warning sign at each end","Adequate bridges or walkways with standard guardrails","A competent person stationed at the crossing during shifts"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Where employees or equipment must cross over an excavation, adequate bridges or walkways with standard guardrails must be provided. Depth does not excuse the requirement, because a fall into a 4-foot trench still causes serious injury. Barricades and signs are required for excavations that are not readily seen, but they do not replace a crossing structure.\n\n当员工或设备必须跨越挖掘区域时，必须提供带标准护栏的足够桥梁或走道。深度不能免除该要求，因为跌入 4 英尺深的沟槽同样会造成严重伤害。不易被发现的挖掘需设路障与标识，但不能替代跨越结构。","related":[{"n":"4.7","t":"关键挖掘要求"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A worker's audiogram shows an average shift of 12 dB at 2,000, 3,000, and 4,000 Hz in the left ear compared to baseline. What is the employer's required action?","options":["No action — this is normal","Retest within 30 days to confirm the STS","Immediately remove the worker from the job","Provide new earmuffs within 90 days"],"correct":1,"explanation":"An average shift ≥10 dB at 2,000/3,000/4,000 Hz is a potential Standard Threshold Shift (STS). The employer must retest the worker within 30 days to confirm the STS. If confirmed, the worker must be fitted with hearing protection (or refitted/retrained) and the audiogram must be flagged in records.\n\n在2,000/3,000/4,000 Hz的平均偏移≥10 dB是潜在的标准阈值偏移（STS）。雇主必须在30天内重测以确认STS。如果确认，必须为工人适配听力保护（或重新适配/培训），并在记录中标记该听力图。","related":[{"n":"17.5","t":"非电离辐射"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-17.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"In the AREC framework, which phase involves conducting design reviews and Pre-Startup Safety Reviews (PSSRs) to predict hazards before they exist?","options":["Evaluate","Anticipate","Control","Recognize"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The Anticipate phase involves predicting potential hazards BEFORE they exist through activities such as design review, Prevention through Design (PtD), PSSR, review of SDS prior to chemical purchase, and Management of Change (MOC) review.\n\n预判阶段包括在危害存在之前通过设计审查、预防性设计（PtD）、PSSR、购买化学品前审查SDS以及变更管理（MOC）审查等活动预判潜在危害。","related":[{"n":"16.1","t":"AREC框架"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-16.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A facility stores 2,500 gallons of diesel in a single aboveground tank located inside a sealed concrete room with no floor drain. The site is three miles from any waterway and has no storm sewer connection or overland drainage pathway. Must the facility prepare an SPCC plan?","options":["No, because a discharge could not reasonably be expected to reach navigable waters","Yes, because any aboveground oil storage over 1,320 gallons always requires a plan","Yes, because diesel is a CERCLA hazardous substance at any quantity","No, because the tank is smaller than 5,000 gallons"],"correct":0,"explanation":"SPCC applies where a facility could reasonably be expected to discharge oil into navigable waters or adjoining shorelines; if there is no direct or indirect pathway, such as a sealed room with no drain and no overland route, a plan may not be required. The 1,320-gallon threshold is the capacity trigger, but it does not override the pathway analysis. The tank size is irrelevant to the rule once above 1,320 gallons, and the diesel quantity is far below any CERCLA reportable quantity basis for the plan.\n\nSPCC适用于可能合理预期会将油类排入通航水域或邻近岸线的设施；如果不存在直接或间接通道（例如无排水口的密闭房间且无地面径流路径），则可能无需制定计划。1,320加仑是容量触发值，但并不能取代通道分析。一旦超过1,320加仑，储罐大小与该规则的适用性无关，而该柴油量也远未达到CERCLA报告量的依据。","related":[{"n":"14.1","t":"泄漏预防与控制对策"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d5.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"Charcoal tubes are the standard collection medium for which category of contaminants?","options":["Asbestos fibers","Inorganic gases such as CO and NO₂","Organic vapors such as benzene, toluene, and methylene chloride","Metal fumes"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Activated charcoal sorbent tubes collect organic vapors (aromatic and chlorinated solvents). Silica gel tubes collect polar compounds (amines, alcohols); impingers collect reactive/inorganic gases (NH₃, acids). Metal fumes and fibers use filter cassettes.\n\n活性炭吸附管收集有机蒸气（芳香族和氯化溶剂）。硅胶管收集极性化合物（胺、醇）；吸收瓶收集反应性/无机气体（NH₃、酸）。金属烟尘和纤维使用滤膜夹。","related":[{"n":"16.7","t":"暴露评估策略与统计分析"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-16.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"The signal word \"Danger\" on a GHS label indicates:","options":["A more severe hazard than \"Warning\"","The chemical is non-hazardous","An environmental hazard only","A less severe hazard"],"correct":0,"explanation":"GHS uses \"Danger\" for the more severe hazard categories and \"Warning\" for the less severe categories. The signal word reflects the severity of the hazard.\n\nGHS对更严重的危害类别使用\"危险\"，对较不严重的类别使用\"警告\"。信号词反映危害的严重程度。","related":[{"n":"13.8","t":"HazCom"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-13.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A design team is asked to propose controls for a new carton-packing station where workers currently lift and twist 40-lb cases. Which proposal represents the HIGHEST level of the hierarchy that is still feasible?","options":["Install lift-assist arms at each packing position","Rotate packers every 30 minutes and train them in lifting technique","Redesign the line so cases are filled and sealed at floor level","Issue back belts and non-slip gloves to every packer"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Redesigning the line removes the manual handling task entirely, which is elimination and the highest feasible level. Lift-assist arms are an engineering control, rotation and training are administrative controls, and belts and gloves are PPE. Only after documenting that redesign is infeasible should the team settle for a lower level.\n\n重新设计生产线彻底取消了人工搬运，属于消除，是可行的最高层级。助力机械臂是工程控制，轮岗与培训是行政控制，护腰带与手套是 PPE。只有在记录证明重新设计不可行之后，才应退而选择较低层级。","related":[{"n":"1.8","t":"控制措施选择"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Using a 6-ft lanyard with a deceleration device, what is the approximate MINIMUM fall clearance required below the worker?","options":["10 feet","13.5 feet","20 feet","6.5 feet"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Total fall clearance = free fall (6 ft) + deceleration (3.5 ft) + harness stretch (1 ft) + D-ring slide (1 ft) + safety margin (2 ft) = 13.5 feet minimum. A conservative estimate for exam problems is 17.5–18.5 ft.\n\n总坠落净空 = 自由坠落（6英尺）+ 减速（3.5英尺）+ 安全带拉伸（1英尺）+ D型环滑动（1英尺）+ 安全系数（2英尺）= 最低13.5英尺。考试题的保守估算为17.5–18.5英尺。","related":[{"n":"3.4","t":"坠落间隙与PFAS计算"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Monthly incident counts at a site are: 4, 5, 5, 6, 8, 100 (one catastrophic event). Which measure of central tendency is MOST appropriate to report?","options":["Median = 5.5, because it is robust to the extreme outlier","Mode = 5, because it occurs most often","Range, because it captures variability","Mean = 21.3, because it uses all the data"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The median (5.5) is most appropriate because the value 100 is a rare catastrophic outlier that skews the mean (21.3). The median is unaffected by outliers and better represents the typical monthly incident count.\n\n中位数（5.5）最合适，因为值100是罕见的灾难性异常值，会使均值（21.3）偏斜。中位数不受异常值影响，更能代表典型的月度事故数。","related":[{"n":"6.6","t":"安全分析的统计基础"},{"n":"6.8","t":"帕累托分析与数据展示"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Under OSHA 1910.134 (Respiratory Protection), how often must respirator training and fit testing be conducted?","options":["Every 3 years","Only at initial hire","Every 2 years","Annually"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Respiratory protection training and quantitative or qualitative fit testing are required at least annually (1910.134). Fit testing must also be repeated whenever a change in facial features (weight gain/loss, dental changes) could affect the seal.\n\n呼吸防护培训和定量或定性适合性检验要求至少每年进行一次（1910.134）。每当面部特征变化（体重增减、牙齿变化）可能影响密封时，也必须重复适合性检验。","related":[{"n":"20.7","t":"OSHA培训要求"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"Which of the following is an example of an intrinsic motivator for adult learners?","options":["A cash bonus for completing the course","Job satisfaction and personal safety","Fear of termination","A certificate framed in the office"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Intrinsic motivators are internal — job satisfaction, self-esteem, quality of life, protecting one's health. Extrinsic motivators are external rewards (bonuses, certificates, avoiding punishment). Knowles emphasizes intrinsic motivation for adults.\n\n内在动机是内部的——工作满意度、自尊、生活质量、保护自身健康。外在动机是外部奖励（奖金、证书、避免惩罚）。诺尔斯强调成人的内在动机。","related":[{"n":"20.1","t":"Knowles成人学习理论"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"4","text":"Which sequence correctly describes the four steps for using a portable fire extinguisher?","options":["Squeeze, Pull, Aim, Sweep","Aim, Pull, Sweep, Squeeze","Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep","Pull, Aim, Sweep, Squeeze"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The PASS sequence is Pull the pin, Aim the nozzle at the base of the fire, Squeeze the handle, and Sweep the agent side to side across the base of the fire. Aiming at the base rather than the flames, and sweeping rather than holding one spot, are what actually extinguish the fire. The other sequences put the steps out of order, for example squeezing before aiming.\n\nPASS顺序为：拔销（Pull）、将喷嘴对准火焰根部（Aim）、压下压把（Squeeze）、左右横扫喷射（Sweep）。对准根部而不是火焰本身，并横扫而非固定一点，才真正能灭火。其他顺序把步骤颠倒了，例如先压把后瞄准。","related":[{"n":"13.5","t":"便携式灭火器"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d4.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Which PSM element is MOST directly responsible for preventing process equipment failure through inspections, testing, and preventive maintenance?","options":["Process Hazard Analysis","Employee Participation","Management of Change","Mechanical Integrity"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Mechanical Integrity (Element 8) maintains the ongoing integrity of process equipment through written procedures, training, inspections and tests per RAGAGEP, and quality assurance. MOC manages changes, PHA identifies hazards, and Employee Participation involves workers in the program.\n\n机械完整性（要素8）通过书面程序、培训、按RAGAGEP进行的检查和测试以及质量保证，维护工艺设备的持续完整性。MOC管理变更，PHA识别危害，员工参与让工人参与计划。","related":[{"n":"2.5","t":"机械完整性与泄压"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"At what height does OSHA require fall protection for employees on a walking-working surface in general industry?","options":["6 feet","10 feet","3 feet","4 feet"],"correct":3,"explanation":"General industry (29 CFR 1910.28) triggers fall protection at 4 feet. Construction (29 CFR 1926.501) triggers at 6 feet. This distinction between general industry (4 ft) and construction (6 ft) is a classic CSP exam item. Scaffolds require fall protection at 10 feet.\n\n一般工业（29 CFR 1910.28）在4英尺触发坠落防护。建筑（29 CFR 1926.501）在6英尺触发。一般工业（4英尺）和建筑（6英尺）之间的区别是CSP考试经典题目。脚手架在10英尺要求坠落防护。","related":[{"n":"3.3","t":"坠落防护"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-03.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"According to ISO 45001, management review must be conducted by:","options":["External consultants acting alone","The safety manager","The audit team","Top management"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Management review is the responsibility of top management. While the safety professional provides inputs (performance data, audit results, risk assessments), it is top management that reviews the system's suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness and makes decisions. This is a distinguishing feature vs. an audit.\n\n管理评审是最高管理层的职责。虽然安全专业人员提供输入（绩效数据、审核结果、风险评估），但由最高管理层评审体系的适宜性、充分性和有效性并做出决策。这是与审核相区别的特征。","related":[{"n":"5.5","t":"管理评审"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-05.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A sample of 5 noise measurements has values 4, 6, 8, 10, 12. What is the SAMPLE standard deviation?","options":["8.0","2.83","3.16","4.47"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Mean = 8. Sum of squared deviations = 16+4+0+4+16 = 40. Sample variance = 40/(n−1) = 40/4 = 10. Sample SD = √10 = 3.16. Note: 2.83 is the population SD (using n=5); the sample SD uses n−1 = 4.\n\n均值 = 8。离差平方和 = 16+4+0+4+16 = 40。样本方差 = 40/(n−1) = 40/4 = 10。样本标准差 = √10 = 3.16。注意：2.83是总体标准差（用n=5）；样本标准差用n−1 = 4。","related":[{"n":"6.6","t":"安全分析的统计基础"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-06.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under the Respiratory Protection standard (29 CFR 1910.134), respirators may be used only when:","options":["Feasible engineering controls are not sufficient or are being implemented","The hazard is classified as a nuisance dust","The employer has budgeted for them in the annual safety plan","The worker requests respiratory protection"],"correct":0,"explanation":"1910.134 requires that engineering controls (e.g., ventilation, enclosure, substitution) be used first; respirators are permitted when these controls are not feasible, are being implemented, or are insufficient to reduce exposure below the PEL. This mirrors the hierarchy: PPE after engineering.\n\n1910.134要求首先使用工程控制（如通风、封闭、替代）；当这些控制不可行、正在实施或不足以将暴露降至PEL以下时，才允许使用呼吸器。这体现了层级：先工程后PPE。","related":[{"n":"1.4","t":"行政控制与PPE"},{"n":"1.5","t":"关键OSHA标准"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-01.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A shift supervisor walks the production line at the start of every shift with a checklist that verifies guard presence, housekeeping and eyewash access. This activity is BEST classified as:","options":["An inspection","A third-party audit","A management review","A certification audit"],"correct":0,"explanation":"An inspection is a walk-through verification of physical conditions and practices against a checklist, and it is normally performed by line personnel as part of routine operations. An audit is a systematic, documented, independent evaluation of conformity against defined criteria, and it produces findings against management system requirements. Management review is a top-management evaluation of the system, and certification audits are performed by external bodies.\n\n检查（inspection）是依据检查表对现场物理条件和作业实践进行的巡视核实，通常由直线人员作为日常运营的一部分实施。审核（audit）是针对既定准则、系统化并有文件记录的独立符合性评价，产出针对体系要求的发现。管理评审是最高管理层对体系的评价，认证审核则由外部机构实施。","related":[{"n":"5.6","t":"审核与检查"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Which risk financing strategy is MOST appropriate for low-severity, high-frequency risks?","options":["Contractual indemnification","Risk retention","Risk transfer (insurance)","Risk avoidance"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Low-severity, high-frequency risks are best retained — insurance premiums would exceed expected losses (the claims would drive premiums up). High-severity, low-frequency risks are best transferred.\n\n低严重性、高频率风险最适合保留——保险费会超过预期损失（理赔会推高保费）。高严重性、低频率风险最适合转移。","related":[{"n":"11.6","t":"五大策略"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-11.html"},{"domain":"7","text":"The biggest barrier to achieving Kirkpatrick Level 3 (Behavior) results after training is:","options":["Insufficient pre-test scores","A work environment that does not reinforce new behaviors","Inadequate Level 1 reaction scores","Poor quality training materials"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Even excellent training fails at Level 3 if the post-training environment does not support behavior change. Without management reinforcement, coaching, accountability, and a supportive culture, new skills will not transfer to the job.\n\n即使培训非常出色，如果培训后环境不支持行为改变，第3级也会失败。没有管理层强化、辅导、问责和支持性文化，新技能将无法转移到工作中。","related":[{"n":"20.5","t":"Kirkpatrick四级评估"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-20.html"},{"domain":"5","text":"A company generates exactly 1 kg of a P-listed acute hazardous waste in a month along with 500 kg of non-acute hazardous waste. What is its generator status?","options":["VSQG","SQG","LQG","Conditionally exempt"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Generating more than 1 kg/month of acute hazardous (P-listed) waste automatically classifies the facility as an LQG, regardless of the total non-acute volume. The 1 kg acute threshold is an independent trigger for LQG status.\n\n每月产生超过1 kg急性危险（P名录）废物会自动将设施归类为LQG，无论非急性总量如何。1 kg急性阈值是LQG状态的独立触发条件。","related":[{"n":"15.4","t":"清洁空气法与清洁水法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-15.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"According to NIOSH fatigue research, what is the recommended power nap duration to improve alertness WITHOUT causing sleep inertia?","options":["15-20 minutes","45-60 minutes","2 hours","5 minutes"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A 15-20 minute power nap improves alertness without entering deep sleep. Naps longer than 45 minutes can cause sleep inertia (grogginess on awakening). Napping should complement, not replace, adequate nighttime sleep (7-9 hours).\n\n15-20分钟的打盹可提高警觉性而不会进入深睡眠。超过45分钟的小睡会导致睡眠惯性（醒来时昏昏沉沉）。小睡应补充而非替代充足的夜间睡眠（7-9小时）。","related":[{"n":"18.7","t":"局部排风LEV"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-18.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"The PSM emergency planning and response element requires the employer to do which of the following?","options":["Establish an emergency action plan per 1910.38(a) and small-release procedures","Rely entirely on the local fire department for all release response","Post the community emergency response plan at each process unit","Conduct a full-scale community evacuation drill every year"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Element 12 requires a plant-wide emergency action plan meeting 1910.38(a) plus specific procedures for handling small releases, and coordination with local emergency responders. Relying entirely on outside responders does not satisfy the element. Community drills and posting community plans are not what the element requires.\n\n要素 12 要求制定符合 1910.38(a) 的全厂应急行动计划，并针对小型泄漏制定具体处置程序，同时与当地应急响应机构协调。完全依赖外部救援不满足该要素。社区演练与张贴社区预案并非本要素的要求。","related":[{"n":"2.2","t":"PSM十四要素"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"Under PSM, compliance audits must be conducted at least every:","options":["5 years","10 years","2 years","3 years"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Compliance audits must be performed at least every 3 years (1910.119(o)). The audit team must include at least one person knowledgeable in the process. A report of findings must be developed, and the two most recent reports retained.\n\n合规审核必须至少每3年进行一次（1910.119(o)）。审核团队必须包括至少一名了解工艺的人员。必须编制发现报告，并保留最近两份报告。","related":[{"n":"2.2","t":"PSM的14个要素"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-02.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"Why do capital safety projects use net present value rather than simply adding up future savings?","options":["Because NPV eliminates all uncertainty about future injury costs","Because OSHA requires NPV for all safety investments","Because NPV ignores the initial investment cost entirely","Because future savings are worth less, so cash flows are discounted"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Money available today can be invested or earn a return, so a dollar received in year five is worth less than a dollar today; discounting converts future cash flows to a common present basis. NPV compares the discounted benefits with the initial cost and shows whether the project adds value. It does not remove uncertainty, and no OSHA rule requires it.\n\n今天的钱可以投资并取得回报，所以五年后的一美元价值低于今天的一美元；折现就是把未来现金流换算到同一现值基准。净现值把折现后的效益与初始成本比较，判断项目是否创造价值。它不能消除不确定性，也没有任何 OSHA 法规要求使用它。","related":[{"n":"8.2","t":"ROI 与回收期"}],"level":"recall","src":"practice-d2.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"A task is initially rated likelihood 5 and severity 4. After a machine-feeding interlock is installed, the team re-rates likelihood as 2 while severity stays at 4. By what percentage was the risk score reduced?","options":["75%","40%","50%","60%"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Initial score = 5 x 4 = 20; residual score = 2 x 4 = 8. Reduction = (20 - 8) / 20 = 12 / 20 = 60%. Severity is unchanged because the interlock reduces the probability of entanglement but does not reduce the harm if entanglement still occurs.\n\n初始分值 = 5 × 4 = 20；残余分值 = 2 × 4 = 8。降幅 = (20 − 8) ÷ 20 = 60%。严重性未变，因为联锁降低的是卷入发生的可能性，一旦仍然发生，伤害程度不变。","related":[{"n":"9.8","t":"风险登记册"},{"n":"9.3","t":"风险=可能性×严重性"}],"level":"calculation","src":"practice-d3.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"When using the 5 Whys technique for root cause analysis, what is the primary goal?","options":["To drill down through symptoms to reach underlying system-level causes","To classify the incident into one of five predetermined categories","To identify exactly five distinct causes for every incident","To determine which employee was at fault for the incident"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The 5 Whys technique is not about finding exactly five causes or assigning blame. It is about repeatedly asking \"why\" to move past immediate/superficial causes and reach deeper, system-level root causes. \"Five\" is a guideline — it may take fewer or more iterations.\n\n5Why法技术不是要找出恰好五个原因或追究责任。它是通过反复问\"为什么\"来超越即时/表面原因，达到更深层次的系统级根本原因。\"五\"是一个指导性数字——可能需要更少或更多的迭代。","related":[{"n":"7.5","t":"根源分析方法"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-07.html"},{"domain":"3","text":"Why does a high Detection rating INCREASE the RPN?","options":["Because a high Detection number means the failure is hard to detect, leaving more risk undetected","Because detection is the most important factor","It does not; high Detection lowers the RPN","Because better detection increases severity"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The Detection scale is inverted: a rating of 10 means poor detection. A high D means current controls are unlikely to catch the failure, so it propagates to the customer — raising risk and the RPN.\n\n检测度量表是反向的：10分表示检测差。高D意味着当前控制不太可能捕获失效，因此它传播到客户——提高风险和RPN。","related":[{"n":"10.2","t":"RPN"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-10.html"},{"domain":"6","text":"A fan moves 8,000 cfm through a 4-ft × 5-ft opening. What is the average face velocity?","options":["500 fpm","640 fpm","300 fpm","400 fpm"],"correct":3,"explanation":"V = Q / A = 8,000 cfm / (4 ft × 5 ft) = 8,000 / 20 = 400 fpm. This is the average velocity across the opening (face velocity).\n\nV = Q / A = 8,000 cfm / (4英尺 × 5英尺) = 8,000 / 20 = 400 fpm。这是开口处的平均速度（面风速）。","related":[{"n":"18.6","t":"通风一般原则"}],"level":"recall","src":"week-18.html"},{"domain":"1","text":"A plant wants to troubleshoot a live 480-V motor control center because shutting down would stop a continuous process for eight hours. Production argues the downtime is too costly. Is energized work justified under NFPA 70E?","options":["Yes, if the electrician has more than five years of experience","No; the cost of downtime alone is not a justification for energized work","Yes; any production loss justifies energized work","Yes, provided the electrician wears Category 2 PPE"],"correct":1,"explanation":"NFPA 70E permits energized work only when de-energizing introduces additional or increased hazards, or when the task is infeasible in a de-energized state, such as diagnostic voltage testing. Production cost is not one of the recognized justifications. When energized work is justified, an energized electrical work permit, a risk assessment, and appropriate arc-rated PPE are required.\n\nNFPA 70E 仅在断电会引入额外或更大危害，或任务在断电状态下不可行（如诊断性电压测试）时才允许带电作业。生产损失成本不属于认可的正当理由。确需带电作业时，必须签发带电作业许可证、完成风险评估并穿戴相应等级防弧 PPE。","related":[{"n":"3.2","t":"电气安全工作条件"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d1.html"},{"domain":"2","text":"A control chart of monthly recordable counts shows one point above the upper control limit, after which the process returns to its previous pattern. What is the MOST appropriate action?","options":["Recalculate the control limits to include the high point","Treat the point as common-cause variation and take no action","Suspend the safety programme until the chart is stable again","Investigate that month for a special cause"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A point outside the control limits is the classic signal of special-cause variation, and the correct response is to investigate what was different about that period. Removing the point to recalculate limits would hide the signal, and treating it as common cause ignores the chart's own rule. Control limits are usually set at plus or minus three standard deviations, so a point beyond them is unlikely to occur by chance.\n\n控制图上的点超出控制限是特殊原因变异的经典信号，正确响应是调查该时段有何不同。删除该点重算控制限会掩盖信号，把它当作普通原因则无视了控制图自身的判异规则。控制限通常设在 ±3σ，点落在其外纯属偶然的概率很低。","related":[{"n":"6.8","t":"帕累托分析"}],"level":"application","src":"practice-d2.html"}] }
};
